[886]={"Barallas can be found to the east of Drû Vádokan.\
\
You have dealt a crippling blow to the smiths of Isengard within the Balewood. Their tools are shattered, their numbers thinned, and their fires extinguished.","Defeated Orc-smiths in Drû Vádokan (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Smother Orc-fires (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat Orc-smiths in Drû Vádokan (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Orc-smiths and their tools can be found inside Drû Vádokan in north-west Balewood.\
\
Barallas has asked that you defeat the Orc-smiths in the Balewood and shatter their tools in hopes that their flames and axes will no longer be used against the inhabitants of the forest.","Smothered Orc-fires (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Destroyed White Hand forges (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Alas for Brúndoron....\
\
'Hoom. The Orcs seek to master this forest then... I have seen the smoke rising on the hill since your return and fear for what time may bring us.\
\
'The smiths you saw, without question, are the cause of such evil doings. Their fascination with the flame, and their handiwork that leads only to the death of my kin cannot continue. I would ask that you return to their camp... slay the smiths, shatter their tools, and smother the fires.'","Talk to Barallas outside Drû Vádokan","Destroy White Hand forges (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Orc-smiths of the Balewood fuel the war effort through their weaponry and fires throughout the forest. Until they are defeated and their tools destroyed, peace cannot return to the Balewood.","A Thorn in Their Side","'Hom. It is done? Such things are unfit for this forest... it is good that the Orcs' makings will no longer hew and burn my kin.\
\
'So many have been lost... perhaps it is time at last for us to stand against them.\
\
'Hom. There is much discussion to be done yet....'"},
[887]={"Completed The Rings of Isengard","Andras suggested only one course of action to remove the threat of Saruman's rings: enter Orthanc, face Saruman, take the rings, and destroy them.","Completed the Into the Pit of Abomination","Andras has asked you to enter the Ring of Isengard, the eaves of Fangorn, and the Pits of Isengard and disrupt Saruman's war-efforts.","Completed Dargnákh's Rage","Talk to Andras at the Ox-clan encampment","Completed Ringing of the Hammer","Complete Into the Pit of Abomination in the Pits of Isengard 3-man instance","Complete Dargnákh's Rage in the Dargnákh Unleashed 3-man instance","Andras is at the Ox-clan encampment in Nan Curunír.\
\
You should return at once to Andras with news of your success and your discovery within Saruman's Foundry.","Complete Ringing of the Hammer in the Foundry 6-man instance","Complete The Rings of Isengard in the Tower of Isengard 12-man Raid","Andras escaped from the dungeons of Isengard. From his vantage point in the Ox-clan encampment, he saw Isengard empty and march south. The opportunity to exact his revenge on Saruman of Many Colours was beyond his ability to resist, and he sent forth a call through the Boar-clan resistance to all who would heed to come to Nan Curunír and make a stand against the White Hand.","Complete Protecting the Forest in the Fangorn's Edge 3-man instance","'It was glorious, ${PLAYER}! I found a perch where I was able to witness your attacks both on the lumber-camp and the troll's rampage within the Ring of Isengard. The Wizard's forces will be in confusion for weeks!\
\
'As you live, I assume you were successful within the Pits as well? Good. Some of those abominations may once have been my kinsmen, but they have been twisted into creatures wholly evil.\
\
'Now, I have task for you that is perhaps a bit more daunting, and for which I recommend you go as a party of no less than six. When I was enslaved in Isengard, I was tasked with bringing ore to a Foundry where only Saruman and his most trusted servants were ever seen. I believe that there he is forging weapons of great magical power, obscene things that should not be permitted to see the light of day.\
\
'I ask that you go there and destroy his evil forge, so that no more evil may come of that place. His chief acolyte, Penrith, is a kinsman who has abandoned the ways of the lûth and has embraced Saruman's evil magic called 'industry'... he must be destroyed.\
\
'Will you do this?'","Andras has asked you to enter Saruman's Foundry, defeat the wizard's acolyte, Penrith, and destroy the forge to prevent more weapons of evil power from coming into existence.","Andras is at the Ox-clan encampment in Nan Curunír.\
\
You should return to Andras and tell him that Saruman's rings of power have been destroyed.","'I have no love for the Forgoil whom you give aid, but for now our purposes are closely entwined. Isengard has emptied -- may the Orcs and Horse-lords destroy each other -- leaving its defences weakened. There is still a Wizard within, but there may be something we can do to disrupt Saruman's plans.\
\
'I have noted three places that might be easily and secretly accessed where we can sow the most strife: the Ring of Isengard, the eaves of Fangorn, and the Pits of Isengard.\
\
'The Orcs and trolls in service to Isengard have begun clear-cutting the eaves of Fangorn. It is an ancient forest, and one my people fear, but I received a dream from the Uch-gwirod telling me to save the wood, for there is life there that is older than most that walk the earth. I will not forsake the Ox-spirit's command and bid you disrupt Saruman's lumber-camp.\
\
'As well, I have learned that Saruman's forces captured a strange, white troll in Fangorn and are holding it within the Ring of Isengard. If you could free the troll and goad it into a rampage, it might wreak great destruction among the Wizard's remaining forces.\
\
'Thirdly, Saruman has laboratories beneath Isengard, where he experiments on his hapless prisoners and twists them into terrible monsters. I want you to enter the Pits of Isengard and destroy the wretched abominations there, particularly the great troll Ironarm.\
\
'You and a couple of friends should be able to stir up trouble in these places... they are not nearly as guarded as Orthanc. Will you aid me?'","'What? Y-you live? Bless the Uch-gwirod! You look like you barely made it out of that evil place alive, though. Were you routed?\
\
'The rings are destroyed, five subservient and his master ring? All of them? Thrice blessed be the Uch-gwirod! Though I see from your look that Saruman lives and is hardly powerless, the threat I feared no longer exists: his Ring-forge is destroyed and the last of the rings with it!\
\
'While you were gone, Gwin of the Avanc-lûth came and left gifts for any heroes who dare to stand against the Wizard... they are yours and with great thanks. We will begin our journey home as soon as my strength returns, with hope of peace in our hearts.'","'Penrith is dead? Then my revenge is nearly com... what was that, you say? The Foundry was not producing magical weapons, but the wizard was in fact forging rings of power?\
\
'Even among my people there are ancient tales of the Shadow Walkers... kings of old who took the Great Rings of Power from Sauron and became undead sorcerers of terrible power. I do not wish to see this thing come to pass in my lands, watching as my people are turned into evil shadows in the service of Saruman of Many Colours.\
\
'I fear, ${PLAYER}, that there is only one course: to face the Wizard and take his rings. They must be destroyed, each and every one, before great evil befalls Dunland, Rohan, and the world beyond!\
\
'I warn you, this will be no easy task, so you must go in great number... six warriors, no matter how hardy, cannot hope to enter the Tower of Orthanc and stand against a Wizard! Will you do this?'","Talk to Andras at the Ox-clan encampment in Nan Curunír","A Thorn in the Hand","Andras is at the Ox-clan encampment in Nan Curunír.\
\
You should return to Andras with news of your successes.","Completed Protecting the Forest"},
[890]={"Examine the boot-print","'In my time, I have seen many arrive and depart the Field of Celebrant, but there is one who has not yet left.\
\
'He crept into the Field among the fog of the Rushgore and hid within the ruins of Ost Celebrant. I know not who this man is, nor what his purpose in Ost Celebrant can be. However, I fear that no good can come of his presence here.\
\
'Search the outside of Ost Celebrant near the Rushgore, perhaps this wanderer left some clue to his origin.'","Cabed is atop a small hill along the southern road in Parth Celebrant.\
\
You should bring the twisted blade to Cabed.","You do not see anymore boot-prints, but a glint in the distance across the water catches your eye","You see a fading boot-print in the mud nearby","You should examine the glint you saw in the distance.","Cabed has sent you to investigate the outskirts of Ost Celebrant near the Rushgore where he believes that an unknown force passed through before entering the ruin.","Follow the trail of boot-prints","Talk to Cabed","'What is this?\
\
'I know this blade...and others like it. This is the blade of an Easterling. I had my suspicions of who the stranger could be, but I wished to believe it untrue.\
\
'These men do not belong on the field and such audacity cannot go unanswered, you must show this to your allies and Doron when the time comes.'","Examine the glint in the distance","You see another boot-print nearby","You see a trail of boot-prints leading into the distance","Find the wanderer's trail outside Ost Celebrant","You have found a dulled and twisted blade of strange make","'¿Has encontrado algo?'","A Threat Unseen","Cabed has sent you to track down a mysterious invader's trail. The trail ends at the bridge to Ost Celebrant, but Cabed is unsure where it begins.","'You should follow the tracks of the Easterling....'"},
[891]={"'Al menos las arañas no tendrán la satisfacción de arruinar el arco de mi padre.'","Arco de Sprigley recogido","Cal Sprigley se puede encontrar al norte de las ruinas de la Posada del Tejón Loco en Archet.\
\
Después de que las arañas atacaran su granja, Cal Sprigley y su esposa huyeron a la seguridad de Archet. Atli Matarañas te ha pedido que hables con el granjero.","Recoge la caja fuerte de Sprigley","'Mi granja está al sur del Capricho de Bronwe, por el segundo sendero hacia el este desde la carretera del sur. El lugar ha cambiado mucho ahora: es un miserable nido de arañas.'","Cal Sprigley y su esposa te esperan al norte de las ruinas de la Posada del Tejón Loco en Archet.\
\
Cal y Holly Sprigley están esperando en Archet las pertenencias que recuperaste de su granja infestada de arañas. Deberías regresar a verlos de inmediato.","'¡Espero que puedas ahuyentar a esas horribles arañas de nuestra tierra para siempre! Somos gente decente y respetuosa de la ley y no deberíamos tener que soportar tales problemas.'","Saco de semillas de Sprigley recogido","Recoge el saco de semillas de Sprigley","'¡Las arañas salieron de la bodega en la noche y apenas tuvimos tiempo suficiente para escapar! Muchos de los jornaleros no tuvieron tanta suerte. Vimos al pobre Henry tratando de ahuyentar a las arañas en el patio lateral con el arco de Cal.\
\
Si puedes recuperar ese arco, nuestro saco de semillas de los corrales de ganado y mi caja fuerte cerca del cobertizo de almacenamiento, estaremos muy agradecidos.'","'No te preocupes por mí, ${PLAYER}. Es solo una herida menor que obtuve en la pelea.\
\
Ahora que los Helecharroyo, padre e hijo, han ahuyentado a los Montebruno de Archet, quizás esta gente pueda volver a vivir sus vidas como lo hacían antes. Sin embargo, he recibido noticias de que hay una nueva amenaza que enfrentar.\
\
Una granja cercana ha sido invadida por arañas, y la gente allí se ha refugiado en Archet. Mi herida me impide lidiar con las plagas, pero tú has demostrado ser un guerrero capaz y no deberías tener problemas. Busca al granjero aquí en Archet. Puede que ya lo conozcas... su nombre es Cal Sprigley.'","'Deberías llevarle a Sprigley sus pertenencias de inmediato. Tales posesiones son casi tan importantes para un granjero como lo es mi hacha para mí.'","La granja de Cal Sprigley ha sido invadida por arañas. El granjero y su esposa huyeron a Archet, dejando atrás sus pertenencias.","'Un día, recuperaremos esa granja de las arañas.'","Una amenaza de arañas","Recoge el arco de Sprigley","'¡Esto es todo lo que pedimos: mi saco de semillas, la caja fuerte y el confiable arco de mi padre! No puedo agradecerte lo suficiente, ${PLAYER}, y debo pedirte disculpas por haberte tratado tan mal antes.\
\
Si hubiera sabido lo que iba a pasar con mi granja, habría seguido tu consejo y me habría retirado a Archet de inmediato, ahorrándonos muchos problemas... y la vida del pobre Henry.\
\
Aun así, me alegra que podamos empezar de nuevo. Dile a Matarañas que también le agradezco por enviarte a ayudarnos.'","'Sprigley y su esposa huyeron a Archet con lo poco que pudieron llevar de su granja. Las arañas debieron sorprenderlos de repente.'","'No puedo agradecerte lo suficiente por traerme mis cosas.'","La granja de Cal Sprigley está al sur del Capricho de Bronwe.\
\
Cal Sprigley te ha pedido que vayas a su granja y recuperes su caja fuerte, saco de semillas y arco. Con estas cosas, podría ser capaz de comenzar de nuevo.","Habla con Cal Sprigley en Archet","'Ahí estábamos, listos para defendernos de esos villanos Montebruno, cuando unas arañas monstruosas salieron de la bodega en plena noche. ¡No parece justo!\
\
Aun así, si Matarañas te envió, quizá puedas ayudarnos. Nuestra granja está justo al sur del Capricho de Bronwe. Si puedes recuperar mi saco de semillas de los corrales y mi caja fuerte del cobertizo, podríamos empezar de nuevo. ¡Ah, y también el arco de mi padre! El pobre Henry intentó matar algunas arañas con él. Era buen trabajador, pero las arañas acabaron rápido con el muchacho.\
\
Vuelve pronto, si puedes... aunque con todas las arañas alrededor de mi granja, no sé cómo lo harás.'","'Aún no has recuperado todo lo que te pedí. ¿Cómo vamos a empezar de nuevo sin el saco de semillas, la caja fuerte o el arco de mi padre? No siempre habrá gente como tú que traiga carne de jabalí, ¿sabes?'","'Estoy seguro de que serás de gran ayuda para Sprigley. Las arañas no son amigas de los Hombres y deben ser tratadas con severidad si se las va a enfrentar.'","Lleva el saco de semillas, el arco y la caja fuerte a Cal Sprigley","Caja fuerte de Sprigley recogida"},
[892]={"'Corsairs! Corsairs have come up the river! What does it mean? How came they to Lamedon? O, whatever will we do?'\
\
The inhabitants of Dínadab are suddenly bustling with activity, frightened by the sudden sighting of Corsairs. You should speak with townspeople and see if there is any fact behind this wild claim.","Question frightened townsfolk about the Corsair sighting (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Frightened townsfolk can be found in Dínadab in northern Lamedon.\
\
You should question townsfolk about the sighting of corsairs.","You see tents sprawling as far as the eye can see in the shady swamp to the east...","Find the watchman and tell him about the Corsairs","'I heard rumours, ${PLAYER}. What if there is truth to them? You are a famous adventurer... have you ever encountered Corsairs in your travels? Are you going to protect us?'","The watchman cannot help, for all the soldiers of Dínadab have followed Prince Imrahil to war","'I just came here this morning from the town south of here, and I swear to you, I saw them. Corsairs! Hordes of them. Everyone was running, and I hastened here. What are we to do? What if they come here?'","The townspeople of Dínadab have reported sightings of Corsairs over the ridge to the east.","This townsperson reports having seen the beginning of a Corsair invasion of the town south of Dínadab","'I put my head down to take a nap, and I had a terrible dream, that Fuirion... Fuirion was lost to us forever. He told me things that made my heart heavy with sadness. I woke up to check on him, and he was gone.\
\
'I... I cannot say anything more. It is very like the dream! Fuirion is gone, and the watchman tells us that he came seeking bounties. He went to the Corsair camp!'","'Help, help! Should we evacuate? Where can we go that is safe? The Corsairs will take everything!'","Speak with Gladion","'${PLAYER}, I am not much of a fighter, but I must go to this encampment and search for my brother. Will you meet me there? I need the help of someone strong.\
\
'I will not sit idly by and let my brother kill himself. I do not know what madness has possessed him, but I will stop him.'","Este es un buen punto de vista","Limril had a terrible dream about Fuirion, and woke to find him gone","'Why, why is he doing this? Fuirion has run off. He is wounded -- he could die!'","This townsperson mentions that the invaders' tents could be seen from the east ridge","A Threat from the Shore","'I was looking over the ridge to the east, and I saw tents... strange tents! Is it brigands? Someone said it was Corsairs... but that is impossible.'","Gladion stands outside the Watchman's home in Dínadab in northern Lamedon.\
\
You should speak with Gladion about Fuirion.","The ridge that may offer a view of the Corsair camp can be found to the east of Dínadab.\
\
You should <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> over the ridge towards the east.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest requires emotes.</rgb>","<rgb=#FF0000>Look</rgb> eastward for signs of Corsairs from atop the ridge","'Yes, I've had many reports of Corsairs. The soldiers have all followed Prince Imrahil, and only farmers are left. I am sorry, but I have no one to send to rescue Fuirion.\
\
'What could he be thinking, in the state he's in?'","Gladion is determined to rescue Fuirion","'Why would he leave in his state?'","The Watchman of Dínadab can be found standing outside of his home in northern Lamedon.\
\
You should speak with the watchman.","'Corsairs! Did you hear? Corsairs have come from Umbar! Does this mean Dol Amroth is fallen? What are we to do? I must hide and lock away all of my things, and I must run! But where shall we go?'","Ask the watchman for help in rescuing Fuirion"},
[893]={"'Nethgarch se puede encontrar en Pembar, al noreste de Echad Eregion y al sureste de Glâd Ereg.'","Pembar se encuentra al noreste de Echad Eregion y al sureste de Glâd Ereg.\
\
Faenhilith te ha pedido que viajes a Pembar y elimines al padre de sierpes Nethgarch.","Aunque los sierpes de Pembar probablemente estén dirigidos por una matrona, no puede haber descendencia sin un padre.","Faenhilith está en Echad Eregion, al suroeste de Pembar.\
\
Debes regresar a Faenhilith e informarle de tu victoria sobre Nethgarch.","Nethgarch, padre de sierpes, derrotado","'Con Nethgarch derrotado, los sierpes disminuirán en Pembar. Te agradezco, ${PLAYER}.'","'¿La bestia ha sido derrotada? Los sierpes nunca han avanzado tanto hacia el sur; es una mala noticia para quien aún habita al este del Mar.\
\
'Pero has logrado mucho, ${PLAYER}, y debes tener tu recompensa por tu valor.'","'Las ruinas de Pembar son un lugar triste, una vez llenas de la música de las arpas y el suave golpeteo de los martillos de los joyeros. Ahora está lleno del hedor de la carne podrida y las bestias malvadas.\
\
'Uno de estos monstruos ha estado esparciendo la suciedad de su especie por las ruinas de Pembar, un gran sierpe: Nethgarch. Ve a Pembar y busca a este padre de sierpes. Sin él, esta línea de gusanos fracasará.\
\
'Pembar se encuentra al noreste de Echad Eregion y al sureste de Glâd Ereg. Estará acechando en algún lugar dentro de las ruinas.'","Una amenaza para Pembar","Habla con Faenhilith en Echad Eregion"},
[895]={"Lúlstrok can be found in the north-western reaches of the Gladden Fields.\
\
A bunting has delivered a message on Radagast's behalf asking you to investigate and drive out the Orkish presence in the Gladden Fields.","Unmistakably held by the remnants of the Shapag-hai in the Vales, Lúlstrok is heavily-fortified","A Thunder of Drums","The leader of the Shapag-hai can be found somewhere in Lúlstrok.\
\
You should seek out and defeat the leader of the Shapag-hai in Lúlstrok.","A tribe of Orcs known as the Shapag-hai has invaded the Gladden Fields, polluting its marshlands and threatening the inhabitants of the Vales of Anduin.","As the sound of drums echoes through Lúlstrok, a harsh voice rises within the tent","Siege-towers can be found in Lúlstrok.\
\
Aware that the Shapag-hai have siege-towers for some as of yet known purpose, you have been advised to sabotage the Orcs' siege-towers and keep them from inflicting more harm on the Gladden Fields.","Investigate Lúlstrok","As you stand and curiously look at the bunting, it lowers its beak to point at a small scroll bound to its leg. You take the scroll and begin to read it.\
\
The scroll contains hasty writing which you swiftly identify as the writing of Radagast the Brown. As you read on, Radagast explains that a company of Orcs who survived the end of the War has now made camp at a place they call Lúlstrok in the Gladden Fields. Radagast's writing continues and he describes how until a few days ago the Orcs had apparently often feuded with the Men and half-orcs in the centre of the Gladden Fields, but they did not seem to pose a serious threat to the Wilderfolk. However, Radagast now fears they have been stirred by the words of a large Orc among their number and as a consequence, they have grown more bold in recent days. Troubled by the harm their siege engines might inflict on the Gladden Fields and concerned that the Orcs might soon attack the Beornings and Woodmen, Radagast concludes by asking you to drive off the Orcs and damage their siege engines beyond repair.\
 \
As the bunting remains perched nearby, you decide to investigate Lúlstrok.","Sabotaged siege-tower wheels in Lúlstrok (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Durbkhat falls defeated, but his last words echo in your mind","Sabotage siege-tower wheels in Lúlstrok (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The bunting can be found near Lúlstrok in the Gladden Fields.\
\
You have done much to repel the Shapag-hai in the Gladden Fields, and you should now return to the bunting and send it to inform Radagast that you have drive out the Orkish presence in the Gladden Fields.","Find and defeat the leader of the Shapag-hai in Lúlstrok","Deliver tidings of the Shapag-hai's defeat to the bunting","The bunting appears to have awaited your return. It points its beak at its leg, and you realize it intends to return to Radagast with the scroll.\
\
You turn over the scroll and begin to write on the side Radagast left blank. You tell Radagast of victory over the Shapag-hai in the Vales of Anduin. However, you mention that the Orcs once loyal to Mazog now seek vengeance against the dwarves who escaped the downfall of the Iron Garrison. Whether they resurface in days soon to come or many years from now, the battle for Moria is not yet ended and a vigil must be kept.\
\
You roll the scroll and bind it to the bunting's leg. It chirps in what you take to be a friendly farewell and flies off."},
[896]={"Collect farm tools (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Repair broken fences (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","A Time for Rebuilding","Some of the wooden fences around Thrymm's Farm are broken or in need of repair, and there are tools scattered about the farm. All of the tools and broken fences can be found in the fields.","The tools you picked up should be returned to Oter to be put away properly. He can be found by the large barn near the centre of Thrymm's Farm.","Fence repaired (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The Warg-riders may leave us alone long enough to repair what we can, and maybe put up a few defences here. Forlaw needs more supplies of food to survive this unnatural winter. However, they cannot spare men to protect the farm, or they risk the city itself. It is up to us to defend this farm and begin working the fields again.\
\
'Can you help us repair a few of the fences, and maybe clean up some of the tools scattered around the farm?'","Bring the tools back to Oter","'Thrymm's Farm is coming along nicely, thanks to you. Soon we can start to work these fields and hopefully get them ready for planting crops. Forlaw needs these supplies as quickly as we can make them!'","Thrymm's Farm, once a cornerstone of the Forlaw marketplace, has fallen on hard times of late. However, the farmers are working hard to repair the farm and prepare it for growing crops again.","Tool collected (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[898]={"You and Amarion have escaped from the Black Dens","'Amarion's absence troubles me greatly, ${PLAYER}. He said he would return within a few hours, and he is not one to lose track of time in the field.\
\
'That he has not returned yet bodes ill. He said that he wished to examine the Black Dens for himself, hoping to find some way to stop the scourge of the Shadow-wolves, but that was the last I saw of him.\
\
'The Black Dens lies to the south-east of here. I ask that you search for him there...I fear for his life if they have caught him unaware.'","'What of Amarion, ${PLAYER}? Did you find him?'","Amarion is in the Black Dens, south-east of Echad Dagoras.\
\
Braigiar has asked you to find Amarion and rescue him from the Shadow-wolves.","'Who is that down there? ${PLAYER}? It is long since you aided me at Amon Raith. I do not suppose you could lend me a hand once more?'","Find Amarion the Ranger near the Black Dens","'Let us be off then, shall we?'","'Help Amarion if you can...he went to the Black Dens alone.'","Help Amarion escape from the Black Dens","Amarion is at the Black Dens, south-east of Echad Dagoras.\
\
Amarion has asked for your help to escape from the Black Dens.","Amarion left camp to search the Black Dens where he believed he might find some way to destroy the Shadow-wolves -- but he has been gone too long.","'My thanks for your aid, ${PLAYER}! \
\
'For a little while, I was not sure I was going to make it back alive....'","'I am afraid that the Shadow-wolves caught my scent and chased me up here some hours ago...I have been biding my time in the hopes that perhaps they would leave, but I have had no such fortune.\
\
'Now that you have found me here though, I think it would be best if we left swiftly before they find you as well.'","Amarion is at Echad Dagoras, north-west of the Black Dens.\
\
You should speak with Amarion about your escape from the Shadow-wolves.","A Timely Rescue","'Amarion went to the Black Dens alone...I hope he is well.'","Talk to Amarion at Echad Dagoras"},
[899]={"'Los nerbyg están por todas las dunas. Es imposible no verlos. Simplemente ve al norte.'","Caparazones de norbog conseguidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los caparazones de los norbog de arena pueden parecer marrones por fuera, por por dentro son de un verde brillante.","'El vidrio es algo difícil de colorear. Solo para una tonalidad, hay muchos materiales que hay que conseguir. El verde no es tan díficil de hacer, pero lo que usamos quizá te sorprenda.\
\
'Sé que los nerbyg de arena parecen marrones y se camuflan con las dunas. Sin embargo, si rompes sus caparazones y miras por la parte de abajo, verás un color verde como la hierba.\
\
'Puedes encontar a los nerbyg de arena por todas las dunas del sur del Barandalf, justo al norte de aquí. Tráeme un puñado de sus caparazones y los machacaré para hacer algo de vidrio verde.'","Los caparazones de norbog pueden obtenerse de los nerbyg de arena en las dunas al sur del Barandalf, al norte de Dwaling.\
\
Perla Buenavista te ha pedido que consigas caparazones de los nerbyg que viven en las dunas.","Perla Buenavista está en la casa de Hob Cimacolina, justo en el exterior de Dwaling.\
\
Perla Buenavista querrá empezar a extraer el verde los caparazones de norbog tan pronto como sea posible.","Una pizca de verde","Lleva los caparazones de norbog a Perla Buenavista en Dwaling","Consigue caparazones de norbog (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Estos servirán. No son los mejores que he visto nunca, pero creo que puedo conseguir suficiente verde de ellos para hacer lo que necesito, al menos de momento."},
[900]={"Ragnarr Cuernollama fue a vivir entre los Hijos de la Tierra, pero una traición reciente los ha vuelto desconfiados.","'Los Jorthkyn siempre han sido un misterio; ayudan a mi gente sin pedir nada a cambio. Vine aquí para vivir entre ellos y que nuestros pueblos se conocieran mejor.\
\
Este grupo es todo lo que queda de una partida de caza de más allá de Ram Dúath. Tras cruzar el paso, su Primer Cazador se volvió contra ellos, sumiendo al grupo en el caos.\
\
Sigo siendo un extraño y no confían plenamente en mí, especialmente tras esta reciente traición. Necesitaré ganarme su confianza de nuevo. Sé que su tótem tribal es el urochs. Cuando el grupo del Primer Cazador se rebeló, se llevaron uno de los cráneos del tótem. He visto un santuario de tótem entre las colinas al noreste de aquí. Recoge ese cráneo para mí, así podré ganarme la confianza de la tribu.'","Un símbolo de valor","Lleva el cráneo de urochs a Ragnarr.","Recoge el cráneo de urochs","Cráneo de urochs recogido","El cráneo de urochs se puede encontrar en el territorio de los huargos al noreste del campamento de los Hijos de la Tierra.\
\
Para recuperar la confianza de los Hijos de la Tierra, Ragnarr Cuernollama te ha pedido que recojas un cráneo de urochs del tótem en las colinas del este de Nan Amlug y se lo lleves al campamento de los Hijos de la Tierra. Un grupo de huargos merodea actualmente por este territorio.","'Esto está bien, lo has hecho bien pero... bueno, puede que haya cometido un error...'","'Los Jorthkyn aún dudan de mis intenciones; debes traerme ese cráneo de urochs.'"},
[901]={"The ledger is with Andras' belongings in his caravan on the northern road in Starkmoor.\
\
The pages should be placed back within the ledger.","The pages fit back within the ledger, and it closes smoothly. Care will need to be taken to make sure they do not fly out, but at least they have all been returned.","A Torn Ledger","Collected ledger-pages (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Return the pages to the ledger","Collect ledger-pages (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The ledger's pages detailed the items at Andras' estate that are ready for auction: a very important list for a man in desperate need of money.","It would take much more time than Andras has to reassemble this ledger from scratch. The pages must be found and returned.","Most of the pages of this ledger have been ripped out and taken. The few remaining pages appear to detail crop amounts and various household items. This is most likely an accounting of all goods Andras has at his homestead.\
\
The missing pages are vital if he is to put together a respectable auction. The Dragon-clan raiders must have taken the pages with them.","The missing pages of the ledger have been taken by the Dragon-clan raiders in the hills to the east of the broken caravan.\
\
You should recover the missing pages of Andras' ledger."},
[903]={"'As you know, Edash has devised a clever cure for the Orkish poisons used by Azog's kin. However, his supply has again run short.\
\
'You are familiar with twistbeard, yes? Gather as much as you can find in the dale, bring it to me, and I will see that Edash receives it at once!\
\
'Be swift, my friend. Several of our warriors are in dire need of the antidote!'","A Touch of Twistbeard","'Ah, let us hope this will suffice!\
\
'You have my thanks.'","Although Edash discovered a cure for the Orkish poisons used by Azog and his clan, it has proven difficult to maintain a supply of twistbeard.","Deliver the twistbeard to Thorin at Amdân","Collected twistbeard (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect twistbeard (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Twistbeard can found on rocks in Azanulbizar.\
\
Thorin has asked you to gather twistbeard for the Dwarves of the Haban'akkâ.","Thorin can be found at Amdân.\
\
You have collected a great deal of twistbeard and should now deliver it to Thorin."},
[904]={"Tad Cortahoja está fuera del pabellón de caza, al que puedes llegar siguiendo el camino fuera de la Sala de Subastas de Bree hacia el oeste hasta su final.\
\
Se te ha indicado que hables con Tad Cortahoja.","La Sala de Subastas de Bree está al este, pasando la Puerta de los Leñadores, luego al sur.\
\
Dawn Manzanadorada te instruyó que hablaras con uno de los subastadores en la Sala de Subastas.","'Habla con los líderes de los Hombres de Bree. Los encontrarás al oeste por el camino.'","'${PLAYERNAME:Bienvenido[m]|Bienvenida[f]} a las Bóvedas de Bree. No cobramos nada por almacenar muchos de tus bienes y, por una pequeña pero creciente tarifa, almacenaremos aún mas.\
\
'Tenemos protección de la guardia de la ciudad a toda hora del día, así que puedes estar seguro de que tus objetos de valor están a salvo aquí.\
\
'Siéntete libre de mirar alrededor en la entrada antes de cruzar hacia la Taxidermia de Espinablanca.'","La Fuente del Jabalí está un poco al norte de la Sala de Artesanía de Tres Partos.\
\
Bonny Techador te dijo que hablaras con el Segundo vigilante Heathstraw en la Fuente del Jabalí en la Plaza del Mercado.","Un Recorrido por Bree","'Encontrarás las bóvedas al sur de aquí, justo mas allá de los guardias en los viejos edificios de piedra.'","Dirígete hacia el sur al salir de la Taxidermia de Espinablanca; antes de llegar a la estatua del enano, gira a la izquierda, hacia el este, y avanza hasta la Escalera del Erudito. Entra y habla con Newbold Cortahoja.\
\
Clar Espinablanca te indicó que hablaras con Newbold Cortahoja dentro de la Escalera del Erudito.","'Hola, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}. Debes ser nuevo en Bree y enviado por el Alcalde Tenderlarch. Es un gusto conocerte. Soy Lirio Hojarena..... me encargo de todos los bienes cultivados por los hobbits que viven en la colina.\
\
'También disfruto de coleccionar reliquias históricas, lo cual me recuerda que mi ayudante aún no me ha enviado nada... espero que todo esté bien.\
\
'Ah, debo enviarte a visitar la Puerta Oeste para hablar con Harry Goatleaf. Sigue hacia el oeste en dirección a la puerta y deberías ver allí a Harry. Quizás quieras hablar también con Bill Rosewood... él cuida los caballos de Bree Oeste.'","Graeme Tenderlarch está en el Ayuntamiento de Bree, casi directamente al noroeste desde la Puerta Sur.\
\
Tad Cortahoja te dijo que regresaras con Graeme Tenderlarch.","'Vaya, vaya. Es bueno verte de nuevo. Asumo que estás en tu recorrido por Bree y buscas algo de información sobre la ciudad. No soy tan historiador como cierta otra gente, pero sé un poco sobre la ciudad y la razón por la cual el jabalí tiene un papel tan importante en la decoración del pueblo.\
\
'Cuando Bree fue asentada, el área era un terreno de caza ideal para jabalíes salvajes. Las bestias servían como la principal fuente de carne para los primeros colonos y se han convertido en un símbolo de tenacidad. La Fuente del Jabalí fue construida para honrar a aquellos primeros pobladores que se asentaron en Bree y usaron a los jabalíes salvajes circundantes como provisión.\
\
'Bueno, ha sido un placer hablar contigo, pero querrás seguir tu camino para ver las mercancías en el Mercado de Lalia. Saluda a la propia Lalia dentro de la tienda; está justo al otro lado de la plaza, hacia el norte.'","Habla con un subastador","'¿Qué quieres? Tenderlarch es un necio si piensa que alguno de nosotros quiere perder el tiempo hablando con gente que estará en Bree causando problemas sin fin. Debería concentrarse en asuntos que realmente pueda manejar.\
\
'Fuera de mi vista. Habla con el Vigilante Cardoon si quieres mas ayuda. Está justo por el camino hacia el este.'","La Posada del Poney Pisador está al norte de la Plaza del Mercado.\
\
Lalia te ha indicado que hables con Cebadilla Mantecona, propietario de la Posada del Poney Pisador.","Habla con el Vigilante Cardoon en Bree","'Es hora de que visites a los otros ladrones de Bree, los subastadores.\
\
'Los encontrarás mas allá de la Puerta de Madera.'","'El Mercado de Lalia está en el lado norte de la Plaza del Mercado, justo al lado de la Fuente del Jabalí. Lalia se encuentra dentro.'","'Bien entonces, Bree es una ciudad bastante grande, y hay muchos lugares que visitar y gente que conocer. Quiero ayudarte con esto y he pedido a muchos de los habitantes de la ciudad que te den la bienvenida cuando hables con ellos. Esta ciudad necesita tantos aliados como pueda encontrar en estos tiempos oscuros.\
\
'Tu primera parada será al norte, justo mas allá de la Puerta del Comerciante, en la Sala de Artesanía de Tres Partos. Entra en el edificio y habla con Bonny Techador.'","La Sala de Artesanía de Tres Partos se encuentra al norte del Ayuntamiento de Bree, pasando por la Puerta del Comerciante.\
\
Graeme Tenderlarch te ha pedido entrar en la Sala de Artesanía de Tres Partos y hablar con Bonny Techador.","'Mat Matosos vive en la parte menos agradable de la ciudad, hacia el este. Los refugiados del sur parecen instalarse allí mas a menudo que en cualquier otro lugar de Bree.'","Habla con Tad Gardener en la bóveda","'Encontrarás la taxidermia al otro lado del camino.'","Habla con Clar Espinablanca en la Taxidermia de Espinablanca","Harry Goatleaf se encuentra en la Puerta Oeste, al oeste de la casa de Lirio Hojarena.\
\
Lirio Hojarena te dijo que hablaras con Harry Goatleaf.","Habla con el alcalde Graeme Tenderlarch en el Ayuntamiento de Bree","'${PLAYERNAME:Bienvenido. Bienvenido[m]|Bienvenida. Bienvenida[f]} a mi pequeña tienda. Me dijeron que esperara nuevas caras entrando, pues he tenido el honor de ser incluida en el recorrido turístico de nuestra ciudad.\
\
'Los ciudadanos de Bree han sido excepcionalmente acogedores con mi pequeño emprendimiento aquí, y he estado mas ocupada que nunca cosiendo, remendando y organizando los artículos en exhibición.\
\
'Los atuendos cerca del frente del mercado rotan mensualmente, y todos los demás diseños van y vienen cuando llega el momento adecuado. Siéntete libre de visitarnos y ver nuestras mercancías en cualquier momento.\
\
'Ahora, cuando termines aquí, te hará bien conocer a Cebadilla Mantecona. Es otro comerciante exitoso, pues es dueño de la posada mas concurrida de todo Bree. Lo encontrarás al norte por el camino, mas allá de la Puerta del Mercado, dentro de la Posada del Poney Pisador.'","'Encontrarás la Escalera del Erudito al sureste bajo el arco y entrando al callejón al este antes de la estatua del enano. Habla con Newbold. Es un buen viejo.'","'Hola ${PLAYERNAME:amigo, bienvenido[m]|amiga, bienvenida[f]} a la Taxidermia de Espinablanca. Mi hijo y yo, junto con el señor Panblanco, podemos crear maravillosos trofeos a partir de hallazgos únicos que encuentres en tus aventuras. Puedes exhibir estas maravillas dentro de tus hogares si lo deseas.\
\
'Echa un vistazo si quieres, y cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]}, toma el camino fuera de mi casa hacia el sureste, mas allá de la Puerta del Herrero, hasta el Barrio de Piedra. Gira al este antes de la estatua del enano y sigue el callejón hasta los estudiosos. Son buenos camaradas y muy conocedores de Bree. Habla con Newbold Cortahoja en la Escalera del Erudito.'","Habla con Lirio Hojarena en su casa","Habla con Bonny Techador en la Sala de Artesanía de Tres Partos","'Te dije que no tengo nada que decirte. Si quieres saber algo mas sobre esta ciudad, habla con el vigilante mas hacia el este. Cardoon es su nombre.'","Habla con Tad Cortahoja en el pabellón de caza","'Regresa al Ayuntamiento y habla con Graeme Tenderlarch.'","'Saludos, ${PLAYER}. ¿Goatleaf te envió aquí? Ha estado actuando mas extraño y mas extraño últimamente.\
\
'No es motivo de preocupación, estoy seguro. Deberías visitar la bóveda ahora. La encontrarás por el camino hacia el sur. Es un gran edificio de piedra con dos guardias vigilando.\
\
'Entra en la bóveda y habla con Tad Gardener o con Maud Dedalera.'","Habla con Newbold Cortahoja","'Bien entonces, has estado en cada rincón de Bree y deberías poder orientarte mas fácilmente ahora.\
\
'Con todas las historias de fantasmas cerca de la Puerta Sur, los bandidos expulsando gente del Callejón del Mendigo, y el flujo de refugiados desde el sur, Bree está lleno de actividad... y no siempre de forma positiva. Los Sureños son un problema que me preocupa mas. Mas incluso que las historias de fantasmas de la Puerta Sur; esos relatos existen desde hace años.\
\
'Espero que hayas llegado aquí como un rayo de esperanza, ${PLAYER}. Una vez mas, te doy la bienvenida a nuestra hermosa ciudad.'","'Harry Goatleaf está por el camino hacia el oeste, en dirección a la puerta. Es un hombre bastante malhumorado si me preguntas, pero sin duda tiene algo que decir.'","'La casa de la señorita Hojarena está colina abajo hacia el oeste. Vive en la primera casa del camino que se extiende hacia el norte.'","El Vigilante Cardoon está al este de la Puerta Oeste de Bree.\
\
Harry Goatleaf te dijo que hablaras con el Vigilante Cardoon.","'Gran parte de la historia de Bree y de las Tierras de Bree se guarda dentro de estos muros y en otros lugares seguros de la ciudad. Estamos siendo mas diligentes que nunca para mantener a salvo la historia de nuestra tierra.\
\
'Hombres viles merodean por toda la ciudad, y se habla de sombras que saltan sobre la gente en los últimos días.\
\
'Debes hablar con Mat Matosos. Él y personas como él, aquellos que no tienen mucho, son los mas afectados por estos rufianes. Gira a la izquierda al salir por nuestra puerta y dirígete hacia el suroeste, mas allá de la estatua del enano bajo los aleros, para encontrarlo.'","Encontrarás la Taxidermia de Espinablanca al otro lado del camino frente a la Bóveda de Bree.\
\
Te dijeron que hablaras con Clar Espinablanca en la Taxidermia de Espinablanca.","La Cárcel de Bree se encuentra siguiendo el camino hacia el este a través de Bree, mas allá del Ayuntamiento, luego girando hacia el sur.\
\
Mat Matosos sugirió que hablaras con Lirio Manzanadorada en la Cárcel de Bree.","'Descubrirás que la mayoría de los villanos encuentran su camino hacia las cárceles. Hacia el sur y el este mas allá del Ayuntamiento, pero antes de la Puerta de Madera.'","'Busca al Segundo vigilante Heathstraw justo por el camino, cerca de la Fuente del Jabalí. Estoy seguro de que tendrá información interesante sobre Bree.'","Habla con Maud Dedalera en la bóveda","El Mercado de Lalia está justo al norte de la Fuente del Jabalí en la Plaza del Mercado.\
\
El Segundo-vigilante Heathstraw te ha sugerido que explores el Mercado de Lalia y hables con la propietaria.","Habla con Cebadilla Mantecona en la Posada del Poney Pisador","'Vaya, vaya, hemos estado recibiendo una enorme cantidad de viajeros que llegan a Bree. No tienes el aspecto de uno de esos Sureños, sin embargo...\
\
'Soy Cebadilla Mantecona, y esta es la Posada del Poney Pisador, la mejor posada de todas las Tierras de Bree. Puedes beber aquí y hospedarte aquí, si tienes las monedas. Ahora estoy olvidando algo... me pasa seguido, con lo ocupado que estoy. Ah sí. Debo enviarte a tu próxima parada en tu recorrido por Bree.\
\
'Sal de mi posada y desciende la colina, al oeste mas allá de la Puerta de la Posada. Una corta distancia mas adelante verás que el camino se divide. Gira al norte y visita a Lirio Hojarena en la primera casa allí.'","'Habla con los líderes de los Hombres de Bree. Sigue el camino al oeste fuera de la Sala de Subastas.'","'${PLAYERNAME:Bienvenido[m]|BienvenidA[f]} a las Bóvedas de Bree. No cobramos nada por almacenar muchos de tus bienes y, por una pequeña pero creciente tarifa, almacenaremos aún mas.\
\
'Tenemos protección de la guardia de la ciudad a toda hora del día, así que puedes estar seguro de que tus objetos de valor están a salvo aquí.\
\
'Siéntete libre de mirar alrededor en la entrada antes de cruzar hacia la Taxidermia de Espinablanca.'","Habla con Mat Matosos en el Callejón del Mendigo","'${PLAYERNAME:Bienvenido[m]|Bienvenida[f]} a Bree. Echa un buen vistazo a tu alrededor... estas son las celdas donde terminan quienes tienen malas intenciones hacia la gente de Bree, . También es donde entrenamos a los futuros reclutas de la Guardia y los Vigilantes de la ciudad.\
\
'La diferencia entre ambos es sutil, pero los Vigilantes tienen mayor autoridad para recorrer los alrededores y proteger las muchas granjas de Bree. En las últimas semanas y meses ha habido un aumento en la actividad de bandidos, y los Vigilantes están terriblemente sobrecargados. Cualquier ayuda que puedas dar será apreciada.\
\
'A tu próxima visita, . Desde la cárcel, ve hacia el este bajo la Puerta de los Leñadores, luego gira al sur. Busca el jabalí de bronce frente a la Sala de Subastas de Bree y entra. Habla con uno de los subastadores dentro.'","'Como representante de los Hombres de Bree, te doy la bienvenida a nuestra ciudad. Tras las puertas detrás de mí encontrarás el pabellón de caza de Bree. Cuando hayas ganado suficiente respeto entre los Hombres de Bree, podrás entrar a los salones para comprar artículos de los cazadores.\
\
'Deberías regresar con Graeme Tenderlarch en el Ayuntamiento. Ve hacia el este por este camino hasta llegar a la Puerta del Este, luego gira hacia el noroeste y sigue el camino hasta el Ayuntamiento.'","Mat Matosos se encuentra en el Callejón del Mendigo, al suroeste desde la Escalera del Erudito, luego al oeste bajo la Puerta del Lodo desde el Barrio de Piedra.\
\
Newbold Cortahoja te dijo que hablaras con Mat Matosos después.","La bóveda se encuentra al sur del Vigilante Cardoon. Él te dijo que siguieras el camino y buscaras el gran edificio de piedra protegido por dos guardias.\
\
El Vigilante Cardoon te indicó que hablaras con Tad Gardener o con Maud Dedalera en la bóveda.","'La Sala de Artesanía de Tres Partos está al este y al norte del Ayuntamiento de Bree. Busca allí a Bonny Techador; ella te explicará sobre la sala de artesanía de Bree.'","'Saludos, ${PLAYERNAME:forastero[m]|forastera[f]}. No estoy seguro de por qué Tenderlarch quiere que nos visites aquí en el Callejón del Mendigo... todo lo que tenemos para ofrecer está en las ruinas al norte. Aun así, me pagó unas monedas para asegurarme de que me conocieras y escucharas lo que tengo que decir sobre nuestra pequeña parte de Bree.\
\
'La mayoría de la gente no nos presta atención y no nos oye cuando hablamos de los sonidos en los callejones por la noche: fantasmas merodeando cerca de la Puerta Sur y el terror que nos oprime a todos.\
\
'La mayoría de los bandidos se han instalado aquí, expulsando a los pocos buenos habitantes que quedaban. Ojalá Grimbriar no hubiera huido. Heathstraw es un buen tipo, pero no tan astuto como el Vigilante Jefe.\
\
'Debo enviarte a la Cárcel de Bree para tu próxima parada. No te preocup...s... es improbable que te arresten. Desde aquí sigue hacia el este por el camino hasta pasar el Ayuntamiento de Bree, luego mantente un poco hacia el sur. Verás los cepos frente a la Cárcel. Habla con Lirio Manzanadorada dentro.'","Habla con el Segundo vigilante Heathstraw cerca de la Fuente del Jabalí","Habla con Lalia dentro del Mercado de Lalia","Habla con Harry Goatleaf en la Puerta Oeste","'Cebadilla Mantecona es uno de los habitantes mas destacados de Bree y encontrarás que su establecimiento está bien atendido y frecuentemente ocupado. Búscalo al norte en la Posada del Poney Pisador.'","'Mira aquí. Otra cara nueva en Bree, y no uno de esos morenos Sureños, sino ${PLAYERNAME:un honesto[m]|una honesta[f]} . Es alentador verlo.\
\
'Graeme me dijo que podrían pasar algunos visitantes mientras aprendían sobre las áreas mas importantes de Bree. Pues aquí está... la sala de artesanía de Bree. Tenemos toda clase de artesanos aquí en Tres Partos. Puedes ejercer cualquier oficio que conozcas dentro de esta sala.\
\
'Me dijeron que te enviara hacia una de las piezas de arte mas preciadas de Bree, la Fuente del Jabalí, para hablar un poco de historia con el Segundo vigilante Heathstraw. Lo encontrarás justo colina arriba, al norte, en la Fuente del Jabalí en la Plaza del Mercado.'","'Esta es la Sala de Subastas de Bree. Aquí puedes intercambiar materiales con otros artesanos y aventureros por un pequeño costo, que ayuda a sostener a Bree.\
\
'Puedes revisar nuestros registros para ver los artículos que la gente está ofreciendo actualmente. Si decides listar un artículo con nosotros, lo mantendremos durante un tiempo acordado y, si se vende, tomaremos una parte de las ganancias para pagar nuestros servicios... el resto te será enviado por el Correo. Si los artículos no logran encontrar comprador, te los devolveremos y nos quedaremos con tus depósitos. Los pormenores de las subastas pueden ser difíciles de entender. El alcalde te entregará una nota explicándolo cuando completes tu recorrido.\
\
'Debes visitar a Tad Cortahoja a continuación. Lo encontrarás al final del camino hacia el oeste.'","Habla con Lirio Manzanadorada en la cárcel de Bree","La casa de Lirio Hojarena está al oeste de la Posada del Poney Pisador.\
\
Cebadilla Mantecona te dijo que hablaras con Lirio Hojarena en su casa.","El alcalde de Bree, Graeme Tenderlarch, pensó que te gustaría familiarizarte con la ciudad propiamente dicha. Te ha enviado a la plaza para comenzar un recorrido por las calles y visitar la ciudad."},
[905]={"Parece que el alcalde Pieblanco ha estado disfrutando un poco demasiado de la comida últimamente","'¡Lo siento, deberías ir a buscar al alcalde! Está en el centro de Delagua, no muy lejos de aquí.'","En la Comarca, se suele pescar en el lugar de pesca que está justo al norte de Delagua.\
\
Dirígete al estanque para saber si la pesca forma parte de la Feria de los Granjeros.","'¿Has vuelto para saber más sobre la Carrera de los Huevos, ${PLAYER}? He oído que en la granja de Arenilla es una auténtica locura por estas fechas. ¡Si quieres visitarla, el caballo que tengo justo detrás te llevará hasta allí!'","'¿Disfrutaste del recorrido, ${PLAYER}? Como puedes ver, hay muchas cosas con las que entretenerse mientras la Feria de los Granjeros esté en el pueblo. ¡Espero que lo pases muy bien!'","Mmm... ¡Hongos!","Godo Ciñatiesa mencionó algo sobre un evento en la granja de Arenilla...","La Carrera de los Huevos parece una locura... ¡Ahora vayamos a Bamfurlargo!","'Oh, ¿alguien más en busca de los deliciosos hongos? Hay de sobra para todos... ¡pero el truco es atraparlos antes de que los perros de Maggot te atrapen a ti!\
\
'Puedes buscar algunos hongos ahora, o puedes terminar tu recorrido volviendo a Delagua y regresando aquí más tarde. ¡Intentaré dejarte unos cuantos!'","Wymarc Cavada está en la granja de Arenilla en la Comarca, justo al este de Cavada Grande y Cavada Pequeña.\
\
Habla con Wymarc Cavada sobre la Carrera de los Huevos.","Viaja a Bamfurlargo para ver los deliciosos y tentadores hongos","'Conque has venido a la Feria de los Granjeros, ¿eh? Con gusto te indicaré el recorrido para que puedas familiarizarte con los eventos. ¡Hay tanto para hacer!\
\
'Lo mejor es que empieces por hablar con el alcalde Pieblanco en el centro de Delagua. Sin duda, este es su festival favorito del año, así que tendrá mucho que contarte sobre él.'","'¡Hola! ¿Te gusta pescar? Durante la Feria de los Granjeros, tenemos muchas misiones emocionantes (y quizás otras no tanto) aquí en el estanque. ¡Es difícil perder en la pesca! Bueno... más o menos.\
\
'Hmm, ¿qué sigue? ¡Ah! Quizás te interese saber qué está pasando en la granja de Arenilla. No está lejos de aquí, pero también hay una forma rápida de llegar. ¡Deberías volver con Caltha Tunelero, la pregonera de Delagua!'","La Pregonera del Festival, Caltha Tunelero, debería conocer un atajo a la granja de Arenilla.\
\
Habla con Caltha Tunelero una vez más.","Bamfurlargo, la famosa granja de Maggot, se encuentra en Marjala, en el extremo sureste de la Comarca. Allí es donde tiene lugar el robo de hongos. Se puede llegar a la granja viajando a caballo desde Delagua.\
\
Habla con Osbert Barroso en Bamfurlargo.","Habla con la pregonera del festival, Caltha Tunelero, en Delagua","'¡Hola, ${PLAYER}! Me alegra ver que te has tomado un descanso de tus aventuras para venir a probar los mejores manjares de la Comarca en la Feria de los Granjeros. Ay, me encanta este festival. ¡Podría comer todo el día!\
\
'He oído que se puede pescar de maravilla en el estanque de Delagua. Ahora, si me disculpas, tengo que hincarle el diente...'","Un caballo está listo para llevarte a la granja de Arenilla de inmediato","'¡Hola, hola! ¿Has venido a conocer la Carrera de los Huevos? Pues has llegado al lugar indicado.\
\
'Cuando quieras jugar, habla conmigo para anotarte en la lista. Espera a que empiece el juego y luego sal a recoger huevos tan rápido como puedas.\
\
'Puedes jugar ahora o terminar tu recorrido y dirigirte a Bamfurlargo. ¡Estoy seguro de que seguiremos aquí cuando vuelvas!'","Habla con el alcalde Pieblanco en la Feria de los Granjeros","¡La Feria anual de los Granjeros llega al pueblo en época de cosecha! Te han ofrecido un recorrido por los numerosos eventos.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro de misiones cuando finalice el evento con el que está asociada.</rgb>","Caltha Tunelero, la Pregonera del Festival, está en la Feria de los Granjeros en Delagua.\
\
Habla con Caltha Tunelero para terminar el recorrido por la Feria de los Granjeros.","Habla con Godo Ciñatiesa en el estanque de Delagua","Habla sobre la Carrera de los Huevos con Caltha Tunelero, la pregonera del festival","Viaja a la granja de Arenilla para ver la Carrera de los Huevos","El alcalde Pieblanco se encuentra en el centro de Delagua durante el festival de la Feria de los Granjeros.\
\
Habla con el alcalde Pieblanco.","Un Recorrido por la Feria de los Granjeros"},
[906]={"The spills are getting closer together","Search the waggon","This seems like the same substance you encountered in Thaurisgar. There is a trail of broken phials.\
\
You should follow the trail leading into Tumladen.","The bile spills have led to Tumladen and keep going further into town.","This one is headed into Tumladen","The waggon is abandoned with evidence of recent use.\
\
Inside the waggon are scattered phials of a green ichor that look eerily similar to you.\
\
Beside the waggon is a spilled phial. There could have been a struggle here.","The trail has led to a dead end","The trail is getting shorter and shorter and must end soon.","A Trail Marked Indagir","Follow the trail up the road","Talk to waggon driver","The trail seems to have led to a dead end.","Follow the trail further into town","You found an abandoned waggon with phials of a familiar substance. This could be the mode of transport Indagir used.\
\
You should search the waggon to support your theory.","This one leads up the road to the right","The bile spills seem to follow the road into Tumladen.","Indagir once again seems to have escaped","'Huh? Who are you?'\
\
The waggon driver rubs his eyes and tries to focus on you.\
\
'My waggon?'\
\
The driver nods his head.\
\
'Some fellow requested a ride all the way to Linhir. I was happy to oblige, but I noticed the phials he was carrying with him had a very pungent and off putting odour. I questioned him about it and he got defensive and hit me... tried to steal the waggon. One of the patrols noticed and gave chase. So he grabbed what he could of his quarry and ran off. I don't know where he is.\
\
'I am sorry.'","Follow the trail of spills into Tumladen","You found an abandoned waggon with traces of a vile ichor that reminds you of the same substance found in Thaurisgar.","It goes further into Tumladen","The trail of spilled substance has led you to an injured waggon driver.","It seems to follow the road","The scattered phials have left a trail","There is an injured waggon driver"},
[907]={"You spy a footprint leading farther into the marshlands","Look for a trail in the Mouths of Entwash that might lead you to Malhar.","'In truth, I would go with you, ${PLAYER}, but I see from my brother's stern look that it is not to be.'","You find a young man standing in the clearing","Go up the hill","'Who are you? You do not look to be a foe, so I judge you friend. I am Malhar, son of Lachnir.'\
\
The young man starts to extend a hand, then winces and holds his side. He gives a wry, pained grin.\
\
'Though if you were foe, I fear I should be somewhat at your mercy. I am starved and wounded and very ready indeed to get back out of this marsh!'","Another footprint. He must have gone this way.","A streak of recently dried mud points up the hill","A Trail in the Entwash","'My brother Malhar slipped his bonds and escaped the Variags. I know not how, only that if anyone might have done so and survived, it was he. Our youngest brother is possessed of the quickest wits in a quick-witted family.\
\
'We had agreed, while they dragged us to Bâr Nadhron, that if any of us escaped we would make for the Mouths of Entwash. I doubt not that he went there and is likely there still.\
\
'We must return to Ost Rimmon, but I beg you, ${CLASS}, go into the marshland and find Malhar. I have every hope he yet lives and, if luck is on our side, has left some trail to find him by.'","The last clue in the trail points up a hill, deep in the Mouths of Entwash. You should see what is there.","'Narvagol, dead? That is a blow. And now the fact that I never polished his armour will haunt me to the end of my days!'","The footprint is clear and it points north","Togbor believes his younger brother Malhar fled into the Mouths of the Entwash after escaping their captors.","'We must return to Ost Rimmon but I beg of you, head into the Mouths of Entwash and search for Malhar. He may still be alive.'","Talk to the young man","Follow the trail in the Mouths of Entwash that might lead you to Malhar.","Search for a trail","Follow the trail","Talk to the young man in the clearing on the hill in the Mouths of Entwash.","Another footprint points northward"},
[909]={"Bring the brigands' note to Thane Ordlac","A Traitor in the Midst?","'Dudsig sent you with this note? Let us take a look at it.\
\
'It appears, my friend, that we have a traitor among us. This note implies that one of my retainers may be in league with Saruman.'","You found a note signed with an 'S' upon the body of a brigand while trying to recover the goods stolen from Oserley.","DNT -- Will not be seen","Thane Ordlac is in the Mead Hall of Oserley.\
\
Dudsig asked you to bring the note you found to Thane Ordlac.","'This is dire news if Saruman seeks to undermine our people. You should take this note to Thane Ordlac...he will wish to know what has transpired. He is young, but he is wise.'"},
[910]={"Tirneldir has asked you to return to Lindil back near the northern gate in upper Lond Cirion.","Search for Tirneldir at the fish traps outside the southern gate","A Trap Sprung","Arthiel said you might find Tirneldir near the fish traps to the south. Investigate to see if you can find out what happened to them.","Arthiel has not seen Tirneldir for some time and told you he may be at his fish traps to the south of Lond Cirion.","There was no sign of Tirneldir at the fish traps just outside of the southern gate in Lond Cirion, he may be at other traps nearby.","'Oh thank you, kind soul!\
\
'Tirneldir has come back, and now he rests. Though wounded, the healers say he'll mend.\
\
'Your kindness will not fade from our memories, be assured of that.'","You have found Tirneldir outside of the southern gate in Lond Cirion. You should speak with him as he appears injured and scared.","You see an injured man near the building ahead","Speak with Tirneldir","Helped Lindil find her missing spouse","There is no sign of Tirneldir. You see more traps on the western shore","'Please help! I beg of you!\
\
'Corsairs are on my tail!'","You have successfully defended Tirneldir","Check the area for signs of Tirneldir","Return to Lindil","'Thank ye kindly for allowing me a moment, friend.\
\
'Aye, I had seen Tirneldir here but he left a bit back to check on his fish traps, and I've not seen him since.\
\
'You can find his traps along the shore outside of the city gate to the south, near a scorched building.\
\
'Luck be with ye in finding him, and I hope no shadows darken their tale.'"},
[911]={"'I have scouted the Emyn Duir, and I have decided if we are to remain in secret here at Halroth, we must do something about the enemy forces that inhabit the lands nearby. I thought we might set traps around the mountain passes near Halroth, but I fear that might alert these very foes to our presence!\
\
'And what happened then? Why, I had a brilliant thought! What about laying traps within their own encampments, all in secret? This would certainly confuse them, and they would not even think to look for us here. I have already made the traps. Would you be willing to sneak into several enemy encampments in order to set them in place? I am sure you would enjoy it!'","You have set all of Terna's traps in the Emyn Duir encampments. It would be best not to return to Halroth unless absolutely necessary, for if you were followed you might endanger the secrecy of the mission. But you know Terna would be satisfied by the thought of enemies stumbling into her traps within their own camps, and you can't help but smile.","Set traps in the encampment of Angathrai (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Terna has devised a plan to trap enemy forces within their own encampments.","Set traps in the encampment of Matum Graz (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Set traps in the encampment of Urshúlagar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Set traps in Matum Graz","Set traps in Urshúlagar","Set many traps in encampments throughout Emyn Duir.","Set traps (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","A Trap Upon Emyn Duir","Enemy encampments can be found throughout Emyn Duir.\
\
You should hide traps at these encampments to confuse the enemy forces within.","This is a good place to set a trap","Completado","Set traps in Angathrai"},
[912]={"Lleva las flechas a Wistan","'¿Trajiste mis flechas y el cuerpo?'","'¿Flechas, pero ningún ciervo? ¿Fallé el tiro?\
\
'¡Ah! Una criatura rastrera llegó antes que yo al cuerpo. Qué humillación.\
\
'Supongo que debemos agradecer que el pescador y su esposa no sufrieran daños.'","Garbert está en su cabaña al sur de Echad Candelleth, en una bifurcación del río Bruinen.\
\
Deberías hablar con Garbert acerca de la criatura.","Garbert ha ideado un plan para atrapar a la criatura sigilosa.","Habla con Garbert y lleva a cabo su plan para capturar a la criatura","Habla con Garbert","'Si colocamos estos peces bajo la ventana abierta de mi cabaña, creo que podríamos sorprenderlo cuando regrese para intentar acercarse otra vez a la cuna. No sabrá que Afanen tendrá a Whelan a salvo.\
\
'Avísame cuando puedas partir, ${PLAYER}, y podremos prepararnos. No soy cazador, así que envié un mensaje a un amigo mío, un cazador llamado Adwold, para que nos ayude. Se reunirá con nosotros más tarde.'","Una Trampa para la Criatura","Garbert está en su cabaña al sur de Echad Candelleth, en una bifurcación del río Bruinen.\
\
Debes hablar con Garbert cuando puedas llevar a cabo su plan para capturar a la criatura.","Wistan está en su hoguera en Echad Candelleth, el campamento élfico en Tâl Bruinen, al norte de la cabaña de Garbert.\
\
Garbert sugirió que devolvieras las flechas de Wistan.","'¡Nunca había visto una criatura así! ¿Estás seguro de que no volverá?\
\
'Aun así, permaneceré alerta hasta estar completamente seguro. Gracias, de todos modos.\
\
'Deberías devolver estas flechas a tu amigo cazador.'","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para ir? Preparemos la trampa para atrapar a esa criatura.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta es una misión en solitario y no puede completarse en Comunidad.</rgb>"},
[913]={"Busca mineral en los rascacuevas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Mineral recogido (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","El mineral se puede encontrar en los depósitos y en los rascacuevas que merodean la grieta al sur de Zelem-melek.\
\
Deberías recoger mineral de esta zona.","Mineral brillante recogido de un depósito mineral (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Extrae mineral de los depósitos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Has conseguido muchos minerales raros de la traicionera grieta en el sur de Zelem-melek.","Completado","Has descubierto una profunda grieta en los límites al sur de Zelem-melek, llena de depósitos de mineral sin explotar.","Una grieta traicionera"},
[915]={"¡Has sido ${PLAYERNAME:capturado[m]|capturada[f]} por los Ordâkhai!","Escapa antes de que aparezcan más Ordâkhai.","Recupera el segundo volumen del libro \\qLos Viajes de Kábuzar\\q de los Salones de Lajór en Zajâna.","Recupera \\qLos Viajes de Kábuzar Volumen II\\q","Derrota a los Ordâkhai dentro de los Salones de Lajór (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","\\qLos Viajes de Kábuzar Volumen I\\q recuperado","Recupera el primer volumen del libro \\qLos Viajes de Kábuzar\\q de los Salones de Lajór en Zajâna.","\\qLos Viajes de Kábuzar Volumen II\\q recuperado","Escapa con los libros antes de que suene la alarma y lleguen más Ordâkhai.","Ordâkhai derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Un tesoro en azul","Recupera \\qLos Viajes de Kábuzar Volumen I\\q","El Consejo de las Joyas ha robado un libro de gran importancia histórica para los Pohâni titulado \\qLos Viajes de Kábuzar\\q, separado en dos volúmenes. Ahora pretenden destruirlo. Por favor, recupera el libro de los Salones de Lajór.","Escapa con los libros antes de que lleguen más Ordâkhai.","'¡Tienes ambos volúmenes! ¡Esa es una noticia maravillosa! Vámonos rápido, antes de que lleguen más Ordâkhai para impedir nuestra huida.'"},
[916]={"'I am saddened to hear that two more of my friends have fallen silent, but I am grateful to see this dear Huorn once more. Hoom, I only wish I could have returned sooner to help them...\
\
'Hoom... he has long wandered these woods, and we have known each other well in our time. I can trust him, as I am now sure I can trust you.'","Quickbeam can be found at Derndingle in south-eastern Fangorn Forest.\
\
You have found one of Quickbeam's Huorns, and it seemed eager to return to his side. You should speak with Quickbeam.","Quickbeam's Huorn can be found to the south-west of Derndingle.\
\
You have found a Huorn that appears to be sleeping, but still aware. You should poke it and see if it responds.","This Huorn has been slain by the insects and wood-trolls of the forest","Search for Quickbeam's Huorn","'If we are to reclaim this forest, it will take more than the two of us, little one.\
\
'A few of my Huorns still wander these woods... yet, I have not seen them in some time. I would ask that you seek them out while I continue to tend to Derndingle.\
\
'One lurks to the north, another in the forest's centre to the west, and one off the path to the south-west. Do not fear, ${PLAYER}, my Huorns are gentle so long as you do not aim to bring them harm.'","Quickbeam desires to find Huorns he once tended in Fangorn Forest, as he will need all the help he can muster to reclaim the forest.","DNT -- Will not be seen","The Huorn stirs from its rest, and begins walking towards Derndingle","Talk to Quickbeam","Another of Quickbeam's Huorns can be found to the west of Derndingle.\
\
Quickbeam has asked you to seek out one of his Huorns in Fangorn Forest. After finding the first Huorn turned tree-ish, you should continue your search.","'...'\
\
The Huorn does not respond to your approach.","Quickbeam's Huorn can be found to the south-west of Derndingle in Fangorn Forest.\
\
You have discovered two of Quickbeam's Huorns, but they were slain or tree-ish. You should search for Quickbeam's Huorn in the last location he mentioned.","<rgb=#FF00FF>Poke</rgb> at Quickbeam's Huorn","A Tree-ish Slumber","This Huorn has gone tree-ish and will not awake as others might","One of Quickbeam's Huorns can be found to the north of Derndingle.\
\
Quickbeam has asked you to seek out one of his Huorns in Fangorn Forest as he hopes to ask for their aid."},
[917]={"Has derrotado a la amenaza en la escalera.","La fuente del temblor se encuentra en el campamento de trasgos de Khadar-zarâm, en la cima de la escalera.","Un temblor bajo los pies...","Completado","Al entrar en Khadar-zarâm, sentiste un gran temblor bajo tus pies...","¡Troll de Khadar-zarâm derrotado!","Encuentra la fuente del temblor","¡Un troll! Elimínalo, pues es una gran amenaza para Khazad-dûm"},
[918]={"Los braseros se encuentran a los pies de las estatuas de los enanos a lo largo del borde norte de la Segunda sala de Nud-melek.\
\
Debes encender los braseros como tributo al fino trabajo en piedra de la época de Durin.","¡El Puente de Khazad-dûm está destrozado!","Svanr fue llamado a tu lado","Enciende los braseros a los pies de las estatuas de los enanos de piedra (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con Svanr en el Puente de Khazad-dûm","El Puente de Khazad-dûm está al este de los enanos de piedra en la Segunda sala.\
\
Debes viajar con Svanr al Puente de Khazad-dûm.","Svanr puede ser llamado con el cuerno.\
\
Debes hablar con Svanr.","El cuerno de invocación se encuentra cerca de Svanr en las escaleras de Khadar-zarâm.\
\
Debes llamar a Svanr para hacerle saber cuándo estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para partir.","Brasero encendido (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Maravilloso! Ahora... vamos a encontrar el Puente de Khazad-dûm, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Me alegra tenerte conmigo en esta peregrinación, porque ninguno de los monumentos históricos de Moria debería ser visto solo.'","Encuentra el Puente de Khazad-dûm con Svanr","'Estoy aquí para admirar los grandes árboles de piedra y ver esta legendaria sala con mis propios ojos antes de salir a la luz.\
\
'Si vas a bajar conmigo, rindamos homenaje a las estatuas de los enanos de la época de Durin que bordean la sala. La leyenda dice que había braseros a los pies de los enanos que proyectaban un resplandor naranja a lo largo de toda la Segunda sala... pero hace mucho tiempo que no se encienden.'","Svanr está en el Puente de Khazad-dûm.","Un tributo de luz","'¡Esto es una locura! ¡El puente está roto, ${PLAYER}! No esperaba una tragedia así...'","Svanr ha sugerido que enciendas los braseros a los pies de las estatuas de los enanos que bordean la Segunda sala de Nud-melek.","Svanr desea encontrar el Puente de Khazad-dûm a continuación","Usa el cuerno de invocación para llamar a Svanr","'¡Ah! Por fin hemos llegado. Ha sido un gran viaje, y me alegra que lo hayamos hecho juntos.\
\
'Pero... algo no está bien aquí.'","Habla con Svanr (usa el cuerno para invocarlo)"},
[919]={"After helping to unload a ship, Tâbrim has reported that a strange creature escaped its crate and fled into the Sail-haven.","'Did you see it? There is a beast loose in the Sail-haven!\
\
'It burst out of that crate over there, and then it ran off into the Sail-haven. It was so swift that it even tore up some of the stonework as it went! I'm told that this shipment was for the dwarf, Henok, and if I've nothing to offer him, it won't be long before word reaches Khôltekh and the rest of the Kindred of the Coins.\
\
'What am I going to do?! If Eshmun finds out, he'll have my head! Won't you help me?'","Henok can be found in a small alley in the Sail-haven.\
\
One of the Temámir, Henok, has arrived to collect his companion. You should talk to Henok.","'Ah! You have found my new companion!\
\
'I spoke to Tâbrim, and much the same as you I suppose, my path led me to this alley. It is all right, friend. I can handle this matter from here, and I think this cave-claw will find quite the pleasant home in the Shoreward Stone. I do thank you for helping to calm him down, though. It is quite the experience to walk the streets of Umbar Baharbêl, and if we are being honest, it can be a bit much for anyone!\
\
'I must confess, though, I do not know your name. What is it?'\
\
You tell Henok your name, and he smiles.\
\
'Ah, well, that might be a strange name for a cave-claw, but we'll give it a try. You have my thanks!'","Kindly offer the potato to the cave-claw","As you approach the cave-claw, you can tell that it is deeply distressed and overwhelmed by its new surroundings in Umbar Baharbêl.\
\
Deciding that it might be unwise to try to capture the creature yourself, you look about the alley and notice a few sacks of potatoes. You hope that offering it something in kindness might soothe the cave-claw's fears.","Sacks of potatoes can be found in a small alley in the Sail-haven.\
\
You have found the cave-claw, but it appears very uneasy. You should find something you can offer it to help calm it down.","A Troublesome Shipment","As Tâbrim suggested, the crate appears to have been broken from the inside!","The escaped creature can be found somewhere in the Sail-haven.\
\
Tâbrim informed you that the creature tore up some stonework as it fled into the Sail-haven. You should follow the damaged stonework and see where it leads.","The broken crate can be found near Tâbrim on the piers of the Sail-haven.\
\
Tâbrim has asked you to examine the broken crate. You should inspect the broken crate.","The stonework has been damaged by the frantic passage of the escaped creature","Collect a potato from one of the nearby sacks","To your surprise, a fearful cave-claw has taken refuge in this alley","Follow the trail of damaged stonework and find the escaped creature","Talk to Henok","Carefully approach the cave-claw","The cave-claw can be found in a small alley in the Sail-haven.\
\
You have found a fearful cave-claw, and it is clearly overwhelmed by its new home. You should carefully approach the cave-claw.","Examine the broken crate","That looks like a good one!","The cave-claw can be found in a small alley in the Sail-haven.\
\
You have collected a fine potato, and you should offer it to the frightened cave-claw.","Your kindness appears to have calmed the cave-claw, and you hear a voice behind you"},
[920]={"A Troubling Delay","Stanric is troubled by a late delivery from one of his men, Brifard, in Parth Celebrant. He wishes for you to seek out Brifard and discover why he is running so late.","'Do you have a moment, ${PLAYER}? In all of our recent turmoil, there is something that completely escaped my memory. To the east lies Parth Celebrant, and more importantly, one of my men, Brifard.\
\
'I sent him out with a peasant to gather reeds for Stangard, but he has yet to return. Brifard means well, but sometimes he fails to see the importance of small tasks.\
\
'It would mean a great deal to me if you would track him down. He should be at a small camp in northern Parth Celebrant, just outside Thinglad. You have my thanks.'","Talk to Brifard","Brifard is stationed at a camp in northern Parth Celebrant near south-east Thinglad.\
\
Stanric has asked you to attend to one of his men, Brifard.","'Of course, Stanric would send someone. Come then, let us speak.'"},
[921]={"Anborn recalls bringing Gollum forth to be questioned by Faramir shortly after his capture, and his fears for the journey of the Halflings and the gangrel-creature.","Talk to Anborn","'The night passed without incident. I was glad to be rid of the gangrel-creature when Faramir led them away in the morning.\
\
'I cannot fathom what could have passed between Captain Faramir and the Halfling to make my lord grant them free passage in Ithilien, but all that I witnessed between them led me to believe that it was some strange, important errand. I trust my lord's judgment.\
\
'I wish I had better news to tell you of your friends. They seemed hale enough ere they departed, but, as I said, they made for an evil place...the pass of Cirith Ungol.'","Anborn can be found within Henneth Annûn in North Ithilien.\
\
Anborn has offered to tell you more of the strange Halflings and their time among the Rangers.","A Troubling Path","Anborn can be found within Henneth Annûn in North Ithilien.\
\
Anborn has finished his tale, and you should now ask him if there remains any more to tell.","Listen to Anborn's tale","'This is the last I saw of them until we parted ways in the forest. I can share what I remember, for these memories will not soon be forgotten.\
\
'It was a strange discussion, and though I do not know the context, perhaps you can guess at it and relay the tale to the friends of the Halflings.\
\
'Faramir asked me to bring the gangrel-creature to him so that he could question it, and so I did.'","'I have more yet to tell. Are you ready to hear of it, ${PLAYER}?'"},
[922]={"The bridge along the Father's Path is out. You will need to find a way around.\
\
You should talk to Hórin.\
\
Use the summoning horn to call Hórin to your side.","Head south along the Father's Path","'That is all I saw. Although the Orcs and hobgoblins are not on friendly terms, Dushtalbúk and Loknashra are forming alliances of their own. I expect that is bad news for us, yes?\
\
'The Angmarim have set up camp to the south-east. They call it Mullach Cagar. I am afraid I do not know their aims, but that camp must be of some importance to them. They have poured no small effort into proving themselves valuable allies to the hobgoblins, seemingly to gain safe passage from the drakes. I hope you and Hórin can find out more. I have a very bad feeling about this.'","Find Molkha","The bridge along the Father's Path is impassable","'Let me start from the beginning. Here's what I saw....'","A Troubling Report","A flare shoots up from the valley below","'It seems our enemies are forming alliances right in front of our faces! My blood boils to hear how they use fallen dwarves as bargaining chips in their games of state-craft! Even with those \\qgifts\\q, I did not foresee the Frost-horde accommodating the Angmarim in this fashion. From what I understood, Sauron's torture of Hrímil had made his former servants her hated enemies. I remember what she did to Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior! It may be that times change, or perhaps she has some nefarious plan in mind for her former foes? Bah, trying to understand the motivations of a Dragon feels like a waste of time. She means to use whatever is at her disposal to exterminate the dwarves, I'm sure!\
\
'But I do think this news merits some investigation before we continue. We need to know why the Angmarim are up here in the first place, and we need to do something about this nest of drakes before they threaten Fellgát and our approaching reinforcements.'","Molkha calls to you as you approach","Molkha has observed a troubling discourse between enemy forces.","You have found Molkha on the frozen lake south-west of Fellgát.\
\
You should talk to Molkha to receive her report.","Talk to Hórin in the valley","Speak to Molkha on the frozen lake south-west of Fellgát to hear her scouting report.\
\
You should complete 'Instance: A Troubling Report.'","Molkha should be somewhere near the frozen lake south-west of Fellgát.\
\
You should find Molkha with Hórin.","The time has come to travel high into the Welkin-lofts seeking Ausma's apprentices.\
\
You should head south with Hórin and travel along the Father's Path.","Talk to Molkha and hear her troubling report","Molkha should be somewhere near the frozen lake, south-west of Fellgát.\
\
You should talk to Molkha.","'Bah, the bridge is out! I suppose I should not have expected the road to be in good condition after all these years. The Orcs certainly wouldn't maintain it! Let us see if we can find a way around by walking across that frozen lake down there. Hmm. Molkha should be around here somewhere. Keep an eye out for her signal.'","'Hello again, ${PLAYER}. Keep an eye on the sky, because this area is a drake hunting ground! A big one flies overhead quite often, hunting for goats. I've seen him pluck one right off the side of the mountain and carry it up to the cliff tops there, where I wager he has a nest of whelplings to feed!\
\
'As for my report, I have both good news and bad. The good news is that I was able to observe the hobgoblins passing through here. The bad news is... well, I should just start from the beginning.'","Talk to Molkha in the valley","Call Hórin and talk to him","Now that you have Molkha's report, it is time to move further up the mountain.\
\
You should talk to Hórin and decide how to proceed.","'Now that the camp is ready to receive our reinforcements and provide us adequate shelter in this harsh place, it is time we venture out in search of our enemies. Ausma's apprentices Molkha, Kyrstig, and Klúso are out there in the wild somewhere, spying on the hobgoblin host. They are to signal us when they see us approaching and give to us their report. If we're lucky, they will have some information on why Dushtalbúk is all the way up here in the freezing cold!\
\
'Let us begin by heading south up the Father's Path. It should wind all the way up the peaks, but who can say what condition the ancient road might be in? Lead the way, ${PLAYER}.'"},
[923]={"'¡Aquí tienes, ! Por tu esfuerzo, he decidido darte una de mis recetas de tarta -- ¡asegúrate de no usar bayas en mal estado!\
\
'Y si te queda estómago para tartas después de todas las aventuras con tartas que has tenido, ¡también quiero darte una de ellas!\
\
'Gracias de nuevo por tu esfuerzo, ${PLAYER}, ${PLAYER:recuperador[m]|recuperadora[f]} de tartas!'","Has recorrido toda la Comarca ayudando a devolver tartas en mal estado a Holly Corneta -- ¡no es poca hazaña!","'{un verdadero amigo[m]|una verdadera amiga[f]}, , y gracias a ti, ¡mi negocio está a salvo! Si me das un momento, buscaré una de mis recetas para ti.\
\
'Ahora, ¿dónde la dejé?'","${PLAYERNAME:Un verdadero amigo[m]|Una verdadera amiga[f]} de Holly Corneta","'¡Gracias por toda tu ayuda, ${PLAYER}! ¡Mis tartas están a salvo!'","Holly Corneta está al norte de la plaza principal de Hobbiton.\
\
Holly ha decidido darte una de sus recetas de tartas y te espera para hablar contigo.","'¡Tartas, tartas, tartas! ¡Tartas, tartas, tartas!'"},
[924]={"'¡Aquí tienes, ! Por tu esfuerzo, he decidido darte una de mis recetas de tarta -- ¡asegúrate de no usar bayas en mal estado!\
\
'Y si te queda estómago para tartas después de todas las aventuras con tartas que has tenido, ¡también quiero darte una de ellas!\
\
'Gracias de nuevo por tu esfuerzo, ${PLAYER}, ${PLAYER:recuperador[m]|recuperadora[f]} de tartas!'","Has recorrido toda la Comarca ayudando a devolver tartas en mal estado a Holly Corneta -- ¡no es poca hazaña!","'{un verdadero amigo[m]|una verdadera amiga[f]}, , y gracias a ti, ¡mi negocio está a salvo! Si me das un momento, buscaré una de mis recetas para ti.\
\
'Ahora, ¿dónde la dejé?'","${PLAYERNAME:Un verdadero amigo[m]|Una verdadera amiga[f]} de Holly Corneta","'¡Gracias por toda tu ayuda, ${PLAYER}! ¡Mis tartas están a salvo!'","Holly Corneta está al norte de la plaza principal de Hobbiton.\
\
Holly ha decidido darte una de sus recetas de tartas y te espera para hablar contigo.","'¡Tartas, tartas, tartas! ¡Tartas, tartas, tartas!'"},
[925]={"'¡Hola, Hola, ${PLAYER}!","'¡El Correo Rápido está funcionando bien! ¡Sin quejas por el momento!'","'¡Gracias de nuevo por tu trabajo restaurando el Correo Rápido, ${PLAYER}! ¡Nuestro buen nombre significa tanto para mí!\
\
'Oh, había una cosa más. Si tienes un momento, dímelo.'","El Maestro de Correos Ganapié está en Delagua, cerca del Agujero Municipal.\
\
El Maestro de Correos Ganapié te ha pedido hablar con él sobre algo.","Has ayudado a restaurar el buen nombre del Correo Rápido, y el Maestro de Correos Ganapié está encantado con lo que has hecho.","${PLAYERNAME:Un Verdadero Amigo[m]|Una Verdadera Amiga[f]} del Correo Rápido","'No, no tengo más correo para que entregues; ¡solo quería felicitarte por tu servicio!\
\
'A partir de ahora, ¡eres ${PLAYER} del Correo Rápido! Gracias otra vez por tu servicio, ¡y te llamaré cuando volvamos a necesitarte!'"},
[926]={"Mildly blighted crocodile meat obtained (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","A Unique Taste","Bíralad wants to treat the scouts of Sâr Marsag to a new meal and has asked you to gather crocodile meat and mushrooms from the Lair of the Shadlúgai to the north-east.","You have gathered mushrooms and crocodile meat that Bíralad needed for his recipe from the Lair of the Shadlúgai. Return to him in Sâr Marsag.","Return to Bíralad in Sâr Marsag","\\qSafe\\q mushrooms gathered (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'${CLASS}! You are back!\
\
'I trust that your task has been a success?'\
\
You give Bíralad the meat and mushrooms you gathered.\
\
'This is exactly what I needed, friend. You have my thanks!\
\
'I will get started cooking the rot right out of these. I will be sure to save you a bowl for when you return. The camp is sure to love the variety to their meals.'","Obtain mildly blighted crocodile meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Adventurer! I need your help to make a treat for the camp.\
\
'I grow tired of making the same lousy meals every day, but I concocted a recipe that will surely spice things up. I just need some help to gather the ingredients.'\
\
Bíralad pulls out a scrap of paper with notes scribbled on it.\
\
'I need you to get me some crocodile meat from the beasts up north-east in the marshlands we call the Lair of the Shadlúgai. I know they are rotten with the pale blight, but I am certain I can cook that right out and it will add a nice flavour to it. Can you also get me some mushrooms from the forest? Try and find the safe ones that have managed to escape the blight... I shouldn't add more of that than will already be in the meat.'","Gather \\qsafe\\q mushrooms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[927]={"'Will you fight your way onto my ship and retrieve my three chests of valuables? You will be rewarded, of course. My ship is docked to the east of here, and some of the ruffians and bruisers that now lurk here in the Fleet-fast were once members of my crew. Feel free to slay as many of them as it takes to retrieve my treasures.'","Collect shipboard treasures from Kenza's ship in the Fleet-fast (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The ship docked to the east holds Kenza's valuables, but it also holds deadly mutineers.","Collected shipboard treasures from Kenza's ship (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Is there anything more lovely than being returned treasure that belongs to you? I do not think so, my friend. I would have brought the chests with me when need drove me to escape from those worthless villains... but I will be truthful with you: mutinies may take awhile to form, but when they do happen they happen quickly.\
\
'I am pleased to be reunited with these valuables. I will give you some valuable wisdom as reward: if you choose to captain a ship, do not hire a crew that believes themselves to be more deadly than you are!\
\
'I think my former crew has now learned they were mistaken. Thank you for your assistance with them.'","'My ship has been overrun by mutineers, stranger. They will be dealt with, I assure, but time is short. You see, there is treasure still aboard the ship, and as it is MY ship the treasure is also mine by right.\
\
'Will you fight your way onto my ship and retrieve my three chests of valuables? You will be rewarded, of course. My ship is docked to the east of here, and some of the ruffians and bruisers that now lurk here in the Fleet-fast were once members of my crew. Feel free to slay as many of them as it takes to retrieve my treasures.'","A Valuables Lesson","Furious about the mutineers who stole her ship, Kenza wants you to help her retrieve her valuables from it.","Kenza is by the steps leading to the upper level in the Fleet-fast.","Bring her valuables to Kenza in the Fleet-fast"},
[928]={"La lista de vendedores","'¡Bien hecho, ${PLAYER}! Completar los pedidos puede ser complicado, pero veo que has conseguido todo lo necesario para satisfacer a este cliente.\
\
¡Eres de gran ayuda!'","El mercado está muy concurrido, y muchos clientes en los puestos de venta tienen listas de vendedores que deben completarse.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro de misiones cuando finalice el evento con el que está asociada.</rgb>","Reúne los productos de la lista de vendedores","Daisy Arenas está en su puesto en la Feria de los Granjeros de Delagua.\
\
Llévale a Daisy Arenas los productos que conseguiste.","Lleva los productos a Daisy Arenas","Eso no está en la lista...","Los productos de la lista de vendedores se pueden encontrar por toda Delagua durante la Feria de los Granjeros. La lista está en tu inventario.\
\
Recoge los productos de la lista de vendedores... ¡pero evita los que no estén en ella!","'¡Hola! ¡Ya era hora! Llevo bastante tiempo esperando a que me atiendan, y este pedido no se va a preparar solo, ¿sabes?\
\
'Aquí tienes la lista. ¡Busca estos productos cuanto antes! No tengo todo el día.'"},
[930]={"Erymeldir has asked you to do battle with the various spiders in the Limlight Gorge and gather the venom-glands from them. He hopes to discover which -- if any -- of the spiders might be responsible for Greylimb's affliction.","Collect bloated venom-glands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect large venom-glands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Twistroot the Ent","Collected glowing venom-glands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You should ask Twistroot about spiders in Fangorn Forest.","A Venomous Culprit","DNT","'You gathered those samples, did you? I do hope you were not bitten. Such a bite would likely be fatal, you understand.\
\
'This is a queer thing. The samples you brought from the larger varieties of spider are dangerous, certainly, but I do not think they would harm an Ent. The Onodrim are quite resistant to such things. But this glowing venom...you say it came from a much smaller variety of spider? It is the most potent I have seen. It is very likely the same venom that has afflicted poor Greylimb. Fortunately, with a pure sample available, I should be able to brew a draught that may help purge the venom from him, in time.\
\
'But mysteries remain. How is it that a spider came to possess such a venom, seemingly meant to kill trees and Onodrim, and how did this venom find its way into the water and the roots of the trees here? If we cannot stop it soon, much of the forest along the river's edge will soon sicken and die. You may want to ask the Onodrim if they have seen these spiders lurking about at the forest's edge of late.'","You should bring the venom-glands you collected from the spiders of the Limlight Gorge to Erymeldir at the Limlight Glade.","Bring the venom-glands to Erymeldir","Collected bloated venom-glands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Spiders, you say? Hoom. We have not had any spiders in these woods for many years, many long years indeed. There is bad blood, you know, between the Ents and spiders. That goes far back...hoom, far back indeed.\
\
'Let me see, I believe it was some years after the Men of the Sea and the Elves drove back the old darkness again, and not so long after the Gardens of the Entwives were laid waste, that an old, dark-hearted spider wove her lair not far from here, in the darkest part of old Fangorn. There she waited, preying upon any so unfortunate as to wander in among her maze of webs.\
\
'Of course, in those days, there were few who came here, for the forest had been roused to great anger after the desolation of the Gardens, and many of those who had once lived near the forest had died in the war or been driven away, so there was little prey for one such as she. I believe she grew ever more ravenous, and in time, we discovered that she had even tried to slake her endless hunger with the living sap of the trees, and so, ta-rum, we turned our anger upon her and her brood.\
\
'We drove her out then, brushing aside her webs as a child brushes aside cobwebs, and hounded her until she fled beneath the roots of the Misty Mountains. Hoom-hom! We never heard her name again...what was it? Let me think. Hoom! Gurthúl? Yes, I think that was it.\
\
'Do spiders live so long? I would not think so, but then, I am not a spider, so I cannot say. She would not return here though. She is not strong enough to fight us, and her webs are no hindrance to an Ent, for we can crush stone if we are so inclined. But still, Greylimb is ill from a spider's venom, and the trees around us sicken....'","Erymeldir has asked you and your allies to try to retrieve some poison-glands from the wandering spiders hunting the northern stretch of the Limlight Gorge, in the hopes of identifying the venom that has afflicted Greylimb the Ent.","Talk to Thickbark","'Our deepest roots sicken, and the water of the Limlight runs foul with venom. The Elves tell us it must come from near to this place, but there are no spiders here, hoom.\
\
'Ta-rum! I have just remembered, then! Greylimb told me about it one long summer's day...of a cave he discovered nearby when he was but a slender Enting. Beneath the waters of the river, he said it was, where many of the ancient roots of the forest gathered to drink. Hoom! but he could not show it to me, because we are full-grown Ents now, and too big for the narrow ways within.\
\
'It opens nearly onto our grove here -- over there, next to the Limlight Falls -- but we have seen no sign of spiders creeping about the entrance. Hoom-hom! If they are within, I cannot say how they came to be there.'","Collect glowing venom-glands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected large venom-glands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You should ask Thickbark about spiders in Fangorn.","'The only way to be sure of the source of Greylimb's affliction would be for you to bring me samples of the spiders' venom that I could compare to the poison I found in his blood.\
\
'Alas, I cannot defeat such a creature myself...even my companion Ordhrien would be hard-pressed against those monstrosities.'"},
[932]={"'Creo que ha resultado ser una fiesta de inauguración bastante satisfactoria, ${PLAYER}, ¿no te parece? Y parece que Dinodas no ha provocado un daño irreparable.'\
\
Adoptas una expresión inocente y le preguntas a Bingo a qué se refiere con eso.\
\
'¡Ja, ja! Guárdame el secreto, pero este hobbit ve más de lo que podrías creer! Sí, soy un tipo bastante perceptivo, y no gano nada guardándome las cosas para mí... ¡asi que desvelaré cualquier misterio al instante! Me di cuenta del error de mi primo muy pronto, y sabía que el cuadro era, por fuerza, del hogar-hobbit equivocado. ¿Quién crees que le dijo a Camelia dónde encontrarte a ti y a Dinodas, justo después de vuestro robo del regalo? Es más lista que el hambre, y pensé que a vuestra pequeña conspiración le vendría bien un poco de ingenio. ¡Sin ofender, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'¿Pensabas que me crucé con Magetha Cavada por accidente, o que no le sugerí que trajera a su casa de fieras a la fiesta? Tengo bastante experiencia gestionando los diversos aprietos en los que los Boffin se meten ellos solitos y, de hecho, ¡resulta que yo mismo he causado bastantes travesuras!'\
\
Bingo suelta una carcajada y te da una palmada en la espalda.\
\
'Oh, una cosa más. Ha llegado a mis manos un caballete y creo que deberías quedártelo tú. Pertenecía a un artista que conocí en el camino poco antes de llegar a la Comarca Allende; cuando hablé con él, me reveló que no solo se había encontrado con un pariente mío, ¡sino que había pintado una casa hobbit para él! Me dijo que ya no necesitaba el caballete y que podía quedármelo. Bueno, se me dan mejor las palabras que los cuadros, así que no tenía intención de conservarlo. Te lo cedo a ti, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Y sí, ya que lo has adivinado: me dijo la dirección que Dinodas le había dado y supe al instante que era la equivocada, así que decidí gastarle esta broma a mi primo. Puede que no sea tan perceptivo como te he hecho creer, pero aun así ha sido una buena chanza, y creo que al final todo ha salido bien.\
\
'Gracias por toda tu ayuda para hacer esto posible, ${PLAYER}. Realmente creo que ha sido una inauguración muy al estilo Boffin, ¡y no habría deseado que fuera de otra manera!'","Habla con Bingo Boffin en la calle Aguamiel","Bingo Boffin está fuera de la nueva casa de Angélica en la calle Aguamiel.","Ahora que todo ha sido resuelto (esperemos) y todos los Boffin han vuelto, ¡es hora de que la fiesta de inauguración de la casa de Angélica comience!","Una inaguración muy Boffin","Habla con Prisca Boffin dentro del nº 8 de la calle Aguamiel y asiste a la fiesta de inauguración de la casa de su hija.","'¿Estás listos para ayudarnos con los preparativos, ${PLAYER}?'","'La fiesta se ha reanudado, y con mis hijos de vuelta no llevará nada de tiempo hacer que la nueva casa de Angélica esté lista para la celebración.'","Prisca Boffin está en el nº 8 de la calle Aguamiel, y está lista para que la fiesta de inauguración de la casa empiece por fin."},
[933]={"You have failed to lead Hírkha to safety","You have found Hírkha, a lost nether-hound as you travelled through Ilmabiri and have led her to safety at the guard post Kruha-sûrja. You should talk to Lebíthi.","You have found Hírkha, a lost nether-hound as you travelled through Ilmabiri. After introducing yourself to her, she seems willing to follow you. You should lead Hírkha to Kruha-sûrja, the guard post in the northern part of the sewers beneath the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.","Talk to Lebíthi","Lead Hírkha back to Lebíthi","You have been asked to stay on the look-out for a lost nether-hound as you travel through Ilmabiri.","A Very Brave Dog","You have found Hírkha, a lost nether-hound as you travelled through Ilmabiri. You should introduce yourself to her.","Introduce yourself to Hírkha","A child of the Sail-haven has lost her dog after it ran into the sewers chasing a rat. Lebíthi has asked you to keep an eye out for the dog while you traverse Ilmabiri.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will fail if you are defeated or log out. If this occurs, it will be removed from your quest log and you will need to accept it again.</rgb>","'While you are travelling through the tunnels, I have a favour to ask of you. A girl has lost her dog, Hírkha. They were walking through the Sail-haven when the hound took off, chasing a rat. She believes the dog followed the rat into the sewers and has not seen Hírkha since. If you happen to see a nether-hound on your trek through Ilmabiri, there is a small reward for her return.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will fail if you are defeated or log out. If this occurs, it will be removed from your quest log and you will need to accept it again.</rgb>","'You found her! This is such good news!\
\
'I will be honest with you that I did not expect her to be found alive. She is lucky to not be inside the belly of a crocodile! I will see that she is returned to her owner. Hírkha must have been very brave to survive down here. Thank you for her rescue!'","Hírkha wags her tail and looks willing to follow you","You spot a small brown dog","Find the lost dog, Hírkha","Hírkha has reached safety"},
[934]={"Los jabalíes salvajes, perfectos para carne o salchichas, pueden encontrarse merodeando por las afueras de Archet.\
\
Debes recoger carne de jabalí para la próxima comida de Mundo, para que no se muera de hambre.","Un Estómago Muy Vacío","Mundo Sacovilla-Bolsón aguarda tu regreso en la aldea de Archet.\
\
Debes llevar la carne de jabalí que recogiste a Mundo, quien probablemente se la coma toda. Solo esperas que sea suficiente para satisfacerlo.","Lleva a Mundo su almuerzo de carne fresca de jabalí","'¡Eh, tú ahí! ¡Sí, tú ahí! ¡Estoy muy hambriento!\
\
'No he comido nada desde que una mujer me dio un poco de pan con mermelada esta mañana para desayunar. Esa comida apenas bastaría para un conejo, ¡mucho menos para un hobbit adulto como yo!\
\
'Si me consigues comida de verdad, te recompensaré generosamente. ¡Quiero algo sustancioso y delicioso!'","Esta misión no puede completarse fuera de la introducción.","Mundo Sacovilla-Bolsón, un compañero prisionero del campamento Montebruno, está naturalmente muy hambriento después del tormento, pues los hobbits tienen apetitos insaciables.","Recolecta carne de jabalí para la próxima comida de Mundo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Carne fresca de jabalí recolectada (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿Qué sigues haciendo aquí? ¿Estás poniendo comida en mi estómago ahora mismo? ¿Tienes algún escondite secreto de provisiones? ¿No? ¡Entonces muévete, por favor!'","'¡Hurra, me trajiste carne de jabalí! ¡O tocino! ¡O quizá salchicha..... oh, no importa; puedo hacer un poco de cada una!'\
\
Mundo pesa el paquete de carnes en sus manos.\
\
'Esto me dará algo para masticar por un rato; con suerte, esta provisión me durará hasta que pueda regresar a casa.'"},
[935]={"Meet with Gûshida in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl about rumours relating to the mistreatment of animals.","Elder Ilaya has asked you to go to Umbar Baharbêl, the City of Corsairs, to investigate rumours of the mistreatment of animals by a man named Ezôti. You should meet with Gûshida in the Upper Ward.","A Vicious Rumour","'We've heard troubling rumours from Umbar Baharbêl about animal mistreatment. I appreciate what you did here for Khûtra's animals, so I know you understand how important our duty is, to protect and respect them. Their lives are as sacred as our own.\
\
'These rumours tell of a street charlatan. They call him Ezôti. His words are sweet but his deeds are dark. He parades animals around for show. He whips them until they do his tricks.' Ilaya spits on the ground, to show her displeasure.\
\
'He does not understand the pact between humans and animals. He does not see them as we do. To him, they are just a means to buy coin and praise. Cheap entertainment, to be used and discarded.\
\
'Go to Umbar Baharbêl, find Gûshida. She can be found in the Upper Ward of the city. She is like you and I. She understands animals. She is looking to expose Ezôti and end his crimes. You've done much to help us and the animals here. Please, find Gûshida, and help the animals there. They don't have much time.'","'Ilaya sent you? Then I know you have a pure heart and devotion to animals. It is good that you've found me. We have much to talk about.'","Meet with Gûshida in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl"},
[936]={"Return to the Temámir Guard Captain Nûru","Return to the Temámir Guard Captain Nûru in Mekab-kuphâr, the Temámir outpost in the southern Khabârkhad.","A Vile Infestation","North of Mekab-kuphâr there is an area infested with spiders. You've been asked to thin their number, lest they over-run Khabârkhad and spill out into greater Umbar-môkh.","'I am grateful. If those spiders got any closer, they might over-run our encampment. You've assured the safety of many Temámir this day.'","Defeat Khabârkhad spiders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You've been asked to cull the number of spiders to the north of Mekab-kuphâr, in Nishabêt.","Defeated Khabârkhad spiders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You look quite capable. We have need of some assistance, if you're willing.\
\
'North of here is an encampment of monstrous spiders. Their numbers are growing, their brood multiplying in the dark with no Man or dwarf to pare them back. Their reach has expanded to the point they've been attacking my patrols here in the southern crypts.\
\
'Please, we need their numbers thinned, before more of my Temámir fall to these terrible beasts. Will you help us?'"},
[937]={"Busca en el carro abandonado","Talk to Hadorion in Barad Faen","'Do I have anything suspicious to report? Why, of course!\
\
'All manner of foul play is afoot! Corsairs are harrying the shores. Animals are pestering our foragers!\
\
'Well, there is one person I do not recognize here, and they seem very anxious.\
\
'I couldn't tell you where to find them, but if they look out of place and disturbed, chances are you have found your quarry.'","You found traces of a green ichor on the victim's clothes. You should report to Hadorion.\
\
Hadorion can be found in Barad Faen.","Talk to Hadorion","'A foul smelling green ichor? We have none of that here in Barad Faen.\
\
'Most of our draughts are for mending and treating injuries. I cannot say such a substance comes from here.'","You found a shard of glass stained with the foul smelling ichor. You should return to Hadorion.\
\
Hadorion can be found in Barad Faen.","A body is found in the middle of the road through Barad Faen. Hadorion is investigating, and needs your help to catch the perpetrator.","Search the corpse","'There is more to discuss.'","The clothes are stained with a green ichor, the stench is foul","Hadorion has asked you to search the body and see if you can find what he could not.","The woman has told you of someone new to town that seems distressed. You should search for them.","Hadorion wishes to speak to you in private, follow him into his hearth.","Follow Hadorion into the cabin","Talk to the distressed man","'You found the victim's clothes stained in a green ichor? That seems to line up with what I found as well.\
\
'It has a fell odour to it also. You should investigate amongst the townsfolk and see if anyone has seen this substance before.'","Look for his abandoned waggon","Hadorion has asked you to question the townsfolk of Barad Faen for more information on the mysterious ichor.","'Hmmm. This shard of glass is intriguing.\
\
'It is... familiar to me, or rather, I've heard of this before.'","Talk to the anxious woman","The man has told you that his waggon was hijacked before arriving in Barad Faen and abandoned along the western exit of Barad Faen.","You found a shard of glass stained with ichor","Talk to the careful merchant","The substance is foreign to Barad Faen","Look for someone who is anxious and puzzled","'What happened here you ask? I'd like to know myself.\
\
'Our men fallen in war, our shores given to the want of Corsairs, land, bridge, and dwelling ravaged by hatred and time. I'm used to all of that, but the sudden end of a man in the middle of the road so close to home, with no sight of Corsair, ship, or pillaging? A dark foreboding indeed... more so than what has wrought these lands for as long as I can remember.\
\
'Perhaps you can find what I could not?'","The concerned merchant has told you the substance is foreign. You should question more townsfolk to see if they have noticed anything suspicious come through.","A Vile Trail","'What is it?!'\
\
The man is startled by your presence.\
\
'I've done nothing wrong! I was just passing through!\
\
'On my way to Lond Cirion, I was. My waggon was hijacked just up the road before arriving here.\
\
'A foul smelling substance? Of course! The person who hijacked my waggon reeked of it.\
\
'I ended up here a day later to find my waggon abandoned on the town's western exit. Surely you will find more of that wretched substance.'"},
[938]={"You found a strange note with barely visible markings. Bring it back to Hadorion.\
\
Hadorion can be found in his cabin in Barad Faen.","Investigate the camp-site","Talk to Hadorion in Barad Faen","The note is barely readable. Maybe Hadorion can make sense of it.","Hadorion wants you to check on a new camp that has been erected to the north.","Hadorion has happened upon more information during his investigation.","'Some new information has shed some light on these new happenings. I shall try to glean more information from the sash you brought back.\
\
'Recently, while out hunting, the folk have noticed a camp in the hills to the north. It has always been empty according to their reports, but there is evidence of recent use.\
\
'As with all cases, this cannot be mere coincidence. It suggests that whoever we are dealing with will not be here for long.'","A Vile Trail Marked by Sea","'What's written on this note is barely readable, but this last line here is of concern: \\qIt is time.\\q It seems we are out of time. Whatever they were planning to do, they plan to do soon.\
\
'I think I may have everything I need to solve this case.'"},
[939]={"'We shall make haste. Are you ready?'","Hadorion wants your help preventing the culprit from making an escape by sea.","Solve the case of the Vile Trail","Hadorion has completed his investigation and needs your help to solve the case.","Talk to Hadorion","'I have been trying to connect the clues and pieces of the puzzle.\
\
'Our culprit is not of this realm and is most likely making their escape... an escape witnessed by our poor victim. They are hastened by worry. They are making mistakes! \
\
'There is an old shipwreck to the south-west. I'd venture to guess that our culprit is going to try and make their escape by fashioning something sea-worthy out of that wreck. We must make haste. We approach under the guise of night.'","Hadorion wants to speak to you about further options pursuing Khâshap.\
\
Hadorion can be found in his cabin in Barad Faen.","'I will need some time to consider our options ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Until then, I want you to seek passage across the seas. We now know that this Khâshap is prone to mistakes when pressured.\
\
'I shall follow the trail to whatever ends. I will make contact with you when the time comes.\
\
'I am grateful for your assistance here.'","A Vile Trail Marked by Shadow"},
[940]={"Indagir, or Khâshap has made their escape. Talk to Hadorion for further instructions.","Hadorion wants your help preventing the culprit from making an escape by sea.","'Good, you're here. The shipwreck is over yonder in the clearing.\
\
'They make fast for an escape using scavenged parts from the shipwreck.\
\
'We must be quick!'","Follow Hadorion in confronting the true culprit to solve the case.","'Let us rid ourselves of this place.'","Hadorion has completed his investigation and needs your help to solve the case.","Confront Indagir","'This Khâshap has gotten away, but now we know what his goal was: to deliver this Bile of Ifrinn.\
\
'We must pursue him at all costs. Meet me back at Barad Faen to discuss our options.'","Talk to Hadorion","A Vile Trail Marked by Shadow"},
[941]={"Follow the trail left by the suspicious figure","'This ichor... it is grotesque and foul in smell. A certain result of fell experiments. I've only heard rumours of such a thing... ghastly abominations roaming the halls of Carn Dûm.\
\
'Of course, I have no experience with this, but my friend was so curious about the depths of that place he decided to venture there. Torvendor was his name.\
\
'I can only assume that whatever lay waiting in those halls has now found its way here to us. I have a new lead.\
\
'One of the townsfolk spotted a suspicious figure running off towards the western road at night. See if you can pick up their trail and follow it to whatever ends.\
\
'I'll be here.'","Search the camp-site","Follow the trail into the tree line","Talk to Hadorion in Barad Faen","The trail veers into the trees to a camp-site","The interloper dropped a strange looking cloth that should be identifiable. You should report to Hadorion.\
\
Hadorion can be found in his home in Barad Faen.","A witness saw a suspicious figure dart off following the western road during the night.","This shard is smaller. The trail keeps going","This shard matches. Keep following the road west","The smell is more foul on this. It continues west","This shard is quite large. The end is near","He was wearing a unique sash","The trail seems to follow the road west. Keep going","'This sash, it is unlike the ilk of Corsair we see that typically trouble these shores.\
\
'Fortunately, it gives us our next clue.'","The trail has led you to an abandoned makeshift camp-site. Search for evidence of use.","¡Te han descubierto!","A Vile Trail of Bile","Hadorion has asked you to pick up the trail of a suspicious figure spotted leaving Barad Faen at night.\
\
The trail should follow the western road."},
[942]={"Has derrotado a Thrâng, y en el proceso, has aprendido que los Ghâshfra sirven al que todo lo ve. Eimyr, el jefe de los Eldgangs, debe ser informado de inmediato, porque ha sido engañado por el que todo lo ve y sin saberlo sirve a sus propósitos malvados.","'Has ganado el respeto de los Eldgangs, pequeño ser. ¡Ahora vamos a ocuparnos del que todo lo ve!'","'¿Has derrotado a Thrâng? Has ganado una gran recompensa de los Eldgangs.\
\
'¿Qué es esto que dices? ¿Los Ghâshfra sirven al que todo lo ve? ¿El que todo lo ve busca liberar el Gran Mal sobre nosotros?\
\
'Los Eldgangs no se quedarán de brazos cruzados y permitirán que esto suceda. ¡Hemos sido traicionados!'","'Los Eldgangs no tienen nada que ver contigo, pequeño ser. ¡Vete!'","Un villano revelado","Eimyr se encuentra en Norbar, en la Grieta de Nûrz Ghâshu.\
\
Has derrotado a Thrâng y tienes su arma como prueba de tu valor. Debes ir a Eimyr y contarle la traición del que todo lo ve.","Has derrotado a Thrâng y descubierto el complot del que todo lo ve.","Lleva la Espada de Thrâng a Eimyr en Norbar"},
[944]={"Aunque los zapadores en la Piedra de Durin hayan sido detenidos, aún pudieron infligir graves daños a la sagrada roca.","Una visión de las profundidades","Lleva los fragmentos de la Piedra de Durin a Haflith en Mekhem-bizru","'Apenas estás comenzando a comprender lo que esta piedra significa para nosotros aquí. Apresúrate y recoge los fragmentos que se rompieron.'","Fragmentos de la Piedra de Durin recogidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Es lo que temía, el daño ya estaba hecho. Aún así, el resto de la piedra se mantiene, vigilando las tranquilas profundidades de Kheled-zâram.\
\
'Un día, quizás, estos fragmentos se reúnan con el resto. Por ahora, los mantendré aquí, a salvo, en caso de que lo impensable suceda y la Piedra de Durin sea destruida.'","Haflith se encuentra en Mekhem-bizru, al noroeste de Uruk-gashan.\
\
Haflith querrá ver los fragmentos de la Piedra de Durin que has recogido.","Recoge los fragmentos de la Piedra de Durin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los fragmentos de la Piedra de Durin se encuentran en Uruk-gashan, al sur de Mekhem-bizru.\
\
Haflith te pidió que fueras a la Piedra de Durin y recogieras los fragmentos que los zapadores orcos habían roto.","'Detuviste a los zapadores orcos, ${PLAYER}, pero me temo que llegaste demasiado tarde. No es tu culpa. Debería haber ido yo mismo tan pronto como los vi. Aunque la Piedra de Durin ha sido salvada, se han hecho graves daños.\
\
'Mientras se preparaban para destruir la piedra, hicieron saltar muchos fragmentos. Ha sido desfigurada y convertida en un objeto de burla. Solo hay un curso de acción para nosotros: debemos recuperar lo que queda.\
\
'Dirígete de nuevo al sur, de vuelta a Uruk-gashan y busca los pedazos rotos de la Piedra de Durin. Reúne lo que encuentres y tráelo de vuelta aquí. Al menos podremos salvar esos fragmentos, y quizás algún día, hacer que la piedra vuelva a ser completa.'"},
[945]={"'¡Muy buenas, ${PLAYER}! ¡Qué sorpresa más agradable!\
\
'Voy de camino a la Comarca Allende para dar la bienvenida a Angélica, la hija de mi prima Prisca, ¡a su nueva casa! Verás, ya ha dejado atrás la veintena, y ha comprado una casa en Nobtella. Qué rápido crecen, ¿verdad?\
\
'Prisa y sus otros hijos están planeando una fiesta de inauguración para Angélica, ¡y estoy segura de que también te darán la bienvenida! Parte de la camada de Prisca hizo el viaje hace unos días; querían encontrar un regalo adecuado para darle a su hermana. Ah... no le digas a Prisca que he dicho eso. No le gusta que me refiera a sus hijos como camada. Se tendría que quedar encamada del disgusto, ¿sabes?'\
\
Bingo se ríe para sí mismo.\
\
'Debo acordarme de apuntar eso. De todas formas... si tienes ganas de fiesta, se supone que tengo que reunirme con mis primos en el centro de Campotieso. Está al noroeste de aquí, en la Comarca Allende.'","Habla con Caléndula Boffin cerca de Tham Amothir","Camellia Boffin y sus hermanos deberían haber llegado ya a Campotieso.","'¡${PLAYER}! ¿Estás en la Comarca Allende para la fiesta de bienvenida de la casa de Angélica? Oh, te va a impresionar el regalo que le he encontrado. ¡Y todos decían que no sería capaz de encontrar algo que le gustara!\
\
'Volvamos con Camelia a Campotieso. ¡Ella y el primo Bingo van a quedar muy impresionados con mi regalo! \\q¡Lo has vuelto a conseguir, Dinodas!\\q dirán. Y ya verás si no, ${PLAYER}, ¡ya verás si no!'","Bingo Boffin ha venido a la Comarca Allende para dar la bienvenida a su prima segunda Angélica a su nueva casa en Nobotella.","Busca a Caléndula y derrota semiorcos en Tham Amothir (${CURRENT}/6)","'¡Bienvenidos de nuevo!\
\
'¿Qué es este regalo de inauguración que has encontrado, Dino? ¡Espero que sea algo que a Angélica le guste de verdad!'","Bingo, Camelia, Caléndula y Dinodas se han reunido en Campotieso","Bingo está en Campotieso con algunos de sus primos segundos.","Habla con Dinodas Boffin y descubre el regalo de inauguración","'Tengo que decirte, Dino, ¡que este cuadro es increíble! Somos afortunados de que encontraras a ese Elfo cuando lo hiciste, ¡porque estoy seguro de que a Angélica le va a encantar este regalo!\
\
'¡No dude de ti ni por un momento, primo!'","'¡Has vuelto!'","Dinodas consiguió que un pintor elfo que pasaba por la Comarca pintase la nueva casa de Angélica.","Caléndula Boffin está cerca de las ruinas de Tham Amothir.","Habla con Dinodas Boffin en Gamwich","Según Caléndula, su hermano Dinodas tenía intención de visitar a un amigo suyo en Gamwich.","¡Dinodas se ha superado! ¡El cuadro es muy bonito!","Camelia Boffin está en Campotieso, pero algunos de sus hermanos se han ido por ahí (como de costumbre).","Dinodas Boffin está en Gamwich, y está encantado de verte.","'¡Bueno, estoy lista para ver ese regalo, Dino! ¿Qué me has traído?'","'Estoy bastante segura de que Dinodas solo quería ir a Gamwich para presumir del regalo de inauguración que encargó para Angélica a unos amigos. Probablemente lo encuentres allí.'","Dinodas sonríe radiante, rebosante de entusiasmo","'¡Preparaos para sorprenderos!\
\
'En mi camino hacia aquí encontré a un Elfo que iba de camino a los Puertos Grises. Viajaba hacia el oeste y mi camino iba hacia el norte, pero caminamos juntos un rato y hablamos de muchas cosas. Era pintor, parece, y aunque poseía una humildad más propia de un hobbit que de un Elfo, puedo decir que no tiene poca habilidad en ese arte. Me quedó claro también que iba sin prisa; no parecía que tuviera prisa en llegar a los Puertos.\
\
'\\q¿Quizá no te importaría pintar algo para mí?\\q le pregunté, y dijo que habían pasado muchos años desde la última vez que había pintado algo de estilo hobbit. \\q¿Cuántos años?\\q le pregunté, pero no me lo quiso decir. Ya sabéis cómo pueden ser los Elfos. En cualquier caso, pensé que esto sería ideal para Angélica: ¡un cuadro de su nueva casa!\
\
'¡Aquí está!'","Bingo está emocionado por ver el regalo de inauguración que Dinodas tiene preparado.","'¡Te doy la bienvenida, ${PLAYER}! ¿Has venido a la Comarca Allende por la fiesta de inauguración de la casa de Angélica? ¡Qué maravilla! He estado ocupada manteniendo a Dinodas y a Caléndula lejos de los problemas, pero madre me ha encargado la tarea y no la voy a decepcionar.'\
\
Le preguntas a Camelia dónde han ido su hermano y hermana, y una expresión de pánico repentino cruza su rostro.\
\
'¿Qué..? ¡Estaban aquí hace un minuto! Les he quitado el ojo de encima un momento, ¿y se han desvanecido? Es muy típico, ${PLAYER}. ¿Puedes hacerme el favor de buscarlos? Caléndula ha estado hablando sobre ir a ver al Elfo de las ruinas al oeste de aquí, pero dónde haya ido Dinodas es un misterio para mí. ¿Quizá Caléndula lo sepa? ¡Más le vale!'","'Es precioso, ¿verdad? ¡Y todos pensabais que no encontraría nada adecuado!'","'Volvamos con Camelia a Campotieso. ¡Ella y el primo Bingo van a quedar muy impresionados con mi regalo! \\q¡Lo has vuelto a conseguir, Dinodas!\\q dirán. Y ya verás si no, ${PLAYER}, ¡ya verás si no!'","'Oh, hola.'","Habla con Bingo Boffin en Campotieso","'Si tienes ganas de fiesta, se supone que tengo que reunirme con mis primos en el centro de Campotieso. Está al noroeste de aquí, en la Comarca Allende.","Dinodas desvela el cuadro de la nueva casa de Angélica","'Buenas, ${PLAYER}.","Busca a Caléndula y derrota semiorcos en Tham Amothir (5/6)","Reúnete con Camelia Boffin y sus hermanos en Campotieso","Derrota semiorcos en Tham Amothir (${CURRENT}/6)","Una visita a la Comarca Allende","'¡Muy buenas, ${PLAYER}! ¿Tus aventuras te han traído a la Comarca Allende? Mi apetito de aventura también me ha conducido aquí y eso es bueno, también: estos semiorcos solo se harían más fuertes hasta quizá llegar a ser una amenaza para la seguridad de los hobbits de Allende, y no podemos permitirlo. ¿Sabías que mi hermana Angélica ahora es uno de ellos? Un hobbit de Allende, quiero decir; no un semiorco.\
\
'¡Es verdad! Ahora reside en Nobotella. Estamos todos aquí para darle la bienvenida a su nueva casa.'\
\
Le preguntas a Caléndula si sabe dónde ha podido ir Dinodas, y sonríe de oreja a oreja.\
\
'Dinodas le ha dado esquinazo a Camelia, ¿eh? ¡Bien por él! ¡Quizá hagamos de él un aventurero después de todo, ${PLAYER}! O quizá no. Estoy bastante seguro de que quería ir a Gamwich para presumir de su regalo de bienvenida para Angélica que encargó a unos amigos suyos. Probablemente lo encuentres allí.'","Habla con Camelia Boffin en Campotieso","'¿Puedes localizar a mis descarriados hermano y hermana? Caléndula ha estado hablando sobre ir a ver al Elfo de las ruinas al oeste de aquí, pero dónde haya ido Dinodas es un misterio para mí. ¿Quizá Caléndula lo sepa? ¡Más le vale!'","Camelia sonríe cálidamente mientras Bingo y tú llegáis","Escuchas los vítores de una niña hobbit cerca de las ruinas","Reúnete con los Boffins de vuelta en Campotieso","Los hermanos Boffin planean reunirse de vuelta en Campotieso, y les encantaría que te unieses.","Encuentra a Dinodas Boffin en Gamwich","Bingo está muy impresionado con el cuadro que Dinodas ha conseguido para Angélica.","Caléndula podría estar metiéndose en líos en Tham Amothir hacia el oeste, especialmente si hay semiorcos en las ruinas.","Dinodas te ve llegar y te indica que te acerques","Examina el cuadro de la nueva casa de Angélica"},
[946]={"'Welcome to Imloth Melui, good traveller. Captain Merenir believes it was you I saw in my dream? Are you the only traveller of your kind who will visit us during this strange darkness, I wonder? Will Merenir send me every one who does? He is a good captain but perhaps not the best interpreter of dreams.\
\
'Still, it is true and well known that I and those of my blood have had dreams of great portent. Are you a bearer of good tidings, ${PLAYER}, or ill? And if you were, would you know the difference?'","Lady Vanyalos can be found in the great hall on the north-east rise of Imloth Melui.\
\
Merenir has asked you to pay a visit to Lady Vanyalos, insisting that somehow she dreamed of you.","A Visit to a Dreamer","It seems that your appearance and the timing of your arrival in Imloth Melui bears a striking resemblance to a dream Lady Vanyalos had the night before.","Talk to Lady Vanyalos in her hall on the north-east rise of Imloth Melui","'Forgive me, ${CLASS}. This is exactly Lady Vanyalos's dream, as she told it to me: a ${RACE}, looking as you, coming up this road under a strangely darkened sky. The description fits exactly!\
\
'Lady Vanyalos will want to speak with you, and at once! You can find her within her hall on the north-east rise. I do not pretend to understand how this can be, but she will certainly be filled with wonder at seeing her dream made flesh. What can this mean?'"},
[948]={"Habla con Laeginn en la Posada Embrujada","'¿Qué es esto? ¿Un mensaje de Ost Galadh? Me ocuparé de ello enseguida.\
\
'Me alegro de ver que has llegado aquí rápido y a salvo. Dale mis saludos a Lomdognir y dile que aquí tengo todo bajo control.'","¡Entrega el mensaje a Laeginn cuanto antes!","Primer hito alcanzado","Laeginn se encuentra en la posada de Audaghaim, en Troncosombríos.\
\
Lomdognir te ha encargado que le entregues el mensaje al elfo Laeginn.","Un mensaje vital","Lomdognir te ha pedido que le lleves un mensaje urgente a uno de sus compatriotas en Troncosombríos.","El segundo hito se encuentra más adelante en el camino al oeste de Emyn Lûm.\
\
Lomdognir ha trazado una ruta concreta que debes seguir con el mensaje que llevas.","'Ha ocurrido algo importante y necesito que enviar un mensaje a nuestro puesto avanzado en Troncosombríos lo antes posible, .\
\
'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:dispuesto[m]|dispuesta[f]} a ser ${PLAYERNAME:nuestro mensajero[m]|nuestra mensajera[f]} en este asunto? Te advierto que necesito que sigas una ruta muy concreta, una que puede estar vigilada por el enemigo, que podría intentar interceptarte. Es muy importante que te abras paso a través de cualquier obstáculo que te pongan y llegues a tiempo.\
\
Hay una serie de hitos a lo largo del camino desde aquí a la aldea en ruinas de Troncosombríos; pasa por cada uno de ellos mientras te diriges hacia allí.\
\
'Cuando llegues, entrega el mensaje a Laeginn; él sabrá qué hacer con él.'","Dirígete al primer hito","El tercer hito se encuentra en el camino, donde este gira hacia el norte, en dirección al pueblo abandonado de Troncosombríos.\
\
Lomdognir ha trazado una ruta concreta que debes seguir con el mensaje que llevas.","Segundo hito alcanzado","¡No entregaste el mensaje a Laeginn a tiempo!","Dirígete al tercer hito","'YOU SHOULDN'T SEE THIS'","'No me malinterpretes, ${PLAYER}, sé que te enfrentarás a peligros por el camino, y quizá incluso caigas en una trampa, pero debes seguir adelante a toda costa. Tu papel en esta batalla no es menor que el mío ni el de ningún otro, ahora que nos enfrentamos a esta oscuridad.\
\
'¡Ahora ve, rápido!'","Tercer hito alcanzado","El primer hito se encuentra en el camino al oeste de Emyn Lûm.\
\
Lomdognir ha trazado una ruta concreta que debes seguir con el mensaje que llevas.","Dirígete al segundo hito"},
[950]={"Derrota a crebain espías (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con Cariad","Cariad te espera en la entrada del refugio de los Cuan-lûth.\
\
Deberías hablar con él allí.","Una apuesta de confianza","Cariad ha sugerido despejar de crebain espías las tierras salvajes al noreste del refugio de los Cuan-lûth.","Has derrotado a crebain espías (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Bien hecho. Ahora mereces saber parte de la verdad: ese campamento que investigaste era nuestro. Hasta ahora mi clan ha evitado a los espías de Saruman, pero saben que debemos estar cerca.\
\
'Si los Montaraces también han notado nuestra actividad, entonces alguien acabará por encontrarnos. Me gustaría que eso sucediera bajo las condiciones de mi pueblo.'","Un dunlendino llamado Cariad ha ofrecido que trabajéis juntos alegando un objetivo común.","'Soy Cariad. Te ahorraré los detalles, pero he avistado a numerosos crebain espías de la Mano Blanca en las tierras salvajes al noreste de aquí. ¿Por qué no me ayudas a derrotar a unos cuantos? Prometo responder a tus preguntas después.\
\
'Oh, no soy tonto... aún no confío en ti del todo. Considéralo una apuesta.'"},
[951]={"'Do you see the pier up there, or the Ship's Prow, as some call it? Well, a man told me that the winds race up its face so fiercely, you couldn't walk off of it if you tried. You'd be shoved back!\
\
'It stands to reason, does it not?'","Gradir said chickens could be found in the Court of Eärnil. The Ship's Prow lies at the very top of Minas Tirith, jutting out of the Citadel.\
\
Find a chicken and drop it off of the Ship's Prow to determine whether Gradir or Tawaris is right.","'What a load of fish-guts! First off, the winds clearly run along the pier down from the tower and fall to the land below. Winds going up. Ha! Doesn't rain fall? Has anyone ever seen rain fly up the pier?\
\
'No, my friends. The winds go down, not up. So say I - and you say otherwise. How shall we settle this? There's gold in your pockets, Tawaris, that should really be in mine.\
\
'What do you say to this? Our ${CLASS} friend here carries a chicken up to the pier's end and tosses it off. If it comes back, you've won. Down it goes? I've won!'\
\
Tawaris nods in agreement and the two look at you expectantly.\
\
'I'll save you the chore of carrying a hen straight from the First Circle. There are some hens in the Court of Eärnil, up in the Third Circle. Go for one of those.'","The soldiers Gradir and Tawaris can be found on the northern side of the Second Circle.\
\
Talk to Gradir to hear his side of the argument.","Find out what happened to the chicken","You drop the chicken and it sails downward, squawking loudly, but it is slowed by an unmistakable updraft!","Talk to Gradir","The soldiers Gradir and Tawaris can be found on the northern side of the Second Circle.\
\
Talk to Tawaris to hear his side of the argument.","You have been asked to help two soldiers settle a wager regarding the Ship's Prow and updrafts.","You should check the First Circle below the Ship's Prow to see what became of the chicken.","Talk to Tawaris","A Wager: In the Wind","The chicken appears somewhat wind-blown and disgruntled, but otherwise unhurt","The two soldiers listen to your account.\
\
'Clearly, I have won. We said that if it fell, the wager was mine, did we not?'\
\
Gradir pauses, shakes his head, and sighs.\
\
'Bah! The gulls can take the rules. You swore there was an updraft, old friend, and it is plain to see that there was. Here, the wager is yours.\
\
'Well, ${PLAYER}, it's a good thing you did not jump off yourself... though that would likely have won me the bet! Still, I thank you all the same.'","'Ah, what have we here? A ${CLASS}, is it? Perhaps you can help us settle this matter!\
\
'You see, my friend and I cannot come to an agreement. We have argued back and forth and then forth and back, and I will confess that in a heated moment, Tawaris here has even wagered good Gondorian gold if he should be proven wrong.\
\
'Come now, you'll hear us out, won't you?'","Return to Gradir and Tawaris","The soldiers can be found on the northern side of the Second Circle.\
\
You should return to Gradir and Tawaris and tell them what happened with the chicken.","Carry the chicken to the Ship's Prow"},
[952]={"'Well, ${PLAYER}, you are a good sort! I would share a drink with you, if I had aught worth drinking. \
\
'But alas! Tawaris here drank the last of our rotgut.'","'Do not listen to this scoundrel. First of all, it was he who drank the last of it. \
\
'But never mind that. Rotgut is not for the likes of you. Why, I have never met anyone but us fisherfolk of Ethir who could stomach it!'","Talk to Gradir","You manage to find the archer's shoulder and say something to him about his aim","The rotgut burns and roils within you, bringing tears to your eyes and making you stagger","The soldiers Gradir and Tawaris can be found on the northern side of the Second Circle.\
\
Hear what Tawaris has to say.","Collect dregs from ale (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You give Gradir and Tawaris a wave","Gradir and Tawaris can be found on the northern side of the Second Circle.\
\
You should return to Gradir with the rotgut ingredients.","'Well! The ${CLASS} can drink some rotgut and stay standing, perhaps. But one step and down you'll go.\
\
'Let us put you to the test. Walk over to that left archer, tap him on the shoulder, and tell him he's aiming well. Then, over on my right, walk between the last two ranks of men there. And last... last... why, climb up upon that barrel there and give us a wave!\
\
'Do all that, and I'll confess you can hold your rotgut after all.'","This is where Tawaris asked you to wave","'Ha ha! The ${CLASS} has done it, Tawaris, and this time the wager is mine. I'll have my gold back, thank you.\
\
'You are welcome back for a drink with us any time, ${PLAYER}. And do not worry, the rotgut will wear off soon and the headache that follows will be fleeting, though quite strong!'","Collected brazier ash (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Wave to Gradir and Tawaris","'Tawaris, you do grievous wrong to our ${CLASS} friend, a seasoned adventurer who could clearly stomach rotgut, even if most could not.\
\
'Why, I dare say we are in disagreement once again. Let us wager on it, and perhaps I can win my gold back. \
\
'${PLAYER}, find me what I need and I will make you some rotgut. If luck would have it, you can find all the ingredients on this very tier so I expect your trip to be swift. \
\
'First, I'll need dregs from ale, which you might find at the Splintered Shield. Then I need hot ash from a brazier and some Healer's Caustic, which is a powerful and pungent tincture used for closing wounds.'","Collect brazier ash (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gradir wants to share a drink of his rotgut with you. Unfortunately, he's all out.","Tap the left archer on the shoulder","You manage to brush against only a few shoulders as you stagger between the lined-up men","Collected Healer's Caustic","The soldiers can be found on the northern side of the Second Circle.\
\
You should return to Gradir and Tawaris so they can settle their bet.","Collect Healer's Caustic","Drink the rotgut","Walk between the last two ranks of men","Talk to Tawaris","You should drink the rotgut that Gradir prepared for you.","Gradir and Tawaris can be found on the northern side of the Second Circle.\
\
Hear what Tawaris has to say.","Standing after a drink of rotgut is not enough for Tawaris. He wants to see you tap the left-hand archer on the shoulder to compliment his aim, walk between the last two ranks of soldiers to his right, and then stand on the barrels and give a wave.","You should bring Gradir the items he needs to make rotgut: ale dregs from the Splintered Shield, hot brazier ash, and Healer's Caustic.\
\
All three ingredients can be found on the Second Circle: the dregs in the southern section, the brazier ash in the northern section, and Healer's Caustic at any healer's stall.","Collected dregs from ale (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'This will do the trick, ${PLAYER}! Now mind you, the ashes here are not quite what they are in Ethir, never mind the difference in the ale dregs, but it will have to do. Yes, it will have to do!\
\
'There, now it's made. Go on, have a taste!'","A Wager: Rot in the Gut","Return to Gradir","The soldiers Gradir and Tawaris can be found on the northern side of the Second Circle.\
\
Hear what Gradir has to say.","Climb on top of the barrel"},
[953]={"There are three guardposts throughout the Pristine Glade.\
\
Maugan has asked you to go and check at each guardpost for any signs of Saruman's forces.","'What? Saruman has attacked? The Elders must be told! This is ill news. Go back to the Elders. Tell them that I, myself, will attend the Assembly.\
\
'The Tree cannot be allowed to perish. I must reinforce the guards, then I will meet you in Lhan Rhos.\
\
'Go. Hurry!'","Talk to Guard Cai at the eastern guardpost","Talk to Guard Edrud at the southern guardpost","Maugan is preparing to defend the Pristine Glade against the onslaught of Saruman's forces.","'Secure the guardposts, ${PLAYER}, then return to me.'","A Walk in the Glade","Talk to Maugan at the Tree","Maugan awaits you at the Tree.\
\
You should return immediately to Maugan and let him know that Saruman is attacking the Glade.","Talk to Guard Ambras at the western guardpost","'The Elders wish to call Assembly? I cannot leave until I know that the Glade is safe. First, we need to make sure the borders are secure. \
\
'Saruman is constantly trying to discover what we have hidden here. We watch the edges of the Glade very carefully for any of his spies because if he finds out the true magic of this place, we fear that he will destroy the Tree. We found this craban and killed it but, I worry that it is one of the Wizard's.\
\
'Go to each guardpost and check with the guards there, then report back to me with your findings.'"},
[954]={"Encuentra a Bill, el poney","'Muchos de los Elfos de Echad Dúnann han visto un poney vagando por las colinas; parecía un lugar extraño para tal bestia, y es un milagro que haya sobrevivido con tanto peligro cerca.\
\
'Fui yo mismo en busca del poney, y cuando lo vi, inmediatamente reconocí al animal: era el poney que el hobbit, Samsagaz Gamyi, tenía estabulado en Imladris.\
\
'Tenía un aspecto salvaje y no llevaba ni bocado ni brida. El poney era bastante desconfiado, pero parecía estar en buena salud. La última vez que lo vi fue más allá de las colinas, al oeste de Echad Dúnann en Torech Andraug. Ve a ver si puedes despejar un camino para que el poney vuelva sano y salvo; la naturaleza salvaje no es un lugar para que una bestia así deambule por sí sola.'","'La última vez que vi al animal fue en Torech Andraug, al oeste de aquí.'","La última vez que se vio a Bill, el poney, fue en Torech Andraug, al oeste de Echad Dúnann.\
\
Glavroleth te ha pedido que encuentres a Bill, el poney, y despejes un camino hacia la seguridad.","Glavroleth vio al poney de Sam Gamyi, Bill, vagando cerca de Echad Dúnann.","Has encontrado nada menos que a Bill, el fiel corcel de Sam Gamyi.\
\
Parece que Bill está en un aprieto en esta zona infestada de huargos.","Un poney errante","Has encontrado a Bill, el poney"},
[955]={"'Never have I been a poet of war. If we found glory in naught more than gleaming armour and feats of battle, then the Enemy has won his first victory against us.\
\
'And so I wrought poetry of the grandeur of works or stone, of the beauty of blossom and branch, of the love of young men and maidens, fair and proud. When I put history to verse, it was of our works and journeys and failings.\
\
'But today - today is a day of war! It is close upon us as the breath in our lungs, and I would write a song of it. As you came upon me here, I was brooding on how to begin. I think I must fill my senses with things dark, dread, and bloody. Will you help me in this?'","Find trampled wheat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Heard the soldiers training","A War-like Word-hoard","Pillaged farmsteads and the enemy army can be found across the Pelennor, outside Minas Tirith.\
\
Dúrbethir asked that you find ruined farmsteads and gather charred wood and trampled wheat. He also asked that you hear for him the death-rattle of enemy soldiers and see the gleam in an enemy captain's eye in combat and defeat.","Found a sweaty rag","'If you would, go down among our soldiers in the Second Circle. Listen there to the sound of their training. Find for me a cold knife and a sweaty rag. \
\
'Then go out into the fields - as you are fit for such deeds - and explore our ruined farmsteads. Find for me some charred wood and trampled wheat. Then go in among our foes and hear the death-rattles of their dying soldiers. Observe for me the fell gleam in the eyes of one of their captains as he fights and falls. \
\
'Hm... yes. When you have done what I ask, return to me and I shall make a poem fit for war.'","Found a cold knife","Talk to Dúrbethir in the Fourth Circle and ask how you can help him compose a war poem.","Observe the gleam in the eyes of a captain","Dúrbethir takes the items you have brought him and listens with a grave expression to the impressions you gathered. \
\
'Perhaps I asked too much of you - but yet, it is no more than we ask of every soldier here. Nevertheless, you have brought me ample inspiration. Let me ponder a moment....\
\
'Dark the day and bright the fire \
The fires in the trenches' veins\
Veins go cold and life expires\
Expiring joy and dread and pain\
Dark the day and blood shall flow\
Dark the day and still we go\
\
'Blood shall flow and fear shall clamour\
Clamour like the soldiers' cries\
Cries of fury, hope, and valour\
Valour chance and death defies\
Dark the day and still we go\
Dark the day and blood shall flow\
\
'There, it is done. I have wrought a song for war. Perhaps we will take these words to our graves. If that is so, take my thanks as well.'","Find pieces of charred wood (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Hear the death-rattle of enemy soldiers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Dúrbethir","Find a cold knife","Soldiers can be found training and making ready in the Second Circle.\
\
Dúrbethir asked that you go among the soldiers and listen to them train, as well as retrieve a cold knife and a sweaty rag.","Return to Dúrbethir","'What, did you think I would write lines about sweaty rags and bent wheat? You know little of a poet's work, ${RACE}.'","The foe gasps as he falls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Return to Dúrbethir in the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith.","The captain's eyes were wild and fey as he fought and fell","Help the old poet Dúrbethir compose a war-poem for the coming days.","Find a sweaty rag","Found trampled wheat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Listen to the soldiers training","Found a piece of charred wood (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[956]={"Piel de Colmillo Rojo recogida","Filamentos espirales de araña recogidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lleva los objetos recolectados a Hrotha en Ost Guruth, en las Tierras Solitarias","'Tengo un montón de pieles esperando, ${PLAYER}. ¿Por qué estás aquí sin los objetos restantes?'","Sálvakh mora en Carn Dûm, en Angmar. Dushkâl, Brízrip y Thordragh pueden encontrarse en Urugarth, en Angmar.\
\
Hrotha necesita el tercer y último conjunto de objetos para completar su tarea.","El segundo mejor aliado de un Vigilante","'Estás haciéndome perder el tiempo, ${PLAYER}. No me molestes hasta que tengas lo que te pedí.'","'Una buena lanza puede ser la mejor aliada de un Vigilante, ${PLAYER}, pero ¿de qué te servirá cuando un arquero orco te llene de flechas? ¿O cuando un guerrero de Angmar te atraviese con su espada? Respóndeme eso, si puedes. Necesitarás un buen equipo si vas a enfrentarte a las mayores amenazas de este mundo.\
\
'Si quieres, te guiaré mientras reúnes los objetos necesarios para forjar un equipo digno de alguien como tú. Tráeme los componentes que necesito, ${PLAYER}, y veremos de fabricar objetos de virtud que te resulten de utilidad.\
\
'Los primeros objetos que necesitaré son pieles de los uros canosos que habitan en las Montañas Nubladas y la piel del jabalí Colmillo Rojo, que merodea las colinas de Eregion.'","Pieles de uro canoso recolectadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Ah, y ahora nuestro trabajo ha terminado, ${PLAYER}. Toma este equipo y que te proteja de lo peor que el Enemigo pueda enviarte. Que te sirva bien, ${PLAYER:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}.'","'Dos tandas de tres... el final de este trabajo ya se vislumbra, ${PLAYER}. Pero esta última parte será la más difícil.\
\
'Tráeme una Runa de Presencia Maligna del hechicero Sálvakh en Carn Dûm y los dientes de un Gorthorog... quizá de Dushkâl, Brízrip o Thordragh en Urugarth.'","Los barghests pueden encontrarse en Imlad Balchorth, en Angmar. Las arañas pueden encontrarse por toda Angmar.\
\
Hrotha necesita las colas de barghest y las hiladoras de araña para continuar.","Tan cerca de terminar, ${PLAYER}, y aun así pareces ${PLAYER:confundido[m]|confundida[f]}. ¡Encuentra el último conjunto de objetos!'","Recolecta pieles de uro canoso (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recoge los dientes del Gorthorog","Hrotha te ha ofrecido proporcionarte equipo hecho a mano.","Se dice que los uros canosos deambulan por las Montañas Nubladas. Colmillo Rojo merodea cerca de Torech Braignel, en el nordeste de Eregion.\
\
Hrotha requiere las pieles de uros canosos y la del gran jabalí conocido como Colmillo Rojo.","ecolecta la piel de Colmillo Rojo","'Bien, esto es un comienzo, ${PLAYER}. Curtiré y herviré estas pieles, y tú ve por los siguientes objetos mientras las coso.\
\
'Ahora necesito las colas barbadas de los barghests de Imlad Balchorth y las hiladoras de las arañas de Angmar.'","Recolecta colas barbadas de barghest (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Colas barbadas de barghest recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Dientes de Gorthorog recogidos","Recoge una Runa de Presencia Maligna","Recoge filamentos espirales de araña (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Runa de Presencia Maligna recogida"},
[957]={"El rastro termina en una escena espantosa. Quizá el cuerpo del ciervo tenga pistas sobre el paradero del Huargo.","Inspecciona el ciervo abatido y prepárate para luchar.","Derrota al Huargo en las Piedras Aullantes.","'¡Me alegra verte regresar ${PLAYERNAME:sano y victorioso[m]|sana y victoriosa[f]}! Con suerte, los lobos volverán a ser los de antes pronto, aunque podría llevar algo de tiempo. Hay algo malsano en el aire, y temo que nuestros problemas no hayan terminado del todo. Aun así, creo que la gente de Musgovilla puede respirar un poco más tranquila ahora, en gran parte gracias a tu heroísmo.'","Cledd te pidió derrotar al Huargo que ha pasado a comandar la manada de lobos cercana.","El Huargo no está aquí, pero encuentras algunas huellas de Huargo que seguir.","'Las Piedras Aullantes están al sureste de aquí. Vi al Huargo entre los lobos. Revisa cerca del tronco hueco del gran árbol. Si no está allí, quizá debas buscar más en lo profundo...'","'Mira allí. Las ruinas al este han sido desde hace mucho hogar de una manada de lobos. Siempre estuvieron conformes con dejarnos en paz, y nosotros más que felices de devolver el favor. Algo parece haber alterado ese pacto no dicho. Los lobos se han vuelto agresivos. Me atreví a acercarme a las ruinas y vi una gran bestia conocida como Huargo entre ellos.\
\
'No pensé que fuera real al principio. ¡Los Huargos son monstruos sobre los que contamos historias a los niños para hacerlos comportarse!\
\
'Tenemos las manos llenas reconstruyendo Musgovilla y recuperándonos del ataque. Carecemos de la fuerza para luchar contra esta bestia. Si mataras al Huargo, nos librarías tanto a nosotros como a los lobos de un conflicto innecesario.'","Las huellas continúan hacia el sur, hasta las Piedras Aullantes.","Hay un Huargo en las Piedras Aullantes.\
\
Encuentra y derrota al Huargo.","Has matado al Huargo de las Piedras Aullantes. Da la noticia a Cledd.","Un Huargo entre Lobos","Habla con Cledd","Sigue las huellas hacia el sur.","¡El Huargo emerge de las sombras para defender su comida!","Sigue al Huargo hacia lo profundo de las Piedras Aullantes.","Cledd puede encontrarse cerca de la puerta oriental de Musgovilla.\
\
Habla con Cledd"},
[958]={"'${PLAYER}, one of my men just reported seeing a rider of Walstow approaching in the distance.\
\
'He was being chased by Orcs and doubled back to fight them off. We have not seen a sign of the rider since.\
\
'Get down there as quickly as you are able, and see if you can find him outside town. Aid him if you can!'","The man suffered numerous blade wounds, but more curiously, harsh burns also mar his armour","You have come across the remains of a rider and his steed. You should examine his body and see if you cannot glean more information about what has occurred here.","'This bodes ill for Walstow, ${PLAYER}. It is likely they are under attack as we speak.\
\
'We can spare not the men to take the fight there, especially if the Orcs may turn on us so readily.\
\
'We must decide what to do, and with haste.'","Find the rider's trail","Talk to Cynelac","You see a felled horse and rider in the distance...","Fastred has reported that the rider was last seen along the road to the east.","Cynelac can be found outside the Mead Hall of Snowbourn.\
\
Having discovered a slain Rohirrim outside Snowbourn bearing the garb of Walstow, you have deduced that a great siege will soon befall the town.","Fastred has received word that a rider from Walstow was sighted outside the walls of Snowbourn, but was being pursued by Orcs and turned to engage in combat. If this rider can be found, his message might be of great importance.","A Warning from Walstow","Inspect the fallen Rohirrim rider"},
[961]={"Iris Tunelero se encuentra en Wistmead.\
\
Has reunido varias arañitas en Scary y ahora deberías regresar con Iris Tunelero.","'¡Hola, ${PLAYER}! ¿Podrías ayudarme con un asunto delicado?\
\
'El señor Valeoro se tomó mucho cuidado para envolver muchos de los arbustos en Wistmead con finas telarañas de algodón, pero creo que ha pasado por alto un detalle importante. ¡No hay arañas en Wistmead! O si las hubo... ¡ya se han ido!\
\
'¿Por qué no vas a Scary a buscar algunas arañitas y las pones en este frasco? Si las traes de vuelta aquí, podemos asegurarnos de que nadie más note este pequeño error!'","Has colocado arañitas en telarañas curiosamente vacías en Wistmead (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recoge arañitas en Scary (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Se pueden encontrar telarañas curiosamente vacías en los arbustos de todo Wistmead.\
\
Iris Tunelero te ha pedido que pongas las arañitas que encontraste en algunos de los arbustos enredados de Wistmead.","Walaric Valeoro ha hecho grandes esfuerzos para preparar Wistmead para el Festival de la Cosecha, pero ha pasado por alto algunos detalles que no han pasado desapercibidos para los festivales observadores.","Se pueden encontrar arañitas de los Campos Verdes en Scary y su cantera.\
\
Esperando hacer más convincentes los arbustos entoilados de algodón en Wistmead, Iris Tunnelier te ha pedido que recolectes arañitas en Scary.","Iris Tunelero se encuentra en Wistmead.\
\
Has llenado varios arbustos enredados con arañas. Ahora deberías regresar con Iris Tunelero.","Mete pequeñas arañas en telarañas curiosamente vacías en Wistmead (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Un desperdicio de telarañas","'¡Oh, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'¿Tuviste algún problema para meterlas en las telarañas? ¿No? ¡Maravilloso!\
\
'Por mi parte, creo que estas servirán por ahora. Si se escapan de nuevo, me aseguraré de encontrar una manera de reemplazarlas!'","Has recogido arañitas en Scary (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con Iris Tunelero","'¡Ah, perfecto!\
\
'Ahora... um... ¿Por qué no tomas este frasco de arañas y sacudes algunas de ellas sobre los arbustos enredados de Wistmead? ¡Preferiblemente los arbustos más alejados de mí!\
\
'¡Con suerte, nadie habrá notado siquiera que las arañas estaban desaparecidas!'"},
[962]={"A large force of Orcs has made camp in the Harlond before the wall","Merenir wishes to speak with you before you depart from Imloth Melui.","Talk to Merenir","Merenir stands by the entrance to Imloth Melui.\
\
Lady Vanyalos has asked you to talk to Merenir, who has one last favour to ask you before you depart Imloth Melui.","Dindal the scout can be found high up in a secluded look-out, which can be reached by turning north off the east road from Imloth Melui.\
\
Now that you have looked out to the north-east, you should talk to Dindal again.","Gaze north-east from the look-out","'Well met, ${CLASS}. Did I, by any chance, see you sparring with the guards back in Imloth Melui? No matter. If the ${RACE} I saw was you, you are no common hand in combat.\
\
'Are you as keen in sight as in combat? Look down there and tell me what you see.'","'I have one last favour to ask of you, ${PLAYER}. Or rather, Captain Merenir does. Believe me, he asks only out of our great need. We will hold you in great regard no matter your choice.'","Dindal the scout can be found high up in a secluded look-out, which can be reached by turning north off the east road from Imloth Melui.\
\
Dindal has asked you to stand by his side and look out to the north-east.","Dindal the scout can be found high up in a secluded look-out, which can be reached by turning north off the east road from Imloth Melui.\
\
Merenir has asked you to visit his scout, Dindal, at the look-out and assist in any way that you can.","You tell Dindal what you saw.\
\
'Your eyes are not poor. I have watched them for some time, and they are beyond count. All I can do is watch, but you are mighty and capable of much.\
\
'If you were to help us against these Orcs, what could you do? Hm....'","Find Dindal at the look-out","Talk to Dindal","A Watch on the Walls","'How relieved I am that all under my charge are safe within these walls, ${PLAYER}! Still, I must not take the arrival of these Orcs lightly. I have sent one of my best scouts, Dindal by name, up to a secluded look-out. It lies north off the road east of here. The unknowing eye would miss its rise up into the hillside of the mountain's feet.\
\
'There he will have a perfect view of the Harlond and the walls of Rammas Echor, on our northern border... for it is there, I fear, where the Orcs have crossed and entered Lossarnach. I would ask you to find him there and assist in whatever way you can.'"},
[963]={"'Antes de hacer nada más, debemos encontrar esa tribu de trasgos. Según Kambi, debería encontrarse tras el muro derruido que hay sobre las escaleras orientales.'","El campamento de los trasgos puede encontrarse a través de una grieta en el muro sobre las escaleras orientales.\
\
Túbi Puñogrueso te ha pedido que localices el campamento de los trasgos.","'Según Kambi, el jefe dijo que debíamos pasar por el muro derruido que hay sobre las escaleras orientales. Debemos comprobar si esta tribu de trasgos realmente acecha en las sombras. También quiero saber más sobre esa voz a la que el jefe tanto temía.\
\
'Dirígete hacia el este a través de la grieta y localiza a la tribu.'","Jarmárr se encuentra cerca del campamento de trasgos de Snaga-maudhûl.\
\
Has localizado a la tribu de trasgos y has oído la voz de la que hablaba el jefe. Deberías hablar con el enano junto al camino.","Kambi, herido por un trasgo cerca del Umbral de Durin, habló de los desvaríos de su atacante. Túbi Puñogrueso quiere que el campamento de esta tribu sea localizado cuanto antes.","'¡Por la barba de Durin! ¡Alguien ha venido a ayudarme! Me separé del resto de mi grupo al avanzar por esta zona y acabé aquí....'","Una mirada atenta","Habla con el enano cerca del campamento de trasgos de Snaga-maudhûl","Has descubierto el campamento de los trasgos. Una voz profunda y áspera ladra órdenes secas.","Encuentra a la tribu de trasgos"},
[964]={"'It is a bright day for Gondor, ${PLAYER}, even in such a place of darkness.\
\
'It had come to the mind of King Elessar that Minas Morgul might need to be razed to its lowest stones. Knowing what I do of the terror that still lingers upon Ithilien, even if Gothmog were defeated, I could not see another way. Yet, the words of Galadriel have kindled in my heart a desire to preserve what was lost so long ago.\
\
'When at last we triumph over Gothmog, I shall plead to King Elessar to spare the Dead City that it might be restored by the hand of Gondor. Its stones shall be reshaped, its halls rebuilt, its archives written anew... and it shall again be Minas Ithil.\
\
'Whether you knew of Éowyn's deception, I will not ask. I must admit, I had begun to suspect it myself not long after we entered the Circle of Death. Lady Éowyn is a hale warrior, finer than many Men of Gondor, and she need not answer for decisions made out of loyalty... or love.'","After the wards surrounding Barad Cúron were destroyed, the fell magic sealing Uialrond, the Dome of Evening has been undone.","'Let us see what lies hidden in Uialrond, ${PLAYER}.'","'It seems whatever magic held shut the doors to Uialrond has been undone, but within... all I see is darkness.\
\
'You and...'\
\
Faramir looks around the company.\
\
'...Dolenthol may accompany me within. I do not know what we shall find, but keep your wits about you.\
\
'When you are prepared, I shall lead us inside.'","Talk to Éowyn","'We are fortunate to have an ally like you, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Faramir's heart is lightened, and the end of this strife no longer seems so distant. Many dark days still lay ahead of us, but we shall overcome all the evils that remain in this place.\
\
'You have done much for me... and for Faramir. That we have come to the end of things together is all I can ask.'","Faramir can be found outside Uialrond, the Dome of Evening.\
\
Faramir is prepared to enter Uialrond and confront whatever evils lurk within. You should talk to Faramir when you are ready.","A Waxing Moon","Talk to Faramir","Faramir and Éowyn can be found outside Uialrond, the Dome of Evening in the Circle of Death.\
\
You have discovered a beacon of hope within Minas Morgul and heartened the Rangers of Ithilien. You should talk to Faramir and Éowyn."},
[965]={"Talk to Captain Thandor","A Way Home","'Lady Celebros' lockbox? She did not tell you what this was for, did she? Then I suppose I shall find the answer here...'\
\
As Captain Thandor reads the orders, he raises an eyebrow.\
\
'Well... I was not expecting her to part with her heirloom just to fund this endeavour... but it is a noble cause, and I am glad to see it.\
\
'I shall take things from here. Thank you, ${PLAYER}.'","Though there is no ship to take the Corsairs home, hope is not lost.","You still have papers to deliver to Nasar and his companions.\
\
You should return to them near the West Pelargir gates.","'Lady Celebros agreed to meet with us? And these papers with the seal of Sirgon -- now we may wander freely about the city. Despite every grudge she could hold against us... I can hardly believe it. We've found our way home.'\
\
The soft smile on Nasar's face slowly transforms into a grin.\
\
'No doubt the shipwrights of Pelargir have things to teach us, but I assure you, they shall not be the only ones teaching!'","'Unfortunately, the war consumed most of our seafaring resources. We cannot spare a ship for your friends to return home. Do not fret; I may have a solution. If I can provide the materials and funds necessary, the Corsairs could work with our shipwrights to repair a damaged ship rather than build a new one entirely... and I daresay both groups could learn new things from each other.\
\
'Please, wait right here. I must retrieve something.'\
\
Celebros disappears into the manor. A while later, she returns with what looks like a collection of papers and a sturdy lockbox.\
\
'Would you deliver these orders and the lockbox to Captain Thandor? He stands watch near the East Pelargir gates.\
\
'And once that is done, please give your friends these papers, and let them know they are most welcome here. I would be happy to discuss the matter with them further.'","Celebros has asked you to bring some sealed orders and a lockbox to Captain Thandor.\
\
He stands watch near the East Pelargir gates.","Talk to Nasar"},
[966]={"Talk to Mekhnet","Defeat Orc-sentries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","A recently-arrived Mekhnet wishes to speak with you.","A Way In","Eyes are set on the goblin Thraunákh in Atrad-zarakh, but the Orc camp of Târ-kútoz remains an obstacle.","'I am putting my foot down -- Lúka needs her rest! I know you can handle yourself, maybe even better alone than accompanied by a sleep-deprived dwarf.\
\
'Quickly, let me distract her. Head to Târ-kútoz, defeat their sentries, and come straight back. I wouldn't want you entering that watch-tower without help!'","Talk to Lúka","Orc-sentries can be found in Târ-kútoz.\
\
You should defeat them to ensure easier access to Atrad-zarakh later.","You have defeated as many Orc-sentries as you could find.\
\
You should report back to Lúka in Ashmargathâl.","'I should have known better than to trust Mekhnet the moment you disappeared. But what's done is done -- getting into Atrad-zarakh will be safer now. '","'The goblin Thraunákh must be in Târ-kútoz, holed up with all the bats he needs to create his sapper-bombs. We won't find him outside; I doubt the bats would willingly suffer the elements. Which means... they've made the watch-tower Atrad-zarakh their new home.\
\
'If we are to stop Thraunákh, we must first clear out a path through Târ-kútoz. We ought to target the Orc-sentries -- they are the eyes and ears of the camp.\
\
'I'll come with you. I have no desire to see another dwarf get hurt --\
\
'Ah, wait a moment. It seems that Mekhnet has something to say to you.'","Orc-sentries defeated (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[967]={"Defeat Hafoc","'I have no doubt that we have been betrayed by Hafoc, my predecessor.'","'${PLAYER}, these brigands are too organized to be simple ruffians...or at least the one that leads them is not. Their tactics are all too familiar. I believe their captain may, in fact, be a wayward member of my very own border-guard.\
\
'Hafoc, the captain of Etheburg before me, went missing several months ago...I was but a convenient replacement for him. Hafoc seemed to welcome this assignment, and he was one of the few that had come here at Wormtongue's orders not out of discipline.\
\
'I wonder now if Hafoc has betrayed his people and joined these brigands? Would you go to Helstor and confront this captain? I expect he would be somewhere near their relic-stores.'","'This is welcome news, ${PLAYER}! With Hafoc out of the way, the brigands will be far less of a threat, and we may focus our attention upon the Khundolar.'","Defeated Hafoc","Because of their organized efforts, Céola suspects that the captain of the brigands is, in fact, a wayward member of the border-guard.","Talk to Céola at Etheburg in the Brown Lands","A Wayward Captain","The brigand captain can be found somewhere within Helstor, north of Etheburg in the Brown Lands.\
\
Céola has asked you to confront the leader of the brigands in the Brown Lands.","Céola is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands, south of Helstor.\
\
You should return to Céola with news of your victory."},
[969]={"Recolecta restos venerados de tumulario (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Hrotha forjará para ti un arma de poder y gloria, si le llevas los componentes adecuados.","Lleva los objetos recolectados a Hrotha en Ost Guruth, en las Tierras Solitarias","Recolecta la lanza de Bryok","Peto de invasor recolectado (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recoge un palo de cuentas ensangrentado","'No veo los objetos que te pedí, ${PLAYER}.'","Uñas incrustadas de gemas reunidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recolectados restos venerados de tumulario (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lanza de Bryok recogida","Recolecta petos de invasor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿Has regresado? Tienes una gran determinación, ${PLAYER}. Mucha gente habría dudado... pero eso es lo que nos distingue, ¿no es así?\
\
'Muy bien. Solo un conjunto más de objetos, y la lanza será tuya. Tráeme un palo de cuentas manchado de sangre de los orcos Gríshakrum, Kughûrz y Dafrim en Urugarth, y el cuerno carmesí del Gorthorog Barashal, que mora en Carn Dûm.'","Los tumularios pueden encontrarse en Angmar, Forochel, Annúminas y Helegrod. Los rascacuevas pueden encontrarse en Angmar y Sarnúr, en Ered Luin.\
\
Hrotha requiere los restos de tumulario y las garras de un número equivalente de rascacuevas de Gorothlad.","'Esta lanza no servirá de mucho a menos que me traigas lo que te pedí, ${PLAYER}.'","Gríshakrum, Kughûrz y Dafrim pueden encontrarse en Urugarth. Barashal mora en Carn Dûm.\
\
Hrotha necesita un palo de cuentas de los orcos Ongbúrz y el cuerno de Barashal el Gorthorog.","'Entonces, la lanza... tus armas están bien para un guerrero vagabundo, pero los Vigilantes merecemos las mejores lanzas, ¿no es así, ${PLAYER}? Sí, creo que sí. ¡De lo contrario, podríamos ser como chusma dunledina pinchando cosas con palos afilados!\
\
'Hagamos una para ti, ¿te parece? Sí, una lanza digna de alguien de tu reputación. ¡Entonces los juglares podrán cantar sobre ella tanto como sobre ti!\
\
'Claro que eso significa trabajo para ti. No puedo hacerlo todo yo solo, y tampoco debería. Tráeme los petos de los angmarim que infestan Annúminas y la lanza de Bryok el Gauradan en Forochel. Vamos, ${PLAYER}... ¡El Enemigo no va a esperar mientras te demoras!'","'¡Eso es! Mucho trabajo para un solo arma, pero todas las grandes armas de leyenda requirieron sudor y sangre antes de estar listas.\
\
'Aquí tienes tu lanza, como te prometí. Ahora es tuya, úsala bien. Supongo que no estará verdaderamente terminada hasta que no se haya bañado en sangre de orco, ¿no es así, ${PLAYER}?'","Cuerno carmesí de Gorthorog recogido","Palo de cuentas ensangrentado recogido","¡Ah! Esto es bueno. Esta lanza hará mucho más bien en tus manos que en las de Bryok, de eso no hay duda.\
\
'Entonces, me pondré a trabajar. No tiene sentido demorarse, ¿verdad, ${PLAYER}? Ve a buscar los siguientes objetos y tráemelos cuando los tengas.\
\
'Ahora necesito restos de los tumularios que deambulan por Angmar, Forochel, Annúminas o Helegrod, y las garras incrustadas de gemas de los rascacuevas de Angmar y Sarnúr.'","Los angmarim pueden encontrarse en Annúminas, en Evendim. Bryok vive en Forochel.\
\
Hrotha desea que le traigas los petos de los invasores angmarim en Annúminas y la lanza de Bryok el Gauradan.","Reúne uñas incrustadas de gemas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡${PLAYER}! ¿Qué haces aquí sin esos últimos objetos?'","Recoge un cuerno carmesí de Gorthorog","Un arma de poder y gloria"},
[970]={"You have repaired Penlhun's axe","A Weapon of Old","Bring Penlhun's axe to the mad dwarf in Thrór's Coomb","Talk to Aedh at the Lhanuch crafting hall","Penlhun Brehur, one of the leaders of Nan Laeglin, has asked you if you know of any way to repair the dwarf-axe handed down to him from his father. The axe was forged in Thrór's Coomb, and it is rumoured that at least one dwarf remains among the ruins. Alternatively, if you are a weaponsmith of considerable skill you might try a hand at repairing it yourself.","'Would that my father's axe were whole once more....'","'Penlhun gave you this? I will tell you what I told him. I cannot repair it.\
\
'I do not know how Thrór's smiths forged it to such a temper, but anything I could do to it would make the steel so brittle that it would shatter at the first blow.\
\
'You want this weapon repaired? Go to Thrór's Coomb. There is rumour that a mad dwarf lives there still among the ruins. Perhaps he can repair it.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>If you have Master proficiency in the Weaponsmith profession, you may repair the axe yourself using the anvil in the Lhanuch crafting hall.</rgb>","'Talk to the mad dwarf if you want that axe repaired!'","Penlhun Brehur is at the Brenin's Hall in Lhanuch, far to the west of Thrór's Coomb.\
\
You should return to Penlhun with his father's axe.","Repair Penlhun's axe","'This is a dwarf-axe! Whence did you steal it? From a Man?\
\
'Where did the Man get it? From his father? This man's father was a dwarf? Well, you should have said so to begin with! I will gladly repair this for my half-brother!\
\
'This shouldn't take long... here you go!'","'Tell me, Duvodiad, is it true that the powers of Angmar stir anew? Have the Elves truly allied with the Witch-king in the North as the tales say? Some weeks ago, warriors from the South under the direction of Isengard passed by to do battle in Eregion, but we have heard little but dark rumour since.\
\
'No matter the details, war shall be upon us soon... you mark my words. Would that my father's axe was yet true, I would be unafraid of battle! It was made by the dwarves back when Thrór's folk lived in the mountains, but time takes its toll on all things, and it broke some years ago. None here have the skill to reforge such a weapon, but it is said that the dwarves yet remain in the far north and have shared some secrets of craft with the Men there as well.\
\
'I was thinking that if this is true, then I might have the axe re-made. What of it, Duvodiad? Do you know the secrets of the craft or perhaps know a dwarf who might reforge my father's blade? Take it, if so. It is of no use to me now, and my brethren would have me melt it down to make a less worthy blade. I would not see it end so if it might be made whole again. If it can be done, then I shall be in your debt and shall speak in your favour at the Council of Brehur.'","'My father's axe! It is nearly as sound as the day he brought it from the dwarves!\
\
'You have my thanks, Duvodiad. I shall do what I can to dissuade Glynn Brenin from aiding Isengard.\
\
'We of the Uch-lûth should be our own people, not servants of some power-hungry wizard....'","'Tell Penlhun's father Nár sends his greetings... a good dwarf, he is. Or was? He is a dwarf, yes?'","The mad dwarf dwells somewhere in the mountains surrounding Thrór's Coomb, far to the east of Lhanuch.\
\
Aedh told you to seek out a mad dwarf in the valley of Thrór's Coomb and see if he can repair Penlhun's axe. Alternatively, if you are a master weaponsmith, you might attempt to repair the axe yourself at the forge in Lhanuch.","Bring the axe to Penlhun","Aedh may be found in the crafting hall.\
\
You should speak with Aedh to learn if there is any way to reforge Penlhun's axe."},
[971]={"'Tus estudios continúan a buen ritmo, . Las criaturas de la naturaleza te ven como ${PLAYERNAME:un amigo y aliado[m]|una amiga y aliada[f]}, y los misterios del pasado yacen sin explorar ante ti. Siempre hay más por aprender, pero posees una comprensión de esta Tierra Media que pocos pueden alcanzar.\
\
'Uno de los Sabios más grandes de nuestros días fue un hombre llamado Benton Roblealto. Mantenía un vasto almacén de conocimiento — antiguos tomos y pergaminos, pequeños objetos de herencia inusual. Se dice que Benton tuvo un final triste, pero le sobrevive su hijo Dorset. Dorset también es un Sabio, y sin duda aprendió mucho de su padre antes de que Benton encontrara su destino.\
\
'Un gran árbol crece al sureste de la aldea de Entibo, conocido por sus hojas doradas que conserva durante todo el año, y Dorset Roblealto suele demorarse allí en contemplación. Búscalo, y quizás te revele algunos de los misterios de su padre.'","'Te agradezco, ${PLAYERNAME:Sabio[m]|Sabia[f]} , y más aún, pues compartiré contigo las enseñanzas que se encuentran entre las cubiertas del libro que recuperamos.\
\
'Tal es el camino de la sabiduría, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}. ¡Es mejor cuando se comparte!'","'Te agradezco nuevamente, ${PLAYER}. La biblioteca de mi padre es un lugar confuso.'","'Normalmente podés encontrar a Dorset Roblealto en contemplación cerca del Árbol Amarillo, al sureste de la aldea de Entibo. Entibo está bastante cerca de la ciudad de Bree en las Tierras de Bree'","Dorset Roblealto está en el Árbol Amarillo, al sureste de la aldea de Entibo.\
\
Dorset Roblealto te ha pedido ayuda para localizar el libro \\q Sobre la Resistencia de los Animales en la Naturaleza\\q , y te ha dicho que hables con él cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]}. Mencionó que las tres páginas del catálogo de su padre facilitarían mucho encontrar el libro.","'Tus estudios continúan a buen ritmo, . Las criaturas de la naturaleza te ven como ${PLAYERNAME:un amigo y aliado[m]|una amiga y aliada[f]}, y los misterios del pasado yacen sin explorar ante ti. Siempre hay más por aprender, pero posees una comprensión de esta Tierra Media que pocos pueden alcanzar.\
\
'Uno de los Sabios más grandes de nuestros días fue un hombre llamado Benton Roblealto. Mantenía un vasto almacén de conocimiento — antiguos tomos y pergaminos, pequeños objetos de herencia inusual. Se dice que Benton tuvo un final triste, pero le sobrevive su hijo Dorset. Dorset también es un Sabio, y sin duda aprendió mucho de su padre antes de que Benton encontrara su destino.\
\
'Un gran árbol crece al sureste de la aldea de Entibo, en las Tierras de Bree, conocido por sus hojas doradas que conserva durante todo el año, y Dorset Roblealto suele demorarse allí en contemplación. Búscalo, y quizás te revele algunos de los misterios de su padre.'","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para viajar conmigo a la cueva que contiene la biblioteca de mi padre? Solo te pido que mantengas su ubicación en secreto.\
\
'Espero que no pienses que estoy siendo demasiado directo, pero... ¿has localizado alguna página del catálogo de mi padre? Podemos buscar sin ayuda, pero quizás tú logres descubrir en qué estante se encuentra \\qSobre la Resistencia de los Animales en la Naturaleza\\q, donde yo he fallado. Sin duda, algún trasgo, bandido o buscador de tesoros de las Tierras de Bree ya ha encontrado las páginas y se las ha llevado.\
\
'Si te sientes seguridad de saber en qué estante está el libro, ¡yo también estoy listo para viajar!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta es una misión en solitario, y no puede completarse con una Comunidad.</rgb>","'Bienvenido, . Los rumores sobre la sabiduría de mi padre han traído a muchos Sabios como tú a escuchar mis palabras, y temo que a veces se marchan decepcionados. No tengo el conocimiento que tenía mi padre; de hecho, su forma de pensar era tan distinta de la mía que no puedo comprender ni siquiera lo que él consideraba más simple.\
\
'Considera la organización de su biblioteca. Encontró una cueva adecuada en las colinas rocosas de las Tierras de Bree y la tomó como su biblioteca privada, llenándola con libros y pergaminos recolectados a lo largo de su larga vida. Pero cada vez que intento encontrar uno de los libros de los que me hablaba, estoy completamente perdido. Me confió un catálogo que detallaba qué libros podían encontrarse en qué estantes, pero el sistema simplemente no tenía sentido para mí, y fui descuidado con las páginas. ¡Ahora solo me queda la última! Sin duda, los bandidos y trasgos ya han encontrado las otras. Sin el catálogo completo, ¿cómo voy a encontrar \\qSobre la Resistencia de los Animales en la Naturaleza\\q? Mi padre me aseguró antes de morir que estaba en un estante de su biblioteca.\
\
'Compartiré contigo la sabiduría contenida entre sus cubiertas si me ayudas a encontrar este libro, . La biblioteca es grande, y podemos buscar sin ayuda si lo deseas, pero sin duda sería más fácil con cada página del catálogo. No sé dónde pueden estar, pero buscarlas hará que encontrar el libro sea más sencillo. Necesitaremos apurarnos, pues los trasgos han estado excavando peligrosamente cerca y pronto romperán el acceso a la biblioteca. Habla conmigo cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para partir, aquí está la única página del catálogo que aún conservo.'","Catálogo de Benton Recogido, Página Tres","Lleva el libro que buscaba a Dorset Roblealto","'Normalmente podés encontrar a Dorset Roblealto en contemplación cerca del Árbol Amarillo, al sureste de la aldea de Entibo. Entibo está bastante cerca de la ciudad de Bree.'","'Bueno, ¿dónde está el libro? ¡No lo habrás perdido, verdad?'","Mente Bien Ordenada","Dorset Roblealto suele estar profundamente en contemplación junto al Árbol Amarillo, al sureste de la aldea de Entibo, en las Tierras de Bree.\
\
Te han dicho que hables con Dorset Roblealto con la esperanza de que el Sabio pueda instruirte.","'Normalmente podés encontrar a Dorset Roblealto en contemplación cerca del Árbol Amarillo, al sureste de la aldea de Entibo, en las Tierras de Bree. No muy lejos del pueblo.","Ayuda a Dorset Roblealto a localizar el libro que busca","Habla con Dorset Roblealto","'Normalmente podés encontrar a Dorset Roblealto en contemplación cerca del Árbol Amarillo, al sureste de la aldea de Entibo. No muy lejos del pueblo.'","'Las habilidades organizativas de mi padre quizás necesitaban algo de trabajo, siendo sincero.'","Hay muchos secretos por descubrir en las historias de los Pueblos Libres, esperando solo el estudio cuidadoso de un Sabio con habilidad y paciencia.","'Tus estudios continúan a buen ritmo, . Las criaturas de la naturaleza te ven como ${PLAYERNAME:un amigo y aliado[m]|una amiga y aliada[f]}, y los misterios del pasado yacen sin explorar ante ti. Siempre hay más por aprender, pero posees una comprensión de esta Tierra Media que pocos pueden alcanzar.\
\
'Uno de los Sabios más grandes de nuestros días fue un hombre llamado Benton Roblealto. Mantenía un vasto almacén de conocimiento — antiguos tomos y pergaminos, pequeños objetos de herencia inusual. Se dice que Benton tuvo un final triste, pero le sobrevive su hijo Dorset. Dorset también es un Sabio, y sin duda aprendió mucho de su padre antes de que Benton encontrara su destino.\
\
'Un gran árbol crece al sureste de la aldea de Entibo, conocido por sus hojas doradas que conserva durante todo el año, y Dorset Roblealto suele demorarse allí en contemplación. Búscalo, en las Tierras de Bree, y quizás te revele algunos de los misterios de su padre.'","Dorset Roblealto suele estar profundamente en contemplación junto al Árbol Amarillo, al sureste de la aldea de Entibo, en las Tierras de Bree.\
\
Dorset está esperando para hablar contigo tras tu exitosa recuperación del libro que buscaba."},
[972]={"Puedes encontrar constructores y guardias enanos en los alrededores de la Sala Vigesimoprimera.\
\
Deberías llevar cerveza a los constructores y guardias en nombre del capataz Mögr, que cree que Zelem-melek pertenece ya a los enanos.","Has recogido un barril de cerveza","El capataz Mögr se encuentra en la Sala Vigesimoprimera de Moria.\
\
Deberías hablar con Mögr.","'¿El capataz Mögr nos envía cerveza? ¡Qué considerado! Si él confía en que la sala es segura, yo también. ¡Sírveme una, ${CLASS}!'","Lleva cerveza a Reinn","Puedes encontrar cerveza cerca del capataz Mögr en la Sala Vigesimoprimera.\
\
Deberías recoger algo de cerveza y llevarla a los trabajadores y guardias para que puedan celebrar su victoria.","Una celebración bien merecida","Reinn se encuentra en la Sala Vigesimoprimera de Moria, no lejos de Mögr.\
\
Deberías llevar cerveza a Reinn.","Recoge un barril de cerveza","Lleva cerveza a guardias y constructores (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Regresa con Mögr","Cerveza entregada (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Reinn no cree que los enanos de la Sala Vigesimoprimera deban bajar la guardia","'Hm, bueno. Estaba a punto de ponerme a reparar los andamios, pero supongo que puede esperar, ¿no?\
\
'Sírveme un vaso de esa cerveza, amigo.'","'¡Bah! ¡Bah! Reinn es listo, eso es cierto, pero siempre lo arruina todo con su exceso de cautela.'","'¿Cerveza del capataz Mögr? ¿Ahora?\
\
'¿De verdad es tan seguro que puedo beber durante la guardia? Bueno, supongo que si el capataz lo cree, no habrá problema.'","Mögr, el capataz del próspero enclave de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, cree que la posición de los enanos es tan segura que ha llegado el momento de bajar la guardia y celebrarlo.","'No necesito estar especialmente alerta para este puesto tan sencillo. ¡La guardia en esta sala no es nada: no hay ni un enemigo a la vista!'","'¡Bienvenido, bienvenido! ¿Acaso no es la Sala Vigesimoprimera el lugar más grandioso de todo Khazad-dûm?\
\
'No hemos encontrado peligro alguno aquí, y lo tomo como señal de que los enanos han conquistado Zelem-melek. Hemos establecido una gran posición y llegas justo a tiempo para la celebración.\
\
'Si fueras tan amable, distribuye cerveza entre los valientes enanos que han trabajado tan duro aquí. ¡Se la han ganado!'","'¡Ya estamos celebrando! Es una gran noticia. No sabía que hubiéramos avanzado tanto aquí, pero lo tomaré como señal de éxito. Gracias, ${PLAYER}, y transmite también mi agradecimiento al capataz.'","'¿Cerveza de Mögr mientras estoy con reparaciones? Bueno, supongo que no hará daño. ¿Qué prisa hay?'","'Por la barba de Durin, ¿qué está haciendo el capataz Mögr? No quiero cerveza, gracias. Debo mantenerme alerta.\
\
'¿Ese insensato ya está bajando la guardia? Es cierto que no ha habido intrusiones y que progresamos bien, pero no creo que Zelem-melek sea seguro todavía.'"},
[973]={"'Me canso ya de las constantes preocupaciones de Reinn. Sus quejas abiertas son malas para nuestro trabajo aquí, ya lo sabes.\
\
'¿Qué te parece esto? Eres nuevo aquí y no tienes prejuicios. ¿Por qué no patrullas esta amplia sala? Si está libre de enemigos, Reinn deberá dejar a un lado sus temores.\
\
'Creo que es un compromiso justo. Si tengo razón, mis enanos podrán celebrar la victoria sin vacilar.'","No hay enemigos a la vista, pero algo llama tu atención","Regresa con Mögr con tus hallazgos","Habla con Reinn","El capataz Mögr, frustrado por la obstinación de Reinn respecto a la seguridad de Zelem-melek, quiere demostrarte que la Sala Vigesimoprimera es tan segura como puede ser.","Una sala amplia y vacía","Reinn se encuentra en la Sala Vigesimoprimera.\
\
Deberías escuchar lo que Reinn opina sobre tus hallazgos.","Mögr descarta los posibles peligros y problemas que has observado","Patrulla la zona este de la sala","Mögr se encuentra en la Sala Vigesimoprimera de Moria.\
\
Deberías volver con Mögr con un informe de lo que has visto durante tu patrulla.","Patrulla la zona oeste de la sala","Informas a Mögr de que los caminos están despejados, pero también de los problemas evidentes que has observado en la Sala Vigesimoprimera.\
\
'¡No hay enemigos, tal como dije! ¿Lo ves, Reinn? Es hora de abandonar tu cruzada contra que nuestra gente celebre la victoria al reclamar Zelem-melek para la expedición!'","Patrulla la zona sur de la sala","'¿Estás ciego, Mögr? ${PLAYER} también informó de muchos otros problemas: soportes derrumbándose, suciedad por todas partes y pruebas de que orcos o trasgos han pasado por aquí no hace mucho.'","La Sala Vigesimoprimera es una enorme sala columnada que se extiende por el norte de Zelem-melek.\
\
Deberías patrullar la sala y comprobar si hay enemigos."},
[975]={"You have discovered a servant from the household of Thornhope hiding in the ruins","While searching the ruins of Thornhope for survivors, you find a clever servant who managed to avoid the Orcs.\
\
You should help the servant to safety.","Máthild is at Béortnoth's camp, outside of Thornhope.\
\
You should speak with Máthild when you return to Béortnoth's camp.","Talk to Máthild","Talk to Máthild at Béortnoth's camp.","A Wily Servant","'Well now, it has taken you long enough! Now that you have caused a stir with the Orcs, I can find my way out of this burnt husk of a town.'","'I must thank you again, ${PLAYER}. It is sad, really... Thane Béortnoth was always kind to me; now he is all but mad. Perhaps there is a way to bring sense back to him....'","Máthild is hiding near the Mead Hall of Thornhope.\
\
You escort Máthild to safety.","While searching the ruins of Thornhope for survivors, you find a clever servant who managed to avoid the Orcs."},
[976]={"'¡Vaya! ¿Has estado ahí mucho tiempo?\
\
'Me llamo Iris Tunelero, y te doy la bienvenida a Wistmead. Soy bastante nueva aquí, pero he hecho un buen trabajo ayudando al Sr. Valeoro y a los demás a preparar el campo para el Festival de la Cosecha.\
\
'¿Cómo llegué aquí, preguntas? Oh, no preguntaste? Bueno, fue lo más extraño que me ha pasado.\
\
'Estaba saliendo de Staddle cuando una mujer con capa de Bree se me acercó. No conocía su rostro y no me dio su nombre, pero me rogó que le trajera cualquier gato perdido que vagara por el terreno del festival. ¿Cómo podría saber algo así? Pero no pasó ni una hora después de mi llegada a Wistmead cuando encontré estos gatos vagando por el laberinto de trigo. \
\
'¿No son adorables? Bueno, ¡no te dejes engañar! ¡Son un dolor de cabeza!\
\
'Entre tú y yo, creo que el Sr. Dignedor podría llenar ese viejo y apestoso pantano, pero nunca he estado tan emocionada por el Festival de la Cosecha.\
\
'¡Quizás puedas ayudarnos a hacer Wistmead aún mejor!'","Habla con Iris Tunelero","Walaric Valeoro se encuentra en Wistmead.\
\
Has explorado Wistmead y te has familiarizado con los otros miembros de su equipo. Deberías regresar con Walaric Valeoro antes de unirte a las festividades en Wistmead.","'¡Muy bien!\
\
'Espero que disfrutes de Wistmead tanto como nosotros disfrutamos construyéndolo, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'En nombre de todos nosotros, ¡bienvenido!'","Ermentrude Henoloma, Halinard Bonce e Iris Tunelero se encuentran en Wistmead.\
\
Walaric Valeoro te ha pedido que explores Wistmead y te familiarices con los otros organizadores del festival. Deberías echar un vistazo.","'¡Hola! ¿Es tu primera vez en Wistmead?\
\
'¡Bienvenido, bienvenido! Soy Halinard Bunce, y me encargo de algunas de las festividades aquí en Wistmead. ¡Tengo una mano hábil para tallar calabazas y me dedico a elaborar cervezas interesantes!\
\
'Por supuesto, no soy lo suficientemente hábil como para unirme a las filas de la Liga de las Posadas, pero espero que el Festival de la Cosecha me brinde la oportunidad de demostrar mi valía. Lamentablemente, mi cerveza Fognoggin parece ser más 'interesante' que bien valorada, pero he trabajado arduamente para mejorar su receta. ¡Eres bienvenido a probarla mientras exploras los espeluznantes sonidos y vistas de Wistmead!\
\
'He oído decir que el Roble Nostálgico tiene mente propia, pero es solo un viejo árbol... ¿verdad? ¡Quizás deberías ir a verlo por ti mismo!\
\
'Pero basta de hablar de mí... ¡hay mucha diversión que tener aquí en Wistmead! ¡Te dejo con eso!'","'Es impresionante, ¿no es así? La mayoría de los laberintos no son espeluznantes, ¡pero el laberinto de Wistmead ciertamente lo es!\
\
'Se rumorea que el trigo se mueve durante la noche, remodelado por una guadaña invisible. Los hobbits descuidados podrían perderse en sus sinuosos caminos, y una vez que eso sucede, rara vez se les vuelve a ver....'\
\
Ermentrude hace una pausa demasiado larga.\
\
'Hasta que yo vaya a encontrarlos, por supuesto. ¡Si quieres probar el laberinto, estaré aquí!'","'¡Hola! Parece que la noticia sobre Wistmead ha comenzado a difundirse.\
\
'El Festival de la Cosecha ha sido durante mucho tiempo mi favorito de todos los festivales de la Comarca, y después de ver la broma que el viejo Sr. Bolsón le hizo a Lobelia, me inspiré para crear algo propio. ¡Y aquí está!'\
\
Visiblemente orgulloso de su trabajo, Walaric gesticula en todas direcciones.\
\
'Para mi deleite, Ermentrude Haybank, Halinard Bonce e Iris Tunelero han ideado una serie de nuevos juegos y actividades para el Festival de la Cosecha.\
\
'¡Si los encuentras vagando por el campo, asegúrate de presentarte!'","Habla con Walaric Valeoro","Habla con Halinard Bonce","Habla con Ermentrude Henoloma","Wistmead encarna el espíritu del Festival de la Cosecha.","Una caminata ventosa por Wistmead"},
[977]={"'Spiders can be found everywhere you look, ${PLAYER}. If you have trouble finding them in the woods, you could investigate around the Dreadweaver's Lair, south-west from here.'","'You have been sent to aid us and aid us you may, mellon. There are many tasks ahead of us, and our numbers are fewer than we would wish, especially with our scouts missing in the north.\
\
'This forest is rife with poison-fanged spiders, seemingly everywhere one looks. They spout from the Dreadweaver's Lair, south-west from here.\
\
'You should defeat as many Mirkwood spiders as you can, mellon. They are ever a threat to the Elves, and are our enemies of old.'","A Wood Rife with Spiders","The spiders that roam the Dourstocks spill out from the Dreadweaver's Lair, making the forest all the more perilous for the Malledhrim.","Talk to Fernachar at the Haunted Inn","'Suillaid, mellon. You have our thanks for your efforts to pave the way for our offensive against Dol Guldur. This forest is still evil, but it is a little less so with every malicious spider that is brought to death.'","Defeated spiders in the Dourstocks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Spiders can be found throughout the Dourstocks.\
\
You should defeat many spiders to make the Dourstocks safer for the Malledhrim who wish to travel unhindered.","Derrota a las arañas en los Troncosombríos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Fernachar can be found in the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks.\
\
You should return to Fernachar with word of your success against the spiders."},
[978]={"Ardwyn is at Forthbrond, to the south and east of Cadthorn's position.\
\
You should return to Ardwyn with Cadthorn's message.","'The messages that Cadthorn bore were of import, but this edict from Edoras was the word that we sought. It shall be known among the captains.\
\
'Thank you for bringing us this news.'","A Rohirrim messenger disappeared when travelling to bring word to Forthbrond.","'I was unexpectedly attacked by Orcs and their ilk. They ambushed my party and stole a satchel that bore important messages for Forthbrond. Many of my companions fell, and I barely escaped with my life.\
\
'I was given word to bring to Grimbold and his captains: Théoden King has commanded that Isengard is to be called friend, and any reports to the contrary should come only from his son, Théodred.'","Find Cadthorn","'Look for Cadthorn, ${PLAYER}, north and west of Forthbrond.'","'Recently, Cadthorn, one of our messengers,  failed to report back. He is a capable courier that had gone to receive word from Edoras regarding our strategic goals for Forthbrond.  \
\
'Will you set forth and discover Cadthorn's location?\
\
'Begin your search to the north and slightly west from here along the cliff walls. Surely, he has set forth from Edoras already.'","A Word Deterred","Deliver Cadthorn's message to Ardwyn at Forthbrond","'You should return to Ardwyn, ${PLAYER}.'","The missing messenger might be found somewhere to the north and west of Forthbrond.\
\
Ardwyn has asked you to find Cadforn, a messenger who is late returning to Forthbrond."},
[979]={"Habla con Laenin, el Guardián del Claro, en Celondim","El descubrimiento de un collar de fabricación trasga en el cuello de los lobos del valle de Nen Hilith genera seria preocupación entre los Elfos. Será necesaria una acción rápida, y aquellos capaces de hacer algo respecto a esta amenaza deben ser informados.","Regresa rápidamente a Celondim y habla con Laenin, el Guardián del Claro.\
\
Tu descubrimiento de un collar para lobos elaborado por artesanos trasgos ha resultado un hecho alarmante para los guardianes del claro. Se te ha encargado llevar esta noticia a su líder en el puerto élfico de Celondim.","'No podemos dejar pasar otro momento sin informar a otros sobre la llegada de los trasgos. Quizás la protección del Señor Dorongúr se esté debilitando mientras avanzamos hacia las costas para partir, o quizás el Enemigo esté creciendo en fuerza mas rápido de lo que esperamos.\
\
'Sea como sea, ${PLAYER}, debemos enviar un mensaje de vuelta a Celondim y a mi superior allí. ¡Rápido, regresa con Laenin, el Guardián del Claro en Celondim, y cuéntale lo que has descubierto!\
\
'Encontrarás a Laenin en los muelles de Celondim al noreste de este valle.'","Una Palabra de Advertencia","'Regresa rápido con Laenin e infórmale lo que hemos encontrado aquí. Está en Celondim hacia el sureste.'","'Este descubrimiento es preocupante. Me aseguraré de que esta información sea transmitida al Señor Dorongúr en Duillond.\
\
'Nunca habríamos sabido de esto si no fuera por ti, ${PLAYER}. Estamos en deuda contigo.'"},
[980]={"Radwig has relented to his mother Etta's desire to defend Floodwend, but you are not bound to remain in the city.","Radwig can be found in the Mead Hall of Floodwend.\
\
You should return to Radwig with the wood you gathered from the Worksite.","A Worksite Overrun","'While I abide my mother's wishes, you at least are free to march into battle. Are you the sort of warrior that would wish to ride out and defeat foes on their own turf?'\
\
You tell the Thane that you have done such feats countless times, and would welcome the opportunity to rid his lands of the evil that lurks there.\
\
'You will go, then? I admire your boldness, ${PLAYER}! I hope to hear many stories of your might upon your return. The Wargs are our biggest concern right now, for they hold our wood-stores hostage.'","Gathered wood (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Wood can be found in the Warg-infested worksite east of Floodwend.\
\
You should collect wood from the abandoned worksite.","Bring the wood to Radwig in Floodwend","'You succeeded! I am so impressed, ${PLAYER}! Your deeds inspire me; while we have sat here pounding nails and sharpening swords, you actually cleared the wood of that howling menace, and took back our supplies.\
\
'It is amazing, what one ${CLASS} can do....'","Gather wood from the abandoned worksite (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[981]={"Search the fourth patrol point","Talk to Gwilum at Barnavon","After escaping the perils of Wulf's Cleft, you have arrived at the village of Barnavon in Carreglyn. There is little sense of safety in this place, though no one has yet made an overt gesture of hostility.","'The final place to look is at the shrine of the Uch-gwirod. Long ago, the Ox-spirit dwelt there and spoke oft with my forefathers. Perhaps she may be persuaded to intercede on our behalf once more.'","Search the first patrol point","'The first place to look lies at Lhun Avanc. Be wary, for legend tells that the Great Avanc lairs there, waiting for the foolish to fall into its trap!'","There are no signs of Warg-riders here, but something has terrified the miners","'The second place to look will bring you near to the Barnavon Mine. The workers there may need your assistance.'","The fourth patrol point is at Munfaeril's Shrine, upon the lake far to the north-west of Hen Turrau.\
\
Gwilum has asked you to patrol Carreglyn and discover whence came the Warg-riders plaguing his clan's land.","'The third place to look is found at Hen Turrau on the hill above the Barnavon Mine. It has long been a watch-tower of my people, but I fear it is now being used for evil purposes.'","A World of Trouble","Gwilum is at the gate of Barnavon.\
\
You should return to Gwilum with news of your discoveries.","Warg-riders dare not come to this place","You find no evidence regarding the Warg-riders here, but there is a strange chain trailing into the water near the edge of the pond","The first patrol point lies to the south of Barnavon at Lhun Avanc.\
\
Gwilum has asked you to patrol Carreglyn and discover whence came the Warg-riders plaguing his clan's land.","'So, Duvodiad, you have passed through many dangers to come here. I do not believe in chance, so it must be by someone's -- or something's -- design that you are here.\
\
'Believe it or not, word came hither of your journey -- nay, fear not... your secret remains secret. You have assuredly met some of my brethren in arms in the Dunbog... I have learned of your coming through them, and through northern duvodiad who passed through Carreglyn not long ago.\
\
'If you will aid me with a few tasks, I may be able to lend assistance to your cause, as well. First, I would like you to patrol our territory... Warg-riding goblins plague our lands, and I wish to learn whence they came, so that we may drive them back. Seek for signs of the Warg-riders on the banks of Lhun Avanc, at the Barnavon Mine, upon Hen Turrau, and at the shrine of the Uch-gwirod, whom you might call Munfaeril. What say you?'","'Your patrol was not fruitless, though the discoveries are not what I had expected. I am grateful for your efforts. I will review the evidence you have brought to me, and perhaps we will still learn where these Warg-riders come from and what their purpose here is.\
\
'In the meantime -- and if you are willing -- I have more yet for you to do.'","There are signs of Dunlending activity at this tower, but no evidence pointing to the origins of the Warg-riders","Search the second patrol point","The third patrol point is at Hen Turrau, an old watchtower upon the hill west of the Barnavon Mine.\
\
Gwilum has asked you to patrol Carreglyn and discover whence came the Warg-riders plaguing his clan's land.","Search the third patrol point","The second patrol point is at the Barnavon mine, far to the east of Barnavon-town.\
\
Gwilum has asked you to patrol Carreglyn and discover whence came the Warg-riders plaguing his clan's land."},
[982]={"Una sierpe temible se oculta en lo más profundo de las cavernas.","Una sierpe por los cuernos","La morada de Thorgest está al noroeste de las cavernas de las sierpes.\
\
Debes regresar con Thorgest e informarle de que Ruinuan ha muerto a tus manos.","Habla con Thorgest","Un rugido resuena desde las cavernas más profundas. Una gran y temible sierpe debe habitar allí.\
\
Encuentra a la sierpe en lo profundo de las cuevas.","Ruinuan derrotado","Derrota a la temible sierpe en las cavernas","Un rugido resuena desde las cavernas más profundas. Una gran y temible sierpe debe habitar allí.","Entra en las cavernas","Una gran y temible sierpe debe morar en lo más profundo de estas cavernas.\
\
Encuentra a la sierpe adentrándote en las cuevas.","'Entonces... por fin está hecho, y la memoria de mi hermano ha sido vengada. Gracias, ${PLAYER}. Me será mucho más fácil seguir adelante sabiendo que la deuda que tenía con Thorkell ya no pesa sobre mi pecho.\
\
'¿Y ahora qué? Estas montañas se han vuelto aún más peligrosas estos últimos años, y Afwald no es precisamente alguien que me acompañaría en la caza. Quizá deba encontrar un nuevo compañero, o abandonar la caza de una vez.\
\
'Ya no tengo paciencia para las comodidades de la civilización... creo que me quedaré aquí y me las arreglaré con sierpes y hombres-lobo.'"},
[983]={"You should return to Torchún outside of the Houses of Healing and let him know you have dispersed a number of visiting well-wishers.","'A great flood of well well-wishers has been flooding the Houses of Healing, ${PLAYER}. I would swear there are three of them to every wounded soldier! They must be turned away - the healers and herbalists are tripping over them to tend the patients!\
\
'Would you go inside and outside the Houses of Healing and shoo away as many as you can?'","Too many visiting well-wishers around the Houses of Healing are getting in the way of the healers' work and need to be shooed away.","Return to Torchún","Torchún has asked you to disperse visiting well-wishers inside and outside the Houses of Healing, on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.","A Worrisome Crowd","Disperse well-wishers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Dispersed well-wishers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You have sent a good number of them away? You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}.'"},
[985]={"Recolecta gotas corrosivas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Zarpas de barghest podridas recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los barghests se encuentran en Angmar. Las sanguijuelas de azufre también se encuentran en Angmar.\
\
Dardúr necesita ahora zarpas de barghest y gotas del icor de las sanguijuelas de azufre.","'Entonces, ${PLAYER}, ya tenemos dos conjuntos de los objetos necesarios. Solo queda el tercero, y tu prenda estará completa. Ve ahora y termina tu labor.\
\
'Necesito ahora una Insignia de Mando del uruk Lagmâs en Urugarth y un cuerno del Gorthorog Târlug en Carn Dûm.'","Recolecta la piel de Helchuan","Lleva los objetos recolectados a Dardúr en Gondamon","Recolecta una Insignia de Mando","Cuerno grisáceo de Gorthorog recogido","Dardúr ha aceptado ayudarte a crear una prenda digna de un Maestro Rúnico de categoría.","'Aún estoy esperando el primer conjunto de objetos, ${PLAYER}.'","Insignia de Mando recogida","Recolecta zarpas de barghest podridas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gotas corrosivas recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recolecta vides de Glâd Ereg (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Vides de Glâd Ereg recolectadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Muy bien, ${PLAYER}. Esto es un buen comienzo. Ahora debes traerme el segundo conjunto de objetos, tan pronto como puedas.\
\
'Estos incluyen las zarpas de los barghests que merodean Fornost en las Quebradas del Norte y Haudh Iarchith en las Tierras de Bree, y las gotas corrosivas de las sanguijuelas de azufre de Angmar.'","Los ucornos y merodeadores habitan en Glâd Ereg en Eregion. Helchuan merodea cerca de los manantiales al norte de Zigilgund en Forochel.\
\
Dardúr desea que le traigas vides recogidas de las criaturas naturales en Eregion y la piel de la sierpe gélida Helchuan.","Una Prenda Digna","'Esto es lo último, ${PLAYER}. Tu tarea ha sido larga, pero ahora tu prenda está completa. Lúcela con orgullo, y todos sabrán que eres ${PLAYER:un Maestro Rúnico[m]|una Maestra Rúnica[f]}.'","Recolecta un cuerno grisáceo de Gorthorog","Piel de Helchuan recogida","'Sin los materiales adecuados, no puedo completar tu prenda, ${PLAYER}.'","'Los Maestros Rúnicos no somos vanidosos, ${PLAYER}. Tú y yo sabemos que el conocimiento es un tesoro de la mente, no de nuestras vestiduras. Aun así, también es cierto que otros no nos dan el respeto debido si no nos vestimos como desean vernos. Así es el modo de los no iluminados.\
\
'Ahora es el momento de obtener la indumentaria que te dará ese respeto. Busca los materiales que necesito, y haré para ti un equipo digno de un Maestro Rúnico.\
\
'Primero, necesitaré las vides que crecen sobre las pieles de las criaturas que acechan en Glâd Ereg en Eregion y la piel de la sierpe gélida Helchuan, que habita en Forochel. Que tu camino sea seguro, ${PLAYER}.","Lagmâs habita Urugarth y Târlug se encuentra en Carn Dûm, en Angmar.\
\
Dardúr necesita ahora una Insignia de Mando y un cuerno grisáceo de Gorthorog para completar tu recompensa.","'Sin el último conjunto de objetos, no puedo completar la prenda, ${PLAYER}.'"},
[987]={"Orcs can be found throughout the Norcrofts.\
\
Ides has tasked you with dispatching Orcs in a timely fashion, in order to prove yourself to her.","Return to Ides at the training ground","A Worthy Trainer","'Ides is quick to learn fighting techniques, but she lacks size and strength. Training is one matter, but she has absurd ideas of charging alongside the men onto a real battlefield.\
\
'Since you seem to be quite eager to help her, I am going to relinquish her training duties to you. Athelward can speak to you when she gets herself killed... it will be none of my concern. Go speak with her at the mill to the north, above the ridge.'","Do not allow the timer to expire","Talk to Ides","Ides can be found training at the mill, north of the Rohirrim training grounds, at the northern edge of the Norcrofts.\
\
You have surpassed the challenge set forth by Ides, and she awaits your return.","Ides can be found training at the mill, north of the Rohirrim training grounds, at the northern edge of the Norcrofts.\
\
Edwulf has given you control of training Ides, but has counselled you about her headstrong nature.","'I have great respect for Edwulf's prowess in combat, but as a mentor, he leaves much to be desired.\
\
'You have been sent to take his place? You would not have been chosen were you without skill, but you have yet to prove yourself worthy of my favour. I shall have you know that I intend to become a shield-maiden of great renown, and that I take my training quite seriously.\
\
'Allow me to see how quickly you can dispatch of Orcs. Impress me, and I will eagerly follow your guidance.'","Derrota orcos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'That was rather impressive. Even that braggart Edwulf would be pressed to achieve such a hasty feat!\
\
'Very well, I shall heed your counsel. Having skill and strength will not be enough. I must learn to fight with courage and honour if I am to live up to my father's reputation.'","Has derrotado orcos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Edwulf has abandoned the idea of helping Ides train. You have the opportunity to take his place as Ides's mentor, but not until your talents have earned her respect.","You have failed to impress Ides"},
[988]={"'There is a great wounded salamander to the north of here that has been stricken with this dangerous affliction. Healing it will help not only the beast itself, but also ensure its many young are protected from this scourge.\
\
'Will you go and heal this beast?'","Return to Elder Ilaya in Khûtra.","A Wounded Beast","Return to Elder Ilaya in Khûtra","There is a large wounded salamander that needs to be healed with the salve given to you by Heshra, the herbalist. The salamander can be found west of Khûtra.","Administer the salve to Nekarkul on the shore to the west","'Let that be a lesson to you. Nature gives no quarter, and expects none in return. A wounded beast is still savage, and nature only recognizes strength and ferocity. Fortunate, then, that its ferocity was more than matched by yours.'","Elder Ilaya has asked you to heal a large wounded salamander with the salve given to you by Heshra. The beast can be found west of Khûtra."},
[989]={"'I know Tharashil has no time for me or Aítarshun. I am touched she sent you to aid me and him.\
\
'She does not know the weight I carried out of the old oasis to the west. My mother is there, still. She will dwell there forever, as I will in this oasis.\
\
'I left her to fate, rooted, as I am now, to a spot she could not depart. The wrathful spirits swarmed her as she fell to final slumber, and I left.\
\
'I did not look back. Now, friend, I want to claim something of hers. Her tomb's location will be obvious. Her necklace is there.\
\
'I should like to know that some of the wrathful spirits there met a final fate.'","A Wounded Heart","A tear falls from her eye.\
\
'This means the world to me, friend. You are selfless. I have no words but ones of thanks for what you did for me.'","Avenge Filadal's mother by defeating wrathful spirits (${NUMBER}/8)","Recovered Filadal's Mother's necklace","Wrahtful spirits slain (${NUMBER}/8)","Filadal told you of being forced to leave the oasis north-west of Shonith as her mother was set to fade. She fled, and only saw her mother surrounded by wrathful spirits before reaching her final rest. She wants a keepsake and vengeance before she fades.","You recovered the necklace from near one of the trees in the old oasis and defeated a good number of the wrathful spirits there. Return the necklace to Filadal.","Collect Filadal's Mother's necklace","Return Filadal's mother's necklace to her at Shonith","Filadal wants to recover her mother's necklace from the oasis north-west of Shonith and to bring vengeance on the wrathful spirits that drove her from the oasis before she could say good-bye."},
[990]={"While scouring the ruins of Thornhope for survivors, you discovered a wounded soldier.\
\
You should help the soldier to safety.","'I... I will heal. Thank you, stranger... without you... I would have perished.'","Éorpwald is at Béortnoth's camp, outside of Thornhope.\
\
You should speak with Éorpwald when you return to Béortnoth's camp.","Talk to Éorpwald at Béortnoth's camp","You have found a wounded soldier from the household of Thornhope hiding in the ruins","Éorpwald is hiding behind a wall in Thornhope.\
\
You should escort Éorpwald to safety.","'Ah... at last... aid has come! I see you have cleared a way from the gate... I... believe I can make it out... from here.\
\
'Thank you!'","Talk to Éorpwald","A Wounded Soldier","While scouring the ruins of Thornhope for survivors, you discovered a wounded soldier."},
[991]={"¡Cada año en primavera, el Festival de Aniversario se lleva a cabo para celebrar una ocasión muy especial! ¡Participa en las festividades para ayudar a marcar este hito con fuegos artificiales y buen ánimo!'","'¡Nueve días celebrando otro año maravilloso, por Dios!\
\
Waldo Retumbo te entrega una gran recompensa.\
\
'¡Nos has dado tanto, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}!'","¡Has completado 'Otro año maravilloso' (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})!","¡Hay algo que hacer cada día durante el Festival de Aniversario! ¡Ven y únete a todos para participar en muchas actividades del Festival de Aniversario durante tres días más!'","Habla con Waldo Retumbo","'¡Has demostrado que no viniste por nada, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}! Pero, ¿podrás mantener ese espíritu festivo? ¡Tres días más para seguir!'","Waldo Retumbo desea agradecerte por tu continua participación en el Festival de Aniversario.'","El producto de un año (Final)","¡Completa 'Otro año maravilloso' (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})!"},
[992]={"Completa 'Otro hermoso año' (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Todos los años en primavera, el Festival de Aniversario tiene lugar para celebrar una ocasión muy especial. ¡Participa en las festividades para ayudar a marcar este hito con fuegos artificiales y buen humor!","Has completado 'Otro hermoso año' (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Todos los días hay algo que hacer durante el Festival de Aniversario. ¡Ven y únete a todos y participa en muchas actividades del Festival de Aniversario durante tres días más!","'¿Ya seis días?!'\
\
Waldo Retumbo rebusca debajo de su mesa antes de volver con algo que te entrega.\
\
'¡Toma esto, es para tí!'","'¿Veamos si puedes mantener ese entusiasmo, verdad? ¡Participa durante tres días más, y te daré otra recompensa!'","Habla con Waldo Retumbo","El producto de un año (Intermedio)","Waldo Retumbo querría agradecerte por tu continua participación en el Festival de Aniversario."},
[993]={"Todos los años en primavera, el Festival de Aniversario tiene lugar para celebrar una ocasión muy especial. ¡Participa en las festividades para ayudar a marcar este hito con fuegos artificiales y buen humor!","Todos los días hay algo que hacer durante el Festival de Aniversario. ¡Ven y únete a todos y participa en muchas actividades del Festival de Aniversario durante tres días más!","El producto de un año (Intro)","Habla con Waldo Retumbo","'¿Has celebrado durante tres días enteros?! ¡Podrías estar incluso más emocionado por este año que yo!\
\
'Aquí, ten una pequeña recompensa que guardé solo para ti!'","'Otro año encantador' completado (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Hay muchas recompensas que esperan a los participantes del Festival de Aniversario, y para aquellos que celebran durante muchos días, las recompensas son aún mayores!'","Waldo Retumbo quiere agradecerte por tu continua participación en el Festival de Aniversario."},
[994]={"Un Pretendiente en Bree","La casa de la dama es la primera o segunda puerta tras subir la Escalera de los Eruditos y cruzar el primer puente.\
\
Cebadilla Mantecona te indicó que coloques el ramo en el jarrón junto a la puerta de la casa.","'¡Perfecto! Sabía que Mantecona sabría indicarte la dirección correcta. ¡Adelante, entrega ese ramo!'","'Gracias nuevamente, mi ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}, por tu ayuda. Ahora tengo el ramo perfecto, digno de la deslumbrante belleza de la dama a la que deseo impresionar. Si no es mucha molestia, quisiera pedirte un último favor. ¿Podrías entregar mi obsequio? No puedo arriesgarme a encontrarla por accidente.\
\
'Estoy seguro de la dirección en la Escalera de los Eruditos, pero necesito que averigües cuál de las casas del camino pertenece a mi dulce dama. Pregunta a Cebadilla Mantecona, el dueño del Poney Pisador. Él conoce todos los chismes de Bree y seguramente sabrá dónde vive. Por favor, consúltalo antes de entregar el ramo.'","Entregaste el ramo","'¡Maravilloso! ¡Has vuelto! Confío en que entregaste las flores a mi dulce dama.\
\
'¡Mi corazón late con emoción al pensar en el momento en que encuentre mi obsequio!'","Cebadilla Mantecona está en el Poney Pisador, en Bree.\
\
Aún preocupado por causar una buena impresión, Avery Manzanagria te ha pedido que entregues el ramo en la puerta de la dama. Había preguntado discretamente por su dirección sin éxito, pero prefiere que consultes a Cebadilla Mantecona, el posadero del Poney Pisador en Bree, para que te indique la casa correcta.","'¿Qué haces de vuelta aquí? ¡Se supone que estás entregando las flores! Ve a hablar con Cebadilla Mantecona en el Poney Pisador. Ay, no puedo esperar a que ella reciba mi regalo.'","Avery Manzanagria está en la Plaza del Mercado de Bree.\
\
Debes regresar con Avery Manzanagria de inmediato.","'¿Qué decías? ¿La casa de quién? Ay, los días están muy ajetreados...\
\
'Sigue el camino frente al Poney Pisador hacia la Puerta Oeste y gira a la izquierda para subir la Escalera de los Eruditos. Su casa es una de las dos primeras después del primer puente. Debería haber un jarrón cerca.'","Así que, mi ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}, me dicen que estás ayudando al joven Manzanagria. Me ha enviado una descripción de la encantadora dama, y debo decir que la apruebo. Sé de quién se trata. ¡Pobre muchacho, es terriblemente tímido!\
\
'¡Ah, por todos los toneles! Con tantos clientes y trabajo, he olvidado por completo dónde vivía. ¡Oh, espera! Ya lo recuerdo...\
\
'Sigue el camino frente al Poney hacia la Puerta Oeste y gira a la izquierda para subir la Escalera de los Eruditos. Su casa es la primera o la segunda puerta después del primer puente. Debería haber un jarrón cerca... será el lugar perfecto para dejar el obsequio.'","Coloca el ramo en el jarrón","Has ayudado a Avery Manzanagria en su intento por cortejar a la mujer que desea, reuniendo flores raras para crear un hermoso ramo.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000> NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro cuando finalice el festival actual. </rgb>"},
[995]={"Incendio en Târ Stazg","Las tiendas de los semiorcos están en Târ Stazg, al noreste de Echad Dúnann, a lo largo de las montañas frente a la Puerta del Cuerno Rojo.\
\
Para expulsar a los desorganizados semiorcos de Eregion, Palanaer te ha encomendado la tarea de destruir sus tiendas.","'Las tiendas de los semiorcos están repartidas por todo Târ Stazg, al noreste.'","'Aunque no sean muchos, los semiorcos de Târ Stazg siguen representando una amenaza para Eregion. Si no actuamos con rapidez, reconstruirán sus fuerzas y las desplegarán en Barad Morlas.\
\
'Debemos expulsar a los semiorcos de Eregion... con fuego si es necesario. Regresa a Târ Stazg y prende fuego a las tiendas de los semiorcos. Sin refugio ni provisiones, serán presa fácil para nuestros exploradores.\
\
'Las tiendas están dispersas por todo Târ Stazg, al noreste de Echad Dúnann, a lo largo de las montañas frente a la Puerta del Cuerno Rojo.'","'¡Salve, ${PLAYER}, Azote de los semiorcos!'","Habla con Palanaer","Palanaer se encuentra en Echad Dúnann, al suroeste de Târ Stazg.\
\
Debes volver a Palanaer e informar de tu éxito.","Tiendas de campaña quemadas en Târ Stazg (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Quema tiendas de campaña en Târ Stazg (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Los semiorcos de Târ Stazg quedaron abatidos por la derrota de Akashpug, pero no fueron expulsados.","'Sin líder, a los semiorcos les resultará mucho más difícil mantener su presencia sin refugio ni provisiones. Lo has hecho bien, ${PLAYER}.'"},
[996]={"Blaire is at the Boar-clan encampment, south of Lhan Colvarn.\
\
You should return to Blaire with news of your success.","Abolish the Abominations","The Abomination trolls can be found at Lhan Colvarn, north of the Boar-clan encampment.\
\
Blaire has asked you to thin the ranks of the Abominations by defeating some of the trolls.","'Hurry to Lhan Colvarn and defeat the Abominations. We have no time to lose.'","'Impressive. The Elders were right to send you to me. I have spent a long time trying to convince them that we need to take action now, but they are stuck in their ways. They love this pile of mud too much for their own good.\
\
'Perhaps we can convince them that change has to happen now if they are to survive this war.'","Defeated Abomination trolls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Duvodiad, we need to strike at Lhan Colvarn and defeat as many of the Abominations as possible...can you do this? The time for war is on the horizon.\
\
'If you are willing, go north into Lhan Colvarn and defeat as many of the trolls as you can, then return to me when you are done.'","Talk to Blaire at the Boar-clan encampment","Defeat Abomination trolls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Abominations have become a problem for the inhabitants of the Dunbog, and Blaire is concerned that Saruman will use them against the forces of good."},
[997]={"Collected the stolen sword","Bring the stolen sword to Wilferth","'¿No tienes nada para mí?'","Above His Station","Wilferth is at the Rohirrim-camp in the East Wall.\
\
You have recovered the stolen sword and should return with it to Wilferth so he can see it.","'Ah, you did it! Very good, ${PLAYER}. It brings joy to my heart to know that Orc will no longer wield this stolen sword. Now, who did he steal it from, I wonder?'\
\
Wilferth takes the blade and examines it carefully.\
\
'I would say it is from Gondor, though it does not have much in the way of ornamentation. I will hold onto it for now. It could use a good cleaning. Perhaps it will drink Orc-blood again, as it was intended to do!\
\
'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. By wresting it from the clutches of that Orc, you have restored a measure of this blade's dignity.'","'I do not like the idea of an Orc holding such a high-quality sword in his filthy hands, ${PLAYER}. Track down the Orc I saw and take it from him! If he fled with the others, he will be somewhere to the north-east, probably to the camp the Mordor Orcs established between here and the Wold.'","The Orc with the unusually high-quality sword fled after the raid to the north-east and is probably within the camp the Mordor Orcs have established between Mansig's encampment and the Wold.\
\
Wilferth saw an Orc wielding a sword well above its station and wants you to reclaim it.","Wilferth thinks the Orcs and Uruks may have different reasons for being in the East Wall, but he knows that they are all your enemies, and an advantage to any one of them is a problem for your friends.","Find an Orc wielding a stolen sword and take it from him","'They may not be working together, ${PLAYER}, but the various tribes of Orcs and Uruks here in the East Wall are each our enemies. Is it possible for them to set aside their differences and work together, as Men do? I am afraid it is. We must oppose them all, wherever we can. \
\
'During the Orc-ambush that greeted us shortly after our arrival here, I saw an Orc from Mordor carrying a high-quality sword. It was not of Orc-make; their weapons are crude and ugly, but this blade caught the light and seemed to shine as the Orc swung it around him in deadly arcs.\
\
'It is not right for such a weapon to languish in the hands of an Orc. I did not see this Orc after the battle, so he must have escaped into the East Wall somewhere. Find him and take the sword from him, ${PLAYER}. Many of the retreating Orcs fled to the north-east. Begin your search there, at the camp the Mordor Orcs have established between here and the Wold.'"},
[998]={"Talk to Daelarth","'Since the sun was blotted out days ago, we have seen little without the use of torches, but what I saw I shall never forget.\
\
'A flying beast bore a rider in darkened robes and the blade he held reflected what little light passed through the murky sky. As I looked upon him, a great pain overtook me and I turned away.\
\
'When I turned to look again to the sky, he had gone.'","Above the Ashes","'Why do you ask me to recall such things?\
\
'Before terror pulled me to the ground, I saw the form of a great beast above the ashen clouds. It let out a shrill cry as it flew overhead and then it was gone. I swear to you, I speak true!'","Talk to Laerven","'As my men and I journeyed to Pelargir from Linhir, we felt a great weight upon us.\
\
'Days without rest and the fatigue of battle had worn on us all, but this filled me with dread in a way that I had never known. And just as it took hold, it faded away, and those of my men that had cowered found their way to their feet once more.\
\
'I have heard many rumours of what happened that day, but I do not know if there is any truth in them. I have not had much time to think on this matter until now, yet it still troubles me.\
\
'Speak to my men of this, and see if there is any truth to these tales.'","'As with Lord Angbor, I wish I knew what happened in that moment.\
\
'My armour grew heavy and I fell to the ground before I could realize what happened. I regret that I cannot be of more help to you, ${CLASS}.'","Angbor's men can be found in the eastern half of Pelargir.\
\
Angbor has asked you to question his men about strange things they claim to have seen in the hours preceding the battle in Pelargir.","Talk to Thamdir","Talk to Angbor in Pelargir","'I do not doubt their words, my friend. Could this be one of the nine wraiths of which Aragorn spoke?\
\
'Let us hope it has flown back to its master and shall not harry our journey to Minas Tirith. I will not allow its dread to burden my mind any longer.\
\
'My men and I must press on into Upper Lebennin!'","Lord Angbor has heard tales of a great beast flying in the darkened sky above Gondor and seeks to learn more of what his men have seen.","Angbor can be found inside the eastern gate in Pelargir.\
\
You have questioned his men and should now report what you have learned to Angbor."},
}
